{"jobs":[{"id":"452756bd-2f92-47aa-8459-cb8f29f02b08","title":"Senior Software Engineer 2","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-10-22T14:15:03.036+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/452756bd-2f92-47aa-8459-cb8f29f02b08","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/452756bd-2f92-47aa-8459-cb8f29f02b08/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Software Engineer II helps lead the platform development by making architecture decisions to ensure we're building clean, maintainable, and beautiful applications. This person is responsible for maintaining, expanding, and scaling our APIs that power our web applications. They develop specifications for moderately complex software programming applications and modify/maintain the existing software. This position participates in design and coding activities with other staff members. The Senior Software Engineer will work closely with management and other leads to design and implement new systems, maintain operations of the production systems and to coordinate work across all the initiatives of the Engineering team. They will operate in a distributed architecture, building the infrastructure to manage Big Data and solve complex algorithmic problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and develop highly scalable web applications, including AI-powered features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build RESTful APIs and integrate with LLM services and AI capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement streaming responses and real-time UI patterns for AI-driven experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build tools, services, and automation to extend platform capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run critical operational portions of our ingestion, analytics, and storage infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product managers and AI engineers to define strategic solutions and participate in the agile refinement process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with server-side code and database architecture on the back-end in NodeJS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clean UI/UX with the collaboration of our design teams, with attention to AI interaction patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with management and other architects to ensure quality in solutions and software design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in development lifecycle activities like design, coding, testing, and production release</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write reusable, testable, and efficient code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver code in an agile team environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and train on technologies you think may be appropriate for current or future projects, including emerging AI/LLM capabilities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience as a software engineer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience with NodeJS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years experience in NestJS preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience with React</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong skills needed in: Javascript, ES6, NodeJS, TypeORM, MySQL, Git, and REST principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge in Jest and Redis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in object-oriented programming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of algorithms, network protocols, and web services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with one of the major cloud hosting systems (AWS, GCP, Azure)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed, independent, and has experience owning complete features/products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing real-world web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding ability to negotiate difficult tradeoffs (e.g., quality vs. speed, collaboration vs. get-it-done)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agile development experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous startup or scaling experience is a plus</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and adaptable to changing technologies and requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication ability - we want to know your thoughts and input!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: Terraform, ElasticSearch, &amp; Snowflake</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: Experience with compliance frameworks like SOC2, ISO27017, NIST etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual in English &amp; Spanish is a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Experience (required - at least one of the following):</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building features that integrate with LLMs or AI services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated passion for AI through personal projects, contributions, or continuous learning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with prompt engineering and understanding of LLM capabilities and limitations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with streaming responses and real-time UI patterns for AI applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building conversational interfaces, chatbots, or chat-based user experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of conversation state management, context windows, and multi-turn dialogue patterns</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $157,500 - $262,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Senior Software Engineer II helps lead the platform development by making architecture decisions to ensure we're building clean, maintainable, and beautiful applications. This person is responsible for maintaining, expanding, and scaling our APIs that power our web applications. They develop specifications for moderately complex software programming applications and modify/maintain the existing software. This position participates in design and coding activities with other staff members. The Senior Software Engineer will work closely with management and other leads to design and implement new systems, maintain operations of the production systems and to coordinate work across all the initiatives of the Engineering team. They will operate in a distributed architecture, building the infrastructure to manage Big Data and solve complex algorithmic problems.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Architect and develop highly scalable web applications, including AI-powered features\n\n - Build RESTful APIs and integrate with LLM services and AI capabilities\n\n - Design and implement streaming responses and real-time UI patterns for AI-driven experiences\n\n - Build tools, services, and automation to extend platform capabilities\n\n - Run critical operational portions of our ingestion, analytics, and storage infrastructure\n\n - Collaborate with product managers and AI engineers to define strategic solutions and participate in the agile refinement process\n\n - Assist with server-side code and database architecture on the back-end in NodeJS\n\n - Develop clean UI/UX with the collaboration of our design teams, with attention to AI interaction patterns\n\n - Work with management and other architects to ensure quality in solutions and software design\n\n - Participate in development lifecycle activities like design, coding, testing, and production release\n\n - Write reusable, testable, and efficient code\n\n - Deliver code in an agile team environment\n\n - Research and train on technologies you think may be appropriate for current or future projects, including emerging AI/LLM capabilities\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 7+ years of experience as a software engineer\n\n - 3+ years of experience with NodeJS\n\n - 1+ years experience in NestJS preferred\n\n - 3+ years of experience with React\n\n - Strong skills needed in: Javascript, ES6, NodeJS, TypeORM, MySQL, Git, and REST principles\n\n - Knowledge in Jest and Redis\n\n - Proficiency in object-oriented programming\n\n - Good understanding of algorithms, network protocols, and web services\n\n - Experience with one of the major cloud hosting systems (AWS, GCP, Azure)\n\n - Self-directed, independent, and has experience owning complete features/products\n\n - Experience developing real-world web applications\n\n - Outstanding ability to negotiate difficult tradeoffs (e.g., quality vs. speed, collaboration vs. get-it-done)\n\n - Agile development experience\n\n - Previous startup or scaling experience is a plus\n\n - Self-motivated and adaptable to changing technologies and requirements\n\n - Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\n - Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or related field\n\n - Strong communication ability - we want to know your thoughts and input!\n\n - Nice to have: Terraform, ElasticSearch, & Snowflake\n\n - Nice to have: Experience with compliance frameworks like SOC2, ISO27017, NIST etc.\n\n - Bilingual in English & Spanish is a plus\n\nAI Experience (required - at least one of the following):\n\n - Hands-on experience building features that integrate with LLMs or AI services\n\n - Demonstrated passion for AI through personal projects, contributions, or continuous learning\n\n - Experience with prompt engineering and understanding of LLM capabilities and limitations\n\n - Familiarity with streaming responses and real-time UI patterns for AI applications\n\n - Experience building conversational interfaces, chatbots, or chat-based user experiences\n\n - Understanding of conversation state management, context windows, and multi-turn dialogue patterns\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $157,500 - $262,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"938b5802-714a-4843-bf43-4b03b3c0bf12","title":"Senior AI Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}},{"location":"Hybrid - New York","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}},{"location":"Hybrid - San Diego","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Diego"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-17T16:55:27.822+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/938b5802-714a-4843-bf43-4b03b3c0bf12","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/938b5802-714a-4843-bf43-4b03b3c0bf12/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is advancing the frontier of compliance automation by integrating intelligent AI capabilities into its platform. We are seeking a Senior AI Engineer to help design, build, and scale robust, high-impact AI systems that improve operational efficiency, enhance decision-making, and support trust-critical enterprise workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role focuses on solving complex, real-world problems with agentic AI, LLMs, and intelligent reasoning systems, including automating questionnaire answering and other compliance-related workflows. You will work on creating generalizable AI solutions that can be applied across multiple products and domains, collaborating with cross-functional teams to bring cutting-edge research into production-ready systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior AI Engineer, you will own the end-to-end design, implementation, and evolution of AI-driven systems embedded directly into Drata’s core platform. Your work will focus on building generalizable, reusable AI capabilities rather than one-off features, enabling multiple product surfaces and workflows across compliance and security.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Agentic &amp; Intelligent AI Systems</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement <strong>LLM-powered systems</strong> capable of multi-step reasoning, evidence grounding, and decision support in high-trust domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop <strong>agentic workflows</strong> that combine retrieval, tool use, structured reasoning, and human oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create interactive AI experiences that allow users to engage naturally with complex compliance and risk data.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Automated Reasoning Over Regulations &amp; Evidence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI systems that reason over structured and unstructured data to support regulatory interpretation, control alignment, and evidence validation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure AI outputs are traceable, explainable, and auditable, meeting the expectations of enterprise customers and auditors.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Production-Grade AI Architecture</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and deploy scalable <strong>LLM + retrieval + agent</strong> systems in production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize for latency, cost, reliability, and evaluation in real-world enterprise workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with platform, security, product teams, and other <strong>application development teams with diverse skill sets</strong> to operationalize AI safely and effectively.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsible &amp; Trustworthy AI</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embed <strong>human-in-the-loop workflows</strong>, confidence thresholds, and safety guardrails into AI systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure privacy-preserving data handling, robust failure modes, and transparent behavior aligned with Drata’s trust principles.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of hands-on software engineering experience; 2+ years specifically in ML/AI engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Programming Languages:</strong> Proficiency in Python; TypeScript experience is a plus, especially for production AI system integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Retrieval &amp; Vector Stores:</strong> Familiarity with vector databases (Pinecone, Chroma, FAISS, etc.) and RAG system design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>LLM &amp; AI Systems:</strong> Proven experience building and shipping <strong>LLM-based applications in production</strong>, including embeddings, RAG, agent frameworks, prompt engineering, and evaluation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Production Expertise:</strong> Track record of taking AI systems <strong>from concept to production</strong>, designing scalable, maintainable solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problem Solving:</strong> Ability to decompose complex tasks into agentic workflows and reason over high-stakes, structured, and unstructured data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Experience working cross-functionally with product, compliance, security, engineering teams, and partnering with other application development teams with diverse skill sets.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in compliance, security, risk, or audit domains.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Snowflake-based analytics, knowledge graphs, or enterprise data platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with non-technical stakeholders such as compliance or GRC teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This role defines how AI is responsibly embedded into a trust-critical enterprise platform. Your work will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish foundational <strong>agentic AI capabilities</strong> that power multiple present and future product experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enable customers to derive accurate, explainable insights from complex compliance and security data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the technical and ethical standard for applying modern AI in regulated, high-stakes environments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $153,600 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is advancing the frontier of compliance automation by integrating intelligent AI capabilities into its platform. We are seeking a Senior AI Engineer to help design, build, and scale robust, high-impact AI systems that improve operational efficiency, enhance decision-making, and support trust-critical enterprise workflows.\n\nThis role focuses on solving complex, real-world problems with agentic AI, LLMs, and intelligent reasoning systems, including automating questionnaire answering and other compliance-related workflows. You will work on creating generalizable AI solutions that can be applied across multiple products and domains, collaborating with cross-functional teams to bring cutting-edge research into production-ready systems.\n\nAs a Senior AI Engineer, you will own the end-to-end design, implementation, and evolution of AI-driven systems embedded directly into Drata’s core platform. Your work will focus on building generalizable, reusable AI capabilities rather than one-off features, enabling multiple product surfaces and workflows across compliance and security.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\nBuild Agentic & Intelligent AI Systems\n\n - Design and implement LLM-powered systems capable of multi-step reasoning, evidence grounding, and decision support in high-trust domains.\n\n - Develop agentic workflows that combine retrieval, tool use, structured reasoning, and human oversight.\n\n - Create interactive AI experiences that allow users to engage naturally with complex compliance and risk data.\n\nAutomated Reasoning Over Regulations & Evidence\n\n - Build AI systems that reason over structured and unstructured data to support regulatory interpretation, control alignment, and evidence validation.\n\n - Ensure AI outputs are traceable, explainable, and auditable, meeting the expectations of enterprise customers and auditors.\n\nProduction-Grade AI Architecture\n\n - Architect and deploy scalable LLM + retrieval + agent systems in production environments.\n\n - Optimize for latency, cost, reliability, and evaluation in real-world enterprise workloads.\n\n - Partner with platform, security, product teams, and other application development teams with diverse skill sets to operationalize AI safely and effectively.\n\nResponsible & Trustworthy AI\n\n - Embed human-in-the-loop workflows, confidence thresholds, and safety guardrails into AI systems.\n\n - Ensure privacy-preserving data handling, robust failure modes, and transparent behavior aligned with Drata’s trust principles.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - Experience: 7+ years of hands-on software engineering experience; 2+ years specifically in ML/AI engineering.\n\n - Programming Languages: Proficiency in Python; TypeScript experience is a plus, especially for production AI system integrations.\n\n - Retrieval & Vector Stores: Familiarity with vector databases (Pinecone, Chroma, FAISS, etc.) and RAG system design.\n\n - LLM & AI Systems: Proven experience building and shipping LLM-based applications in production, including embeddings, RAG, agent frameworks, prompt engineering, and evaluation.\n\n - Production Expertise: Track record of taking AI systems from concept to production, designing scalable, maintainable solutions.\n\n - Problem Solving: Ability to decompose complex tasks into agentic workflows and reason over high-stakes, structured, and unstructured data.\n\n - Collaboration: Experience working cross-functionally with product, compliance, security, engineering teams, and partnering with other application development teams with diverse skill sets.\n\nBonus Qualifications:\n\n - Experience in compliance, security, risk, or audit domains.\n\n - Familiarity with Snowflake-based analytics, knowledge graphs, or enterprise data platforms.\n\n - Experience partnering with non-technical stakeholders such as compliance or GRC teams.\n\nThis role defines how AI is responsibly embedded into a trust-critical enterprise platform. Your work will:\n\n - Establish foundational agentic AI capabilities that power multiple present and future product experiences.\n\n - Enable customers to derive accurate, explainable insights from complex compliance and security data.\n\n - Set the technical and ethical standard for applying modern AI in regulated, high-stakes environments.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $153,600 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4c85d329-b4b3-4b9d-a5d8-a7ad20a6e8f9","title":"Senior Solutions Engineer, Enterprise - West","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-27T22:20:38.558+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/4c85d329-b4b3-4b9d-a5d8-a7ad20a6e8f9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/4c85d329-b4b3-4b9d-a5d8-a7ad20a6e8f9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a seasoned, hardworking, smart and over achieving Senior Solutions Engineer with proven experience and a passion for selling technology solutions to senior executives. You will be responsible for selling into new prospects as well as farming back into existing customers to ensure high renewal and customer satisfaction levels. Measures of success include new customer acquisition rates, renewal rates, up-selling, cross-selling, customer satisfaction and contribution to overall sales team and business success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with sales executives to plan, prepare and execute on strategic deals in sales cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a process from the ground-up to streamline the communication and increase efficiencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage all technical aspects of RFP / RFI responses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively communicate client needs to the R&amp;D teams for future product enhancements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Focus on shortening the sales cycles while providing technical support on proof of concepts without overcomplicating the buyer’s journey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support sales executives with solution selling into prospect account base</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successfully match customer pain/requirements to proposed solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and deliver powerful presentations and demos that clearly communicate the uniqueness of the value proposition</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect and document competitive intelligence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model the financial business case associated with each sales opportunity</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience as a Sales/Solutions Engineer preferably in the SaaS space.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred knowledge of cloud providers, such as AWS, GCP, etc</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building out proof of concepts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record selling/supporting complex enterprise solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to forge strong, long-lasting relationships with senior executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy to understand manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in software development and web technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent presentation and creativity skills</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This role will receive a competitive base salary, variable compensation, benefits, and/or stock, typically in the form of Restricted Stock Units (RSUs). The applicable range of On-Target Earnings (OTE) for each US-based role is based on where the employee works and is aligned to one of 3 tiers based on the cost of labor for that geographic area. The expected OTE ranges for this role are set forth below, subject to change.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Tier 1: $223,900 - $276,600</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Tier 2: $201,500 - $249,000</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Tier 3: $179,100 - $221,200</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>You can view which tier applies to where you plan to work </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/career-tiers\"><em><u>here</u></em></a><em>. A variety of factors are considered when determining someone’s leveling and compensation–including a candidate’s professional background and experience. These ranges may be modified in the future and final offer amounts may vary from the amounts listed above.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for a seasoned, hardworking, smart and over achieving Senior Solutions Engineer with proven experience and a passion for selling technology solutions to senior executives. You will be responsible for selling into new prospects as well as farming back into existing customers to ensure high renewal and customer satisfaction levels. Measures of success include new customer acquisition rates, renewal rates, up-selling, cross-selling, customer satisfaction and contribution to overall sales team and business success.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Partner with sales executives to plan, prepare and execute on strategic deals in sales cycles\n\n - Create a process from the ground-up to streamline the communication and increase efficiencies\n\n - Manage all technical aspects of RFP / RFI responses\n\n - Effectively communicate client needs to the R&D teams for future product enhancements\n\n - Focus on shortening the sales cycles while providing technical support on proof of concepts without overcomplicating the buyer’s journey.\n\n - Support sales executives with solution selling into prospect account base\n\n - Successfully match customer pain/requirements to proposed solutions\n\n - Create and deliver powerful presentations and demos that clearly communicate the uniqueness of the value proposition\n\n - Collect and document competitive intelligence\n\n - Model the financial business case associated with each sales opportunity\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 5+ years of experience as a Sales/Solutions Engineer preferably in the SaaS space.\n\n - Preferred knowledge of cloud providers, such as AWS, GCP, etc\n\n - Experience building out proof of concepts\n\n - Proven track record selling/supporting complex enterprise solutions\n\n - Ability to forge strong, long-lasting relationships with senior executives\n\n - Ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy to understand manner\n\n - Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in software development and web technologies\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Excellent presentation and creativity skills\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThis role will receive a competitive base salary, variable compensation, benefits, and/or stock, typically in the form of Restricted Stock Units (RSUs). The applicable range of On-Target Earnings (OTE) for each US-based role is based on where the employee works and is aligned to one of 3 tiers based on the cost of labor for that geographic area. The expected OTE ranges for this role are set forth below, subject to change.\n\nTier 1: $223,900 - $276,600\n\nTier 2: $201,500 - $249,000\n\nTier 3: $179,100 - $221,200\n\nYou can view which tier applies to where you plan to work here https://drata.com/career-tiers. A variety of factors are considered when determining someone’s leveling and compensation–including a candidate’s professional background and experience. These ranges may be modified in the future and final offer amounts may vary from the amounts listed above.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cf5e1a06-8720-4e5c-93c6-5494c39c862c","title":"Senior Product Manager 2, Assurance","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-06T18:50:56.128+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/cf5e1a06-8720-4e5c-93c6-5494c39c862c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/cf5e1a06-8720-4e5c-93c6-5494c39c862c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Product Manager is a key position to support our growth, and we are looking for an experienced product manager to join us! As the Senior Product Manager on our growing team, you will be working cross functionally to design, build, and roll-out products and features that align with Drata’s strategy and vision. A top-notch senior product manager will have worked on numerous projects and have a firm grasp of how to satisfy consumers’ needs. Ideal candidates will be equally analytical and creative, and able to justify decisions to a range of stakeholders. This is an ideal position for someone who thrives in changing environments and can build the roadmap to create innovative product offerings.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage a portfolio of products and/or capabilities and build resource investment allocation plans grounded in data and research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define roadmap and requirements to solve the biggest customer problems across one or multiple product lines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define  MVP experiences and quickly learn and iterate based on feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Form hypothesis and run experiments using lean methodologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with engineering and design teams to define, build, and maintain products/features which are critical to growth and retention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with cross-functional teams on release plans and documentation to deliver value to our customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate effectively with GTM partners to plan and launch products and capabilities, including alpha, beta and GA phasis with process success criteria for each phase</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define success criteria and measure the success and effectiveness of features and capabilities from entitlement, to activation, adoption and retention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build business cases justifying investment in feature and capabilities and present to stakeholder across the org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively partner across teams to anticipate and address risk &amp; dependencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate progress and plan to leadership, peers, etc</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the business outcomes including revenue of your product</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years designing and delivering world-class software products in a Product Management role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep customer empathy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for identifying and solving problems with the ability to conduct effective customer interviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capable of breaking down a big vision into small deliverables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ruthless prioritization of the backlog</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-starter with an entrepreneurial mindset and the drive to pursue opportunities beyond current constraints</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional collaboration skills working with PMs, engineers, designers, marketers, and customer success teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth mindset with a desire for continuous improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills paired with a data-informed mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with 2-sided markets is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A GM-mindset and ability to ruthlessly prioritize against market opportunity and revenue implications and customer satisfaction</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $165,000 - $270,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Senior Product Manager is a key position to support our growth, and we are looking for an experienced product manager to join us! As the Senior Product Manager on our growing team, you will be working cross functionally to design, build, and roll-out products and features that align with Drata’s strategy and vision. A top-notch senior product manager will have worked on numerous projects and have a firm grasp of how to satisfy consumers’ needs. Ideal candidates will be equally analytical and creative, and able to justify decisions to a range of stakeholders. This is an ideal position for someone who thrives in changing environments and can build the roadmap to create innovative product offerings.\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Manage a portfolio of products and/or capabilities and build resource investment allocation plans grounded in data and research\n\n - Define roadmap and requirements to solve the biggest customer problems across one or multiple product lines\n\n - Define  MVP experiences and quickly learn and iterate based on feedback\n\n - Form hypothesis and run experiments using lean methodologies\n\n - Partner closely with engineering and design teams to define, build, and maintain products/features which are critical to growth and retention\n\n - Partner closely with cross-functional teams on release plans and documentation to deliver value to our customers\n\n - Collaborate effectively with GTM partners to plan and launch products and capabilities, including alpha, beta and GA phasis with process success criteria for each phase\n\n - Define success criteria and measure the success and effectiveness of features and capabilities from entitlement, to activation, adoption and retention\n\n - Build business cases justifying investment in feature and capabilities and present to stakeholder across the org\n\n - Proactively partner across teams to anticipate and address risk & dependencies\n\n - Communicate progress and plan to leadership, peers, etc\n\n - Own the business outcomes including revenue of your product\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 8+ years designing and delivering world-class software products in a Product Management role\n\n - Deep customer empathy\n\n - Passion for identifying and solving problems with the ability to conduct effective customer interviews\n\n - Capable of breaking down a big vision into small deliverables\n\n - Ruthless prioritization of the backlog\n\n - Self-starter with an entrepreneurial mindset and the drive to pursue opportunities beyond current constraints\n\n - Exceptional collaboration skills working with PMs, engineers, designers, marketers, and customer success teams\n\n - Growth mindset with a desire for continuous improvement\n\n - Strong verbal and written communication skills\n\n - Strong analytical skills paired with a data-informed mindset\n\n - Experience with 2-sided markets is a plus\n\n - A GM-mindset and ability to ruthlessly prioritize against market opportunity and revenue implications and customer satisfaction\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $165,000 - $270,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"51aa1c0e-c624-424e-b319-5e881ed1ca9a","title":"Senior IT Engineer","department":"IT","team":"IT","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-11T23:12:54.820+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/51aa1c0e-c624-424e-b319-5e881ed1ca9a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/51aa1c0e-c624-424e-b319-5e881ed1ca9a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a member of the IT team, you will play an important role in helping Drata scale securely and thoughtfully as we grow. You’ll build, secure, and continuously improve the systems and processes that power our internal operations across identity and access management, device management, network security, SaaS administration, and workflow automation. This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys combining strong technical depth with an automation-first mindset to create secure, seamless experiences for employees across the business. You’ll partner closely with teams throughout Drata to strengthen our infrastructure, improve security controls, and bring scalable solutions to the tools and workflows people rely on every day. You’ll also leverage Drata’s security and compliance automation platform to help ensure our IT environment meets critical security and compliance requirements as the company continues to grow. As opportunities arise, you’ll be encouraged to blog, speak, and participate in events to share your work and how other companies can learn from Drata’s approach.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and evolve identity, device, and network security infrastructure through infrastructure-as-code, changes are version-controlled, peer-reviewed, and auditable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain automated joiner/mover/leaver workflows so access is provisioned and de-provisioned accurately and on time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enforce least-privilege access across the org through scalable IAM governance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with business departments to evaluate, onboard, and integrate new SaaS tools, owning the full lifecycle from requirements and architecture through to automation and security compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish trust and strong relationships with senior leaders, operations managers, and professional staff across other organizational units</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Security team to continuously raise the bar on IT security posture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own technical documentation, support runbooks, and integration templates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide mentorship to junior staff and encourage their technical development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive AI tool adoption and help the business identify opportunities to integrate AI into workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build internal tools (CLIs, bots, and dashboards) that make the IT team faster and more effective</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Like Apple products? So do we! We are a heavy Mac shop. We need you to have deep technical knowledge of MacOS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be our gatekeeper around IAM and have experience with SSO/SAML solutions like Okta and Ping</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We need you to have experience with MDM software like JAMF, Iru (Kandji), or Fleet</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">RFC shouldn't be just a three letter acronym to you. We need someone who understands technology basics like networking, dns, firewalls, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We live in the cloud so we need you to have AWS or GCP experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We need you to be able to do in-depth troubleshooting to problem solve</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are people who are curious and love to learn new things, we want you to have that desire as well</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be Awesome! You are going to need to work well with your peers because they are often coming to you with problems while frustrated, be kind and clearly communicate to them to make things all better</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SaaS APIs (REST, SOAP, OAuth) for provisioning and automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with infrastructure-as-code (e.g., Terraform) and workflow automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong grasp of system design, scalability, and SaaS operational best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with GitOps workflows and version-controlling infrastructure and configuration changes</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $157,100 - $194,040 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs a member of the IT team, you will play an important role in helping Drata scale securely and thoughtfully as we grow. You’ll build, secure, and continuously improve the systems and processes that power our internal operations across identity and access management, device management, network security, SaaS administration, and workflow automation. This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys combining strong technical depth with an automation-first mindset to create secure, seamless experiences for employees across the business. You’ll partner closely with teams throughout Drata to strengthen our infrastructure, improve security controls, and bring scalable solutions to the tools and workflows people rely on every day. You’ll also leverage Drata’s security and compliance automation platform to help ensure our IT environment meets critical security and compliance requirements as the company continues to grow. As opportunities arise, you’ll be encouraged to blog, speak, and participate in events to share your work and how other companies can learn from Drata’s approach.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Manage and evolve identity, device, and network security infrastructure through infrastructure-as-code, changes are version-controlled, peer-reviewed, and auditable\n\n - Build and maintain automated joiner/mover/leaver workflows so access is provisioned and de-provisioned accurately and on time\n\n - Enforce least-privilege access across the org through scalable IAM governance\n\n - Partner with business departments to evaluate, onboard, and integrate new SaaS tools, owning the full lifecycle from requirements and architecture through to automation and security compliance\n\n - Establish trust and strong relationships with senior leaders, operations managers, and professional staff across other organizational units\n\n - Partner with the Security team to continuously raise the bar on IT security posture\n\n - Own technical documentation, support runbooks, and integration templates\n\n - Provide mentorship to junior staff and encourage their technical development\n\n - Drive AI tool adoption and help the business identify opportunities to integrate AI into workflows\n\n - Build internal tools (CLIs, bots, and dashboards) that make the IT team faster and more effective\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - Like Apple products? So do we! We are a heavy Mac shop. We need you to have deep technical knowledge of MacOS\n\n - Be our gatekeeper around IAM and have experience with SSO/SAML solutions like Okta and Ping\n\n - We need you to have experience with MDM software like JAMF, Iru (Kandji), or Fleet\n\n - RFC shouldn't be just a three letter acronym to you. We need someone who understands technology basics like networking, dns, firewalls, etc.\n\n - We live in the cloud so we need you to have AWS or GCP experience\n\n - We need you to be able to do in-depth troubleshooting to problem solve\n\n - We are people who are curious and love to learn new things, we want you to have that desire as well\n\n - Be Awesome! You are going to need to work well with your peers because they are often coming to you with problems while frustrated, be kind and clearly communicate to them to make things all better\n\n - Familiarity with SaaS APIs (REST, SOAP, OAuth) for provisioning and automation\n\n - Comfort with infrastructure-as-code (e.g., Terraform) and workflow automation\n\n - Strong grasp of system design, scalability, and SaaS operational best practices\n\n - Familiarity with GitOps workflows and version-controlling infrastructure and configuration changes\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $157,100 - $194,040 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d3fd0f22-f933-4a3d-85a6-c37d70a3f7a9","title":"Senior AI Product Engineer 2, Audit","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T15:24:29.445+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/d3fd0f22-f933-4a3d-85a6-c37d70a3f7a9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/d3fd0f22-f933-4a3d-85a6-c37d70a3f7a9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Frontend:</strong> Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Backend:</strong> Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Fluency:</strong> Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with <strong>agent frameworks</strong> (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Streaming &amp; Real-Time UI:</strong> Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Sense:</strong> Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambiguous and the iteration is fast</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impact</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns\n\n - Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly\n\n - Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team\n\n - Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack\n\n - Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development\n\n - Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - Experience: 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features\n\n - Frontend: Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully\n\n - Backend: Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services\n\n - AI Fluency: Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production\n\n - Familiarity with agent frameworks (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows\n\n - Streaming & Real-Time UI: Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs\n\n - Product Sense: Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both\n\n - Collaboration: Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambiguous and the iteration is fast\n\nBonus Qualifications\n\n - Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains\n\n - Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents\n\n - Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer\n\n - Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality\n\nImpact\n\nThis role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:\n\n - Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to\n\n - Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use\n\n - Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last\n\n - Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"55fb184d-d97d-4214-9880-5f60256bbae0","title":"Software Engineer, Monetization Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T15:23:59.498+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/55fb184d-d97d-4214-9880-5f60256bbae0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/55fb184d-d97d-4214-9880-5f60256bbae0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Software Engineer, Monetization Platform serves as an engineer on the Product Platform Group with a primary focus on the systems that turn product usage, subscriptions, credits, commitments, and contracts into accurate customer outcomes and clean financial operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This person will help architect and evolve the core billing domain for Drata: usage event ingestion, billable metrics, pricing and packaging, invoice generation, entitlement enforcement, and the integrations that connect engineering to Accounting, Finance, RevOps, Salesforce, CPQ, and ERP systems like NetSuite.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">They should be equally comfortable designing event-driven systems, shaping commercial flexibility with business stakeholders, and building operationally trustworthy software where correctness, auditability, and scale matter. Modern billing is no longer just “charge a credit card once a month” — it is a real-time product control plane that must support evolving pricing models without turning the codebase into a fragile mess.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Finance, Accounting, RevOps, and Engineering leadership to shape Drata’s long-term billing architecture and commercial flexibility across self-serve and enterprise motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help design the primitives of a modern billing platform: usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, subscriptions, overages, and invoice workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build on a system that can accurately meter product usage at scale, transform raw events into billable quantities, and support pricing changes without requiring constant product rework.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve the entitlement layer that separates pricing and packaging from product behavior, so feature access, limits, credits, and plan controls are programmable rather than hardcoded.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with SFDC admins, CPQ owners, and Finance systems stakeholders to ensure quote-to-cash flows are coherent across CRM, product, billing, ERP, and downstream reporting systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure billing systems are operationally trustworthy: idempotent event handling, strong reconciliation paths, reliable notifications, auditability, and clear observability for engineers and business teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot the hard problems: invoice discrepancies, usage drift, contract edge cases, entitlement bugs, migration failures, and cross-system data mismatches.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience as a software engineer, including meaningful time owning business-critical backend systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience architecting billing, payments, pricing, or quote-to-cash systems for a B2B SaaS company at meaningful scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing APIs and event-driven systems that ingest, validate, aggregate, and reconcile high-volume operational data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of modern billing models, including usage-based pricing, subscriptions, prepaid credits, commitments, overages, hybrid packaging, and enterprise-specific commercial terms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working directly with Accounting, Finance, RevOps, and GTM systems where data quality, auditability, and timing matter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating with systems like Salesforce, CPQ, NetSuite, payment platforms, and downstream finance/reporting tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JavaScript/TypeScript and object-oriented programming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building and consuming RESTful web services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relational databases, data modeling, and transactional workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Distributed systems and asynchronous processing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Writing unit, integration, and end-to-end tests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Logging, telemetry, and production debugging</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Git and modern CI/CD practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least one major cloud platform and modern infrastructure tooling</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong product and systems mindset: you can model the commercial domain cleanly, but you also know billing architecture is ultimately customer experience architecture.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus Qualifications</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Usage-based billing platforms such as Metronome, especially concepts like usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, and programmable invoice workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entitlement and monetization platforms such as Stigg, especially entitlements as a system of record for feature access, limits, credits, and packaging logic.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building systems that support both PLG/self-serve and enterprise sales motions on the same technical foundation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit logs, RBAC, webhooks, durable queues, and other patterns that make billing and monetization systems reliable and debuggable in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-assisted development tools</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ve had success in roles where you:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architected or modernized a billing system that had to support real usage metering, invoice correctness, and flexible commercial models rather than a single static subscription plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built systems where raw product activity was transformed into durable billing inputs and surfaced in customer-facing or internal financial workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Worked through pricing and packaging changes without repeatedly hardcoding logic into application code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supported models like prepaid credits, subscriptions with overage, enterprise commitments, or hybrid contracts for different customer segments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partnered directly with Finance, Accounting, and RevOps to close gaps between what the product did, what the customer bought, and what the company invoiced.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $131,00- $178,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Software Engineer, Monetization Platform serves as an engineer on the Product Platform Group with a primary focus on the systems that turn product usage, subscriptions, credits, commitments, and contracts into accurate customer outcomes and clean financial operations.\n\nThis person will help architect and evolve the core billing domain for Drata: usage event ingestion, billable metrics, pricing and packaging, invoice generation, entitlement enforcement, and the integrations that connect engineering to Accounting, Finance, RevOps, Salesforce, CPQ, and ERP systems like NetSuite.\n\nThey should be equally comfortable designing event-driven systems, shaping commercial flexibility with business stakeholders, and building operationally trustworthy software where correctness, auditability, and scale matter. Modern billing is no longer just “charge a credit card once a month” — it is a real-time product control plane that must support evolving pricing models without turning the codebase into a fragile mess.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Partner with Product, Finance, Accounting, RevOps, and Engineering leadership to shape Drata’s long-term billing architecture and commercial flexibility across self-serve and enterprise motions.\n\n - Help design the primitives of a modern billing platform: usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, subscriptions, overages, and invoice workflows.\n\n - Build on a system that can accurately meter product usage at scale, transform raw events into billable quantities, and support pricing changes without requiring constant product rework.\n\n - Build and evolve the entitlement layer that separates pricing and packaging from product behavior, so feature access, limits, credits, and plan controls are programmable rather than hardcoded.\n\n - Work closely with SFDC admins, CPQ owners, and Finance systems stakeholders to ensure quote-to-cash flows are coherent across CRM, product, billing, ERP, and downstream reporting systems.\n\n - Ensure billing systems are operationally trustworthy: idempotent event handling, strong reconciliation paths, reliable notifications, auditability, and clear observability for engineers and business teams.\n\n - Troubleshoot the hard problems: invoice discrepancies, usage drift, contract edge cases, entitlement bugs, migration failures, and cross-system data mismatches.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 3+ years of experience as a software engineer, including meaningful time owning business-critical backend systems in production.\n\n - Experience architecting billing, payments, pricing, or quote-to-cash systems for a B2B SaaS company at meaningful scale.\n\n - Experience designing APIs and event-driven systems that ingest, validate, aggregate, and reconcile high-volume operational data.\n\n - Understanding of modern billing models, including usage-based pricing, subscriptions, prepaid credits, commitments, overages, hybrid packaging, and enterprise-specific commercial terms.\n\n - Experience working directly with Accounting, Finance, RevOps, and GTM systems where data quality, auditability, and timing matter.\n\n - Experience integrating with systems like Salesforce, CPQ, NetSuite, payment platforms, and downstream finance/reporting tooling.\n\n - Strong proficiency with:\n   \n   - JavaScript/TypeScript and object-oriented programming\n   \n   - Building and consuming RESTful web services\n   \n   - Relational databases, data modeling, and transactional workflows\n   \n   - Distributed systems and asynchronous processing\n   \n   - Writing unit, integration, and end-to-end tests\n   \n   - Logging, telemetry, and production debugging\n   \n   - Git and modern CI/CD practices\n   \n   - At least one major cloud platform and modern infrastructure tooling\n\n - A strong product and systems mindset: you can model the commercial domain cleanly, but you also know billing architecture is ultimately customer experience architecture.\n\nBonus Qualifications\n\n - Usage-based billing platforms such as Metronome, especially concepts like usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, and programmable invoice workflows.\n\n - Entitlement and monetization platforms such as Stigg, especially entitlements as a system of record for feature access, limits, credits, and packaging logic.\n\n - Building systems that support both PLG/self-serve and enterprise sales motions on the same technical foundation.\n\n - Audit logs, RBAC, webhooks, durable queues, and other patterns that make billing and monetization systems reliable and debuggable in production.\n\n - AI-assisted development tools\n\nYou’ve had success in roles where you:\n\n - Architected or modernized a billing system that had to support real usage metering, invoice correctness, and flexible commercial models rather than a single static subscription plan.\n\n - Built systems where raw product activity was transformed into durable billing inputs and surfaced in customer-facing or internal financial workflows.\n\n - Worked through pricing and packaging changes without repeatedly hardcoding logic into application code.\n\n - Supported models like prepaid credits, subscriptions with overage, enterprise commitments, or hybrid contracts for different customer segments.\n\n - Partnered directly with Finance, Accounting, and RevOps to close gaps between what the product did, what the customer bought, and what the company invoiced.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $131,00- $178,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d374d673-9903-4189-9190-fbb9c419db47","title":"Staff Platform Engineer, Interoperability","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T15:23:32.293+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/d374d673-9903-4189-9190-fbb9c419db47","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/d374d673-9903-4189-9190-fbb9c419db47/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Platform Engineer plays a pivotal role in crafting and enhancing the tools and platform that elevate the development experience for our internal engineering teams. By focusing on developer efficiency, tooling, and the seamless integration of our development processes, this position is essential in enabling our teams to deliver innovative products rapidly and reliably.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and maintain a comprehensive platform that supports internal development workflows, from code inception to deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the creation of developer tools that automate and streamline our CI/CD processes, enhancing productivity and ensuring consistency across environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement monitoring and analytics tools that provide actionable insights into application performance and development pipeline efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with the Infrastructure and Data Teams to enhance developer tooling and data access, streamlining data-driven development and analytics processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and design architecture diagrams to guide the development of scalable and efficient systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and guide team members, fostering their growth and development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product managers to translate product requirements into technical specifications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and develop highly scalable web applications and RESTful APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build tools, services, and automation to enhance the capabilities of our platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate and enhance the performance, durability, and security of production applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to server-side code and database architecture using NodeJS and NestJS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to client-side code using React.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure adherence to best practices through thorough code reviews and coaching.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt quickly to evolving business needs and transition between different contexts seamlessly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience as a software engineer, with a proven track record of delivering complex solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience with NodeJS and React, with familiarity in NestJS and/or NextJS being a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Temporal, Terraform, ElasticSearch/OpenSearch, PostgreSQL, and Snowflake, JavaScript, ES6, TypeORM, MySQL, Git, Jest, Redis, REST principles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in AWS hosting and building in AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong object-oriented programming skills and understanding of algorithms and web services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience leading engineering teams and delivering successful projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed and independent, with a passion for driving complete features/products from inception to delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to navigate and negotiate difficult tradeoffs effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agile development experience, with a preference for candidates with startup or scaling experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: Familiarity with Temporal, Terraform, ElasticSearch/OpenSearch, PostgreSQL, and Snowflake.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This role will receive a competitive base salary, benefits, and stock, typically in the form of Restricted Stock Units (RSUs). The applicable salary range for this role is: $200,000 - $271,500.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A variety of factors are considered when determining someone’s leveling and compensation–including a candidate’s professional background and experience. These ranges may be modified in the future and final offer amounts may vary from the amounts listed above.</em> </p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Staff Platform Engineer plays a pivotal role in crafting and enhancing the tools and platform that elevate the development experience for our internal engineering teams. By focusing on developer efficiency, tooling, and the seamless integration of our development processes, this position is essential in enabling our teams to deliver innovative products rapidly and reliably.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Design, develop, and maintain a comprehensive platform that supports internal development workflows, from code inception to deployment.\n\n - Lead the creation of developer tools that automate and streamline our CI/CD processes, enhancing productivity and ensuring consistency across environments.\n\n - Implement monitoring and analytics tools that provide actionable insights into application performance and development pipeline efficiency.\n\n - Work closely with the Infrastructure and Data Teams to enhance developer tooling and data access, streamlining data-driven development and analytics processes.\n\n - Create and design architecture diagrams to guide the development of scalable and efficient systems.\n\n - Mentor and guide team members, fostering their growth and development.\n\n - Collaborate with product managers to translate product requirements into technical specifications.\n\n - Architect and develop highly scalable web applications and RESTful APIs.\n\n - Build tools, services, and automation to enhance the capabilities of our platform.\n\n - Evaluate and enhance the performance, durability, and security of production applications.\n\n - Contribute to server-side code and database architecture using NodeJS and NestJS.\n\n - Contribute to client-side code using React.\n\n - Ensure adherence to best practices through thorough code reviews and coaching.\n\n - Adapt quickly to evolving business needs and transition between different contexts seamlessly.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 10+ years of experience as a software engineer, with a proven track record of delivering complex solutions.\n\n - 3+ years of experience with NodeJS and React, with familiarity in NestJS and/or NextJS being a plus.\n\n - Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or related field.\n\n - Proficiency in Temporal, Terraform, ElasticSearch/OpenSearch, PostgreSQL, and Snowflake, JavaScript, ES6, TypeORM, MySQL, Git, Jest, Redis, REST principles.\n\n - Experience in AWS hosting and building in AWS.\n\n - Strong object-oriented programming skills and understanding of algorithms and web services.\n\n - Previous experience leading engineering teams and delivering successful projects.\n\n - Self-directed and independent, with a passion for driving complete features/products from inception to delivery.\n\n - Ability to navigate and negotiate difficult tradeoffs effectively.\n\n - Agile development experience, with a preference for candidates with startup or scaling experience.\n\n - Nice to have: Familiarity with Temporal, Terraform, ElasticSearch/OpenSearch, PostgreSQL, and Snowflake.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThis role will receive a competitive base salary, benefits, and stock, typically in the form of Restricted Stock Units (RSUs). The applicable salary range for this role is: $200,000 - $271,500.\n\nA variety of factors are considered when determining someone’s leveling and compensation–including a candidate’s professional background and experience. These ranges may be modified in the future and final offer amounts may vary from the amounts listed above. ","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0dc5c970-7211-4a8b-8703-3bd521318586","title":"Senior Data Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T15:23:39.687+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0dc5c970-7211-4a8b-8703-3bd521318586","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0dc5c970-7211-4a8b-8703-3bd521318586/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is looking for a Senior Data Engineer! This person will be a key member of the growing data team, supporting one of the fastest growing B2B SaaS startups to achieve unicorn status. At Drata, we’re on a mission to help build trust across the internet! Data accuracy is an essential cornerstone of our mission.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a senior data engineer that can help us strategize and execute our data engineering vision. We’re looking for someone who enjoys building data products at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are building out a first-class data department composed of Data Engineers, Software Engineers, Analytics Engineers, Data Analysts, and Data Scientists. We ensure all teams at Drata can easily self-serve the data and report they need to drive their projects and make decisions. If you’re excited to work on a fast-moving team using cutting-edge technologies to collect, store, transform, analyze, and model data, we want to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automate first! One of our core company values is automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help us build data products that will serve analytics needs, product and engineering services and ML models</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize query performance, data ingestion and processing time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to building the data modeling layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong data governance processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build solid data engineering training and documentation for all analysts so they can learn how to use, move and transform data with minimum data engineering assistance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interview, hire and train future data engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administrate data orchestration through modern tools concepts such as ETL, ELT, Reverse ETL etc.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 5+ years experience as a Data Engineer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are fluent in writing analytical SQL, are able to write complex queries with no assistance, understand the difference between SQL that works and performant SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in Python</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience with some of the following platforms Stitch/Fivetran, Snowflake, dbt, Airflow, Airbyte, Looker/Mode/Sigma, Hightouch/Cencus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a clear, concise communicator that works well with others</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can explain complex data flows, datasets or queries to non-technical people in understandable ways</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: experienced with building ML pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a natural curiosity and investigative mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You want to work in a fast, high-growth startup environment and thrive on both autonomy and collaboration</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $151,000 - $205,300 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is looking for a Senior Data Engineer! This person will be a key member of the growing data team, supporting one of the fastest growing B2B SaaS startups to achieve unicorn status. At Drata, we’re on a mission to help build trust across the internet! Data accuracy is an essential cornerstone of our mission.\n\nWe are looking for a senior data engineer that can help us strategize and execute our data engineering vision. We’re looking for someone who enjoys building data products at scale.\n\nWe are building out a first-class data department composed of Data Engineers, Software Engineers, Analytics Engineers, Data Analysts, and Data Scientists. We ensure all teams at Drata can easily self-serve the data and report they need to drive their projects and make decisions. If you’re excited to work on a fast-moving team using cutting-edge technologies to collect, store, transform, analyze, and model data, we want to meet you.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Automate first! One of our core company values is automation.\n\n - Help us build data products that will serve analytics needs, product and engineering services and ML models\n\n - Optimize query performance, data ingestion and processing time\n\n - Contribute to building the data modeling layer\n\n - Build strong data governance processes\n\n - Build solid data engineering training and documentation for all analysts so they can learn how to use, move and transform data with minimum data engineering assistance.\n\n - Interview, hire and train future data engineers\n\n - Administrate data orchestration through modern tools concepts such as ETL, ELT, Reverse ETL etc.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - You have 5+ years experience as a Data Engineer\n\n - You are fluent in writing analytical SQL, are able to write complex queries with no assistance, understand the difference between SQL that works and performant SQL\n\n - Fluent in Python\n\n - You have experience with some of the following platforms Stitch/Fivetran, Snowflake, dbt, Airflow, Airbyte, Looker/Mode/Sigma, Hightouch/Cencus\n\n - You are a clear, concise communicator that works well with others\n\n - You can explain complex data flows, datasets or queries to non-technical people in understandable ways\n\n - Bonus: experienced with building ML pipelines\n\n - You have a natural curiosity and investigative mindset\n\n - You want to work in a fast, high-growth startup environment and thrive on both autonomy and collaboration\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $151,000 - $205,300 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"964c909d-8cda-4cc1-a58a-1939e6496bb9","title":"Senior Platform Engineer, Interoperability","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T15:23:34.741+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/964c909d-8cda-4cc1-a58a-1939e6496bb9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/964c909d-8cda-4cc1-a58a-1939e6496bb9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Platform “Senior Software Engineer” will help lead the platform development by making architecture decisions to ensure we're building clean, maintainable, and beautiful applications. This person is responsible for maintaining, expanding, and scaling our platform systems that SCALE our Application Development team. Your “customer” is not Drata’s normal users, it’s developers both internally and externally. You’ll develop specifications for moderately complex software programming applications and modify/maintain the existing software. This position participates in design and coding activities with other staff members. They will operate in a distributed architecture, building the infrastructure to manage Big Data and solve complex algorithmic problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and build platform systems that will allow our application developers to build faster more reliable software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builds tools, services, and automation to extend the platform capabilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Runs critical operational portions of our ingestion, analytics, and storage infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborates with our product managers to define strategic solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluates and improves the performance, durability, and security of applications in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assists with server-side code and database architecture on the back-end in NodeJS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with management to ensure quality in solutions and in software design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in development lifecycle activities like design, coding, testing, and production release</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write reusable, testable, and efficient code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver code in an agile team environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and train on technologies you think may be appropriate for current or future projects</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience as a software engineer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience with NodeJS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years experience in NestJS preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong skills needed in: Javascript, ES6, Temporal, NodeJS, TypeORM, MySQL, Git, and REST principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge in Jest and Redis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in object-oriented programming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of algorithms, network protocols, and web services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with building in AWS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: Terraform, ElasticSearch, &amp; Snowflake</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed, independent, and has experience owning complete features/products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing real-world web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding ability to negotiate difficult tradeoffs (e.g., quality vs. speed, collaboration vs. get-it-done)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Agile development experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous startup or scaling experience is a plus</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and adaptable to changing technologies and requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication ability - we want to know your thoughts and input!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual in English &amp; Spanish is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $151,000 - $205,300 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Platform “Senior Software Engineer” will help lead the platform development by making architecture decisions to ensure we're building clean, maintainable, and beautiful applications. This person is responsible for maintaining, expanding, and scaling our platform systems that SCALE our Application Development team. Your “customer” is not Drata’s normal users, it’s developers both internally and externally. You’ll develop specifications for moderately complex software programming applications and modify/maintain the existing software. This position participates in design and coding activities with other staff members. They will operate in a distributed architecture, building the infrastructure to manage Big Data and solve complex algorithmic problems.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Architect and build platform systems that will allow our application developers to build faster more reliable software\n\n - Builds tools, services, and automation to extend the platform capabilities\n\n - Runs critical operational portions of our ingestion, analytics, and storage infrastructure\n\n - Collaborates with our product managers to define strategic solutions\n\n - Evaluates and improves the performance, durability, and security of applications in production\n\n - Assists with server-side code and database architecture on the back-end in NodeJS\n\n - Work with management to ensure quality in solutions and in software design\n\n - Participate in development lifecycle activities like design, coding, testing, and production release\n\n - Write reusable, testable, and efficient code\n\n - Deliver code in an agile team environment\n\n - Research and train on technologies you think may be appropriate for current or future projects\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 5+ years of experience as a software engineer\n\n - 3+ years of experience with NodeJS\n\n - 1+ years experience in NestJS preferred\n\n - Strong skills needed in: Javascript, ES6, Temporal, NodeJS, TypeORM, MySQL, Git, and REST principles\n\n - Knowledge in Jest and Redis\n\n - Proficiency in object-oriented programming\n\n - Good understanding of algorithms, network protocols, and web services\n\n - Experience with building in AWS\n\n - Nice to have: Terraform, ElasticSearch, & Snowflake\n\n - Self-directed, independent, and has experience owning complete features/products\n\n - Experience developing real-world web applications\n\n - Outstanding ability to negotiate difficult tradeoffs (e.g., quality vs. speed, collaboration vs. get-it-done)\n\n - Agile development experience\n\n - Previous startup or scaling experience is a plus\n\n - Self-motivated and adaptable to changing technologies and requirements\n\n - Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\n - Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or related field\n\n - Strong communication ability - we want to know your thoughts and input!\n\n - Bilingual in English & Spanish is a plus.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $151,000 - $205,300 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2a5487d8-9bfa-4a5e-9969-3c56aa7c25c0","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Core GRC","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T17:47:30.379+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/2a5487d8-9bfa-4a5e-9969-3c56aa7c25c0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/2a5487d8-9bfa-4a5e-9969-3c56aa7c25c0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Software Engineer serves as a technical leader across multiple small teams. They design and build scalable systems, guide architectural decisions, and tackle complex challenges that span codebases and domains. They work closely with Product and Engineering leadership to shape the technical roadmap, ensure systems are reliable and secure, and drive key cross-team initiatives from idea to implementation. The role balances deep technical work, collaborative problem-solving, and mentoring in a distributed environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product to shape roadmap requirements and recommend the right technologies and design patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review architecture and code for your team’s projects to ensure quality, scalability, and security—while empowering the team to own implementation and delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot performance and scalability issues escalated from your teams. Identify root causes, guide solutions, and see them through to resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and deliver cross-team projects that are difficult to tackle at the team level—such as introducing new frameworks, improving the developer experience, or migrating shared functionality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers across teams through guilds, office hours, and informal coaching.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience as a software engineer, with a strong foundation in building and maintaining production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience working with Node.js or React in production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years of experience with NestJS (preferred).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related technical field, or equivalent experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with authentication &amp; authorization protocols like OAuth, SCIM, OIDC, and RBAC systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In depth knowledge of authentication and authorization systems from large third party providers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong proficiency with:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JavaScript/TypeScript and object-oriented programming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building and consuming RESTful web services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Networking protocols and relational databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Writing unit, integration, and end-to-end tests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Using logging and telemetry tools to monitor and debug production systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working with Git and modern CI/CD practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least one major cloud platform (e.g., AWS, GCP, Azure) or infrastructure as code tools (e.g., Terraform, Pulumi)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have experience with:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-assisted development tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">TypeORM, Jest, Redis, and ElasticSearch</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ve had success in roles where you:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successfully completed the migration of a large company to a complex, third-party authentication system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Led groups of engineers through feature delivery, from scoping and ticket creation to implementation and release</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Owned major products or features, balancing technical tradeoffs like quality vs. speed or team autonomy vs. alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built and scaled real-world web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Worked in fast-paced environments, such as startups or growth-stage companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicated architectural decisions clearly across teams and kept stakeholders informed through status updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balanced individual contributor work with time spent mentoring or unblocking teammates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adopted new technologies and introduced them thoughtfully into a codebase</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Used product development methodologies like Scrum, Kanban, or Lean</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $200,700 - $271,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Staff Software Engineer serves as a technical leader across multiple small teams. They design and build scalable systems, guide architectural decisions, and tackle complex challenges that span codebases and domains. They work closely with Product and Engineering leadership to shape the technical roadmap, ensure systems are reliable and secure, and drive key cross-team initiatives from idea to implementation. The role balances deep technical work, collaborative problem-solving, and mentoring in a distributed environment.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Partner with Product to shape roadmap requirements and recommend the right technologies and design patterns.\n\n - Review architecture and code for your team’s projects to ensure quality, scalability, and security—while empowering the team to own implementation and delivery.\n\n - Troubleshoot performance and scalability issues escalated from your teams. Identify root causes, guide solutions, and see them through to resolution.\n\n - Own and deliver cross-team projects that are difficult to tackle at the team level—such as introducing new frameworks, improving the developer experience, or migrating shared functionality.\n\n - Mentor engineers across teams through guilds, office hours, and informal coaching.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 10+ years of experience as a software engineer, with a strong foundation in building and maintaining production systems.\n\n - 3+ years of experience working with Node.js or React in production environments.\n\n - 1+ years of experience with NestJS (preferred).\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related technical field, or equivalent experience.\n\n - Strong experience with authentication & authorization protocols like OAuth, SCIM, OIDC, and RBAC systems\n\n - In depth knowledge of authentication and authorization systems from large third party providers\n\nStrong proficiency with:\n\n - JavaScript/TypeScript and object-oriented programming\n\n - Building and consuming RESTful web services\n\n - Networking protocols and relational databases\n\n - Writing unit, integration, and end-to-end tests\n\n - Using logging and telemetry tools to monitor and debug production systems\n\n - Working with Git and modern CI/CD practices\n\n - At least one major cloud platform (e.g., AWS, GCP, Azure) or infrastructure as code tools (e.g., Terraform, Pulumi)\n\nNice to have experience with:\n\n - AI-assisted development tools\n\n - TypeORM, Jest, Redis, and ElasticSearch\n\nYou’ve had success in roles where you:\n\n - Successfully completed the migration of a large company to a complex, third-party authentication system.\n\n - Led groups of engineers through feature delivery, from scoping and ticket creation to implementation and release\n\n - Owned major products or features, balancing technical tradeoffs like quality vs. speed or team autonomy vs. alignment\n\n - Built and scaled real-world web applications\n\n - Worked in fast-paced environments, such as startups or growth-stage companies\n\n - Communicated architectural decisions clearly across teams and kept stakeholders informed through status updates\n\n - Balanced individual contributor work with time spent mentoring or unblocking teammates\n\n - Adopted new technologies and introduced them thoughtfully into a codebase\n\n - Used product development methodologies like Scrum, Kanban, or Lean\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $200,700 - $271,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4b844879-4a4f-476a-b8c4-6f9cd4b47f61","title":"Business Development Lead, AWS","department":"Business Development","team":"Business Development","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T18:28:04.844+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/4b844879-4a4f-476a-b8c4-6f9cd4b47f61","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/4b844879-4a4f-476a-b8c4-6f9cd4b47f61/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Senior Business Development Lead, Cloud Service Providers to join the Drata team. This is a senior individual contributor role responsible for leading and expanding Drata's strategic partnerships across major cloud providers, including AWS. As the primary owner of our CSP partner strategy, you will shape how Drata co-sells, co-markets, and integrates within the cloud ecosystem.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will operate at both a strategic and executional level -  defining the partner motion, enabling field teams across both sides, and directly driving high-value pipelines with and through CSP partners. This role requires a seasoned professional who can influence and navigate large organizations, and consistently translate partnerships into measurable revenue impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to build and own a critical growth lever for Drata at scale - shaping strategy, establishing executive relationships, and leaving a lasting mark on how the company grows through the cloud ecosystem.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and drive Drata's Cloud Service Provider partnership strategy across AWS, defining priorities, go-to-market plays, and success metrics aligned to company revenue goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the senior point of contact and relationship owner for CSP partner organizations, cultivating executive-level relationships with Partner Development Managers, Field Sales leaders, Marketplace teams, and Industry/Segment leads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead complex, multi-stakeholder co-sell and co-market engagements — orchestrating account mapping, pipeline reviews, joint GTM campaigns, field enablement, and executive interlocks across CSP organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and own Drata's Marketplace strategy across AWS, partnering with Product, RevOps, and Finance to optimize listings, private offers, CPPO/PPO structures, and procurement paths to drive Marketplace-sourced ARR.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive senior-level pipeline generation by building strategic joint target account lists, activating CSP field teams, and designing scalable co-sell motions that produce consistent partner-sourced and partner-influenced revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and deliver executive-level enablement to CSP stakeholders - communicating Drata's vision, product strategy, and key differentiators in the context of cloud compliance, AI governance, and Trust Center outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Product, and RevOps to architect and execute joint GTM programs including events, webinars, campaigns, and field plays — ensuring tight integration between Drata and CSP field motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and own reporting frameworks for CSP partnership performance - tracking pipeline, sourced/influenced revenue, Marketplace adoption, and co-sell velocity - and presenting insights and recommendations to leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and inform best practices across the broader partnerships organization, acting as a subject matter expert on CSP programs and elevating team capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Drata at industry and partner events, engaging with CSP leadership, prospects, and customers to strengthen relationships and capture strategic intelligence.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 + years of experience in partnerships, business development, or cloud alliances, with a significant portion focused on CSP ecosystems (AWS, GCP, or Azure) either within a CSP or as a strategic ISV partner.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated track record of owning and scaling cloud partnerships that have produced measurable, material pipeline and revenue impact at a senior level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep knowledge of CSP programs and motions — including co-sell frameworks (ACE, Partner Advantage, MPN/MPE), Marketplace models (CPPO, PPO, transactable listings), and partner incentive and funding programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic thinker and operator — equally comfortable setting long-term partnership direction and rolling up your sleeves to execute on the details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with C-level and VP-level stakeholders both internally and at CSP organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to influence and align cross-functional teams (Sales, Marketing, Product, Finance) around a shared partnership strategy without formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of B2B SaaS, ideally in security, compliance, cloud infrastructure, or DevOps — with the ability to articulate technical value propositions to both technical and business audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed and entrepreneurial — you set your own agenda, drive outcomes with urgency, and take ownership from strategy through execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple strategic initiatives, partner relationships, and pipeline motions simultaneously across CSP organizations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in GRC, security, compliance automation, or risk — with familiarity with frameworks such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, or PCI DSS.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between $186,600 - $230,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Business Development Lead, Cloud Service Providers to join the Drata team. This is a senior individual contributor role responsible for leading and expanding Drata's strategic partnerships across major cloud providers, including AWS. As the primary owner of our CSP partner strategy, you will shape how Drata co-sells, co-markets, and integrates within the cloud ecosystem.\n\nYou will operate at both a strategic and executional level -  defining the partner motion, enabling field teams across both sides, and directly driving high-value pipelines with and through CSP partners. This role requires a seasoned professional who can influence and navigate large organizations, and consistently translate partnerships into measurable revenue impact.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to build and own a critical growth lever for Drata at scale - shaping strategy, establishing executive relationships, and leaving a lasting mark on how the company grows through the cloud ecosystem.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Own and drive Drata's Cloud Service Provider partnership strategy across AWS, defining priorities, go-to-market plays, and success metrics aligned to company revenue goals.\n\n - Serve as the senior point of contact and relationship owner for CSP partner organizations, cultivating executive-level relationships with Partner Development Managers, Field Sales leaders, Marketplace teams, and Industry/Segment leads.\n\n - Lead complex, multi-stakeholder co-sell and co-market engagements — orchestrating account mapping, pipeline reviews, joint GTM campaigns, field enablement, and executive interlocks across CSP organizations.\n\n - Define and own Drata's Marketplace strategy across AWS, partnering with Product, RevOps, and Finance to optimize listings, private offers, CPPO/PPO structures, and procurement paths to drive Marketplace-sourced ARR.\n\n - Drive senior-level pipeline generation by building strategic joint target account lists, activating CSP field teams, and designing scalable co-sell motions that produce consistent partner-sourced and partner-influenced revenue.\n\n - Build and deliver executive-level enablement to CSP stakeholders - communicating Drata's vision, product strategy, and key differentiators in the context of cloud compliance, AI governance, and Trust Center outcomes.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Product, and RevOps to architect and execute joint GTM programs including events, webinars, campaigns, and field plays — ensuring tight integration between Drata and CSP field motions.\n\n - Establish and own reporting frameworks for CSP partnership performance - tracking pipeline, sourced/influenced revenue, Marketplace adoption, and co-sell velocity - and presenting insights and recommendations to leadership.\n\n - Mentor and inform best practices across the broader partnerships organization, acting as a subject matter expert on CSP programs and elevating team capabilities.\n\n - Represent Drata at industry and partner events, engaging with CSP leadership, prospects, and customers to strengthen relationships and capture strategic intelligence.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 3 + years of experience in partnerships, business development, or cloud alliances, with a significant portion focused on CSP ecosystems (AWS, GCP, or Azure) either within a CSP or as a strategic ISV partner.\n\n - Demonstrated track record of owning and scaling cloud partnerships that have produced measurable, material pipeline and revenue impact at a senior level.\n\n - Deep knowledge of CSP programs and motions — including co-sell frameworks (ACE, Partner Advantage, MPN/MPE), Marketplace models (CPPO, PPO, transactable listings), and partner incentive and funding programs.\n\n - Strategic thinker and operator — equally comfortable setting long-term partnership direction and rolling up your sleeves to execute on the details.\n\n - Strong executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with C-level and VP-level stakeholders both internally and at CSP organizations.\n\n - Proven ability to influence and align cross-functional teams (Sales, Marketing, Product, Finance) around a shared partnership strategy without formal authority.\n\n - Deep understanding of B2B SaaS, ideally in security, compliance, cloud infrastructure, or DevOps — with the ability to articulate technical value propositions to both technical and business audiences.\n\n - Self-directed and entrepreneurial — you set your own agenda, drive outcomes with urgency, and take ownership from strategy through execution.\n\n - Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple strategic initiatives, partner relationships, and pipeline motions simultaneously across CSP organizations.\n\nNice to have:\n\n - Background in GRC, security, compliance automation, or risk — with familiarity with frameworks such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, or PCI DSS.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between $186,600 - $230,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ac2552d7-fd19-465b-b1aa-41be4a8d1a45","title":"Commercial Account Executive - Chicago/Minneapolis","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-26T20:45:35.327+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/ac2552d7-fd19-465b-b1aa-41be4a8d1a45","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/ac2552d7-fd19-465b-b1aa-41be4a8d1a45/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a high performing Commercial Account Executive with a strong track record of quota attainment, new business generation, and consultative selling. This person thrives in a fast moving environment, takes ownership of their pipeline, and knows how to build trust with senior buyers through strong discovery, structured execution, and clear communication.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The strongest candidates will bring experience in full cycle B2B SaaS sales, a history of self generating pipeline, and the ability to operate with both urgency and discipline in an entrepreneurial environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>We will be hiring for a Commercial AE in either Atlanta or Chicago.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a full cycle commercial sales motion from prospecting through close, with a focus on landing new customers and exceeding revenue targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generate and manage pipeline through outbound prospecting, referrals, partnerships, and territory development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and prioritize prospects aligned to Drata’s ICP</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead consultative discovery with senior stakeholders to uncover business pain, validate urgency, and align Drata’s value to customer needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and execute thoughtful account and territory strategies to drive pipeline creation and revenue growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run a disciplined sales process, including qualification, multithreading, mutual action planning, and accurate forecasting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver compelling, tailored presentations that connect customer priorities to business value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner effectively across internal teams to move deals forward and improve the customer buying experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share market feedback and customer insights that help strengthen messaging, process, and product direction</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in a customer facing B2B SaaS sales role, including at least 2 years as a quota carrying new business closer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear evidence of quota overattainment, pipeline generation, or top performer recognition in prior roles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong hunter mentality with a passion for creating opportunities, not just managing inbound demand</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience succeeding in a startup, growth stage, or build mode environment where ownership and adaptability are essential</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience confidently demoing software to a variety of stakeholders, with the ability to tailor presentations to customer needs, articulate business value and outcomes, and effectively progress opportunities through the sales cycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with sales methodologies such as MEDDPICC, MEDDICC, SPICED, or similar frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building pipeline through partnerships, local market development, or self sourced outbound strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A consultative selling style with strong discovery skills and the ability to uncover customer pain, navigate buying committees, and engage executive stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A structured approach to sales execution, including comfort with qualification frameworks, forecasting rigor, and deal planning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to tailor messaging to different audiences and build credibility quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High personal accountability, strong preparation habits, and a coachable mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resourcefulness, resilience, and a bias toward action in ambiguous environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong judgment, integrity, and customer focus</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have - Experience selling into security, compliance, risk, or adjacent technical buyers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between $165,000 - $253,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe’re looking for a high performing Commercial Account Executive with a strong track record of quota attainment, new business generation, and consultative selling. This person thrives in a fast moving environment, takes ownership of their pipeline, and knows how to build trust with senior buyers through strong discovery, structured execution, and clear communication.\n\nThe strongest candidates will bring experience in full cycle B2B SaaS sales, a history of self generating pipeline, and the ability to operate with both urgency and discipline in an entrepreneurial environment.\n\nWe will be hiring for a Commercial AE in either Atlanta or Chicago.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Own a full cycle commercial sales motion from prospecting through close, with a focus on landing new customers and exceeding revenue targets\n\n - Generate and manage pipeline through outbound prospecting, referrals, partnerships, and territory development\n\n - Identify and prioritize prospects aligned to Drata’s ICP\n\n - Lead consultative discovery with senior stakeholders to uncover business pain, validate urgency, and align Drata’s value to customer needs\n\n - Build and execute thoughtful account and territory strategies to drive pipeline creation and revenue growth\n\n - Run a disciplined sales process, including qualification, multithreading, mutual action planning, and accurate forecasting\n\n - Deliver compelling, tailored presentations that connect customer priorities to business value\n\n - Partner effectively across internal teams to move deals forward and improve the customer buying experience\n\n - Share market feedback and customer insights that help strengthen messaging, process, and product direction\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 3+ years of experience in a customer facing B2B SaaS sales role, including at least 2 years as a quota carrying new business closer\n\n - Clear evidence of quota overattainment, pipeline generation, or top performer recognition in prior roles\n\n - Strong hunter mentality with a passion for creating opportunities, not just managing inbound demand\n\n - Experience succeeding in a startup, growth stage, or build mode environment where ownership and adaptability are essential\n\n - Experience confidently demoing software to a variety of stakeholders, with the ability to tailor presentations to customer needs, articulate business value and outcomes, and effectively progress opportunities through the sales cycle\n\n - Familiarity with sales methodologies such as MEDDPICC, MEDDICC, SPICED, or similar frameworks\n\n - Experience building pipeline through partnerships, local market development, or self sourced outbound strategies\n\n - A consultative selling style with strong discovery skills and the ability to uncover customer pain, navigate buying committees, and engage executive stakeholders\n\n - A structured approach to sales execution, including comfort with qualification frameworks, forecasting rigor, and deal planning\n\n - Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to tailor messaging to different audiences and build credibility quickly\n\n - High personal accountability, strong preparation habits, and a coachable mindset\n\n - Resourcefulness, resilience, and a bias toward action in ambiguous environments\n\n - Strong judgment, integrity, and customer focus\n\n - Nice to have - Experience selling into security, compliance, risk, or adjacent technical buyers\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between $165,000 - $253,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"855d1119-f88e-4421-b0f3-884926f48a21","title":"Senior AI Product Engineer 2, Evidence","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-30T00:39:10.289+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/855d1119-f88e-4421-b0f3-884926f48a21","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/855d1119-f88e-4421-b0f3-884926f48a21/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Frontend:</strong> Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Backend:</strong> Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Fluency:</strong> Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with <strong>agent frameworks</strong> (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Streaming &amp; Real-Time UI:</strong> Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Sense:</strong> Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambiguous and the iteration is fast</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impact</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns\n\n - Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly\n\n - Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team\n\n - Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack\n\n - Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development\n\n - Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - Experience: 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features\n\n - Frontend: Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully\n\n - Backend: Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services\n\n - AI Fluency: Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production\n\n - Familiarity with agent frameworks (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows\n\n - Streaming & Real-Time UI: Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs\n\n - Product Sense: Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both\n\n - Collaboration: Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambiguous and the iteration is fast\n\nBonus Qualifications\n\n - Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains\n\n - Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents\n\n - Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer\n\n - Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality\n\nImpact\n\nThis role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:\n\n - Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to\n\n - Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use\n\n - Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last\n\n - Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"03b2d32a-b1af-4a67-8239-5ae3abcc2118","title":"Senior AI Product Engineer 2, Control Monitoring","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-30T00:39:16.165+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/03b2d32a-b1af-4a67-8239-5ae3abcc2118","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/03b2d32a-b1af-4a67-8239-5ae3abcc2118/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Frontend:</strong> Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Backend:</strong> Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Fluency:</strong> Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with <strong>agent frameworks</strong> (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Streaming &amp; Real-Time UI:</strong> Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Sense:</strong> Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambigous and the iteration is fast</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impact</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns\n\n - Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly\n\n - Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team\n\n - Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack\n\n - Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development\n\n - Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - Experience: 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features\n\n - Frontend: Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully\n\n - Backend: Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services\n\n - AI Fluency: Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production\n\n - Familiarity with agent frameworks (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows\n\n - Streaming & Real-Time UI: Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs\n\n - Product Sense: Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both\n\n - Collaboration: Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambigous and the iteration is fast\n\nBonus Qualifications\n\n - Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains\n\n - Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents\n\n - Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer\n\n - Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality\n\nImpact\n\nThis role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:\n\n - Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to\n\n - Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use\n\n - Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last\n\n - Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"760b5a7c-a532-44e4-9ee3-89a60669eaa2","title":"Senior AI Product Engineer 2, Control Remediation","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-30T00:39:13.310+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/760b5a7c-a532-44e4-9ee3-89a60669eaa2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/760b5a7c-a532-44e4-9ee3-89a60669eaa2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Frontend:</strong> Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Backend:</strong> Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Fluency:</strong> Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with <strong>agent frameworks</strong> (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Streaming &amp; Real-Time UI:</strong> Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Sense:</strong> Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambiguous and the iteration is fast</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impact</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is reimagining compliance as an intelligent, always-on experience — and AI is at the center of that vision. We are seeking a Senior AI Product Engineer to own the full-stack development of customer-facing AI features, embedded directly within our product teams. This is not a platform or infrastructure role. You'll translate the capabilities of LLMs, agents, and RAG pipelines into intuitive, polished product experiences — streaming chat interfaces, agentic workflows, intelligent summaries, and guided automation that makes compliance feel effortless. You'll partner closely with Platform Engineers, Product and Design but you are the engineer who owns the loop between AI capability and the customer experience.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Build AI-powered product features end-to-end — React/TypeScript UI through Node.js/Python backend — with real-time streaming, graceful degradation, and human-in-the-loop interaction patterns\n\n - Translate AI capabilities — RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, structured reasoning — into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Partner with AI Engineers to define API contracts and output schemas; translate RAG pipelines, agentic workflows, and structured reasoning into interactions that feel natural to compliance practitioners\n\n - Advocate for the user's perspective in technical decisions; surface where model outputs break down in practice and iterate the product layer accordingly\n\n - Build user-facing feedback loops that capture signal on AI output quality and make it actionable for the broader AI team\n\n - Instrument AI features with product-level observability — latency, engagement, task completion, drop-off — alongside integration and end-to-end tests that validate behavior across the full stack\n\n - Establish reusable patterns (streaming hooks, feedback components, AI state management) that accelerate future AI feature development\n\n - Mentor engineers newer to AI product development; participate in design reviews with both engineering depth and product instinct\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - Experience: 7+ years of software engineering experience with a proven track record of shipping full-stack features in production; 2+ years working on AI-powered product features\n\n - Frontend: Strong proficiency in React and TypeScript; experience building responsive, interactive UIs that handle async, streaming, and real-time data gracefully\n\n - Backend: Solid Python and Node.js and Typescript skills; experience designing and consuming APIs that integrate with LLM providers, orchestration frameworks, or AI services\n\n - AI Fluency: Hands-on experience building with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); practical understanding of prompt engineering, context management, RAG, Quality/Evals(Braintrust or others) and structured outputs — not just calling an endpoint, but knowing what makes a prompt reliable in production\n\n - Familiarity with agent frameworks (LangGraph, LangChain, custom runtimes) and how to build product surfaces on top of multi-step agentic workflows\n\n - Streaming & Real-Time UI: Experience implementing streaming response patterns (SSE, WebSockets, chunked HTTP) and building UIs that handle progressive, partial, and uncertain outputs\n\n - Product Sense: Strong intuition for user experience; you ask \"does this feel right to the user\" as often as \"does this work technically\" — and you're right about both\n\n - Collaboration: Track record of working closely with AI/ML engineers, product managers, and designers; comfortable operating in a cross-functional product team where the requirements are often ambiguous and the iteration is fast\n\nBonus Qualifications\n\n - Experience in compliance, security, GRC, or other document-heavy enterprise domains\n\n - Experience with MCP (Model Context Protocol) or similar tool-use interfaces for AI agents\n\n - Exposure to RAG system design — not as an owner, but as a consumer who has debugged retrieval quality issues from the product layer\n\n - Experience building feedback and annotation tooling that captures user signal on AI output quality\n\nImpact\n\nThis role is the bridge between Drata's AI ambitions and the customers who will benefit from them. Your work will:\n\n - Define the standard for how AI features look, feel, and behave across Drata's product — setting a bar that the entire product engineering organization will build to\n\n - Make compliance practitioners more capable and confident by turning AI intelligence into product interactions they actually trust and use\n\n - Accelerate the velocity of AI product development by establishing reusable patterns, components, and interfaces that make the next AI feature faster to ship than the last\n\n - Influence the roadmap through your proximity to both the customer experience and the AI capability layer — you'll see the gaps and the opportunities before almost anyone else\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $192,000 - $259,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0dd897fb-3279-4268-aab3-8fdb5fbe052a","title":"Principal Product Marketing Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-09T23:10:34.589+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0dd897fb-3279-4268-aab3-8fdb5fbe052a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0dd897fb-3279-4268-aab3-8fdb5fbe052a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is looking for a Principal Product Marketing Manager to own how our compliance portfolio comes to market — from strategy through the operational details that get every launch across the finish line. This is a senior, high-autonomy role with no direct reports and high impact. You'll set the positioning and narrative for compliance, run the launch machine behind it, and act as the connective tissue across Product, Marketing, Sales, CS, RevOps, and leadership. If you do your best work as the person who connects all the dots, builds structure where there isn't any, and moves fluidly between strategy and hands-on execution, this is the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a seasoned SaaS product marketer who operates with the judgment of a director without needing a team to drive outcomes — equally comfortable shaping the category narrative and owning the timeline, the readiness criteria, and the deck.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end GTM strategy and execution for compliance launches, framework expansions, and feature rollouts — from positioning and messaging through readiness, rollout, and adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run and continuously improve the NPI process for compliance: tiering and readiness criteria, launch governance, templates, task structures, and documentation that make launches faster, more consistent, and more predictable over time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the product marketing DRI across Product, Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and Enablement — driving alignment and execution through influence and quality of work, and building structure in ambiguous, fast-moving situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead compliance positioning and the category narrative, grounded in customer insight, market dynamics, and competitive intelligence, and translate advanced compliance and automation capabilities into differentiated business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the GTM communications cadence for compliance — recurring updates to ELT, GTM leadership, and the revenue org; crisp weekly updates across Slack, email, and decks tailored to each audience; and early surfacing of launch risks, dependencies, and decisions so leaders can act with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Produce the core internal and external launch assets — messaging, decks, one-pagers, launch briefs, enablement materials, and executive-ready content — and maintain high-quality, on-brand GTM slide repositories that stay accurate to the latest product scope.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish the measurement approach for launches, campaigns, and adoption, and use those insights to sharpen messaging, process, and execution quality over time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion AI-native workflows to accelerate research, content, testing, and execution without sacrificing rigor.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of product marketing experience, with significant time in SaaS — ideally in cybersecurity, GRC, security tooling, or adjacent enterprise platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of executing complex, multi-team product launches end to end, with measurable impact on adoption, pipeline, and revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong project-management instincts — able to manage multiple priorities, owners, and deadlines simultaneously and turn process into execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of enterprise and mid-market buyers across risk, security, compliance, and governance functions, and the ability to turn technical products into compelling, differentiated narratives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication, especially for executive audiences and cross-functional stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated cross-functional influence across Product, Sales, RevOps, Enablement, and Marketing leadership — without relying on formal authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating at both strategic and highly hands-on levels, and hands-on fluency with AI-enabled workflows (e.g., Claude, Notion AI, Jasper, or similar).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Major launches are better planned, better communicated, and better adopted across the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">GTM teams have clarity on what is launching, when, why it matters, and how to talk about it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leadership has consistent visibility into launch status, risks, and next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The NPI process is running smoothly, with fewer surprises and faster execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Core launch assets and communications are delivered with quality and speed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional teams rely on you as the person who helps make launches happen</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $171,000 -$264,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is looking for a Principal Product Marketing Manager to own how our compliance portfolio comes to market — from strategy through the operational details that get every launch across the finish line. This is a senior, high-autonomy role with no direct reports and high impact. You'll set the positioning and narrative for compliance, run the launch machine behind it, and act as the connective tissue across Product, Marketing, Sales, CS, RevOps, and leadership. If you do your best work as the person who connects all the dots, builds structure where there isn't any, and moves fluidly between strategy and hands-on execution, this is the role.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a seasoned SaaS product marketer who operates with the judgment of a director without needing a team to drive outcomes — equally comfortable shaping the category narrative and owning the timeline, the readiness criteria, and the deck.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Own end-to-end GTM strategy and execution for compliance launches, framework expansions, and feature rollouts — from positioning and messaging through readiness, rollout, and adoption.\n\n - Run and continuously improve the NPI process for compliance: tiering and readiness criteria, launch governance, templates, task structures, and documentation that make launches faster, more consistent, and more predictable over time.\n\n - Act as the product marketing DRI across Product, Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and Enablement — driving alignment and execution through influence and quality of work, and building structure in ambiguous, fast-moving situations.\n\n - Lead compliance positioning and the category narrative, grounded in customer insight, market dynamics, and competitive intelligence, and translate advanced compliance and automation capabilities into differentiated business value.\n\n - Own the GTM communications cadence for compliance — recurring updates to ELT, GTM leadership, and the revenue org; crisp weekly updates across Slack, email, and decks tailored to each audience; and early surfacing of launch risks, dependencies, and decisions so leaders can act with confidence.\n\n - Produce the core internal and external launch assets — messaging, decks, one-pagers, launch briefs, enablement materials, and executive-ready content — and maintain high-quality, on-brand GTM slide repositories that stay accurate to the latest product scope.\n\n - Establish the measurement approach for launches, campaigns, and adoption, and use those insights to sharpen messaging, process, and execution quality over time.\n\n - Champion AI-native workflows to accelerate research, content, testing, and execution without sacrificing rigor.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 10+ years of product marketing experience, with significant time in SaaS — ideally in cybersecurity, GRC, security tooling, or adjacent enterprise platforms.\n\n - A track record of executing complex, multi-team product launches end to end, with measurable impact on adoption, pipeline, and revenue.\n\n - Strong project-management instincts — able to manage multiple priorities, owners, and deadlines simultaneously and turn process into execution.\n\n - Deep understanding of enterprise and mid-market buyers across risk, security, compliance, and governance functions, and the ability to turn technical products into compelling, differentiated narratives.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication, especially for executive audiences and cross-functional stakeholders.\n\n - Demonstrated cross-functional influence across Product, Sales, RevOps, Enablement, and Marketing leadership — without relying on formal authority.\n\n - Comfort operating at both strategic and highly hands-on levels, and hands-on fluency with AI-enabled workflows (e.g., Claude, Notion AI, Jasper, or similar).\n\nWhat Success Looks Like\n\n - Major launches are better planned, better communicated, and better adopted across the business\n\n - GTM teams have clarity on what is launching, when, why it matters, and how to talk about it\n\n - Leadership has consistent visibility into launch status, risks, and next steps\n\n - The NPI process is running smoothly, with fewer surprises and faster execution\n\n - Core launch assets and communications are delivered with quality and speed\n\n - Cross-functional teams rely on you as the person who helps make launches happen\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $171,000 -$264,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7d505347-c5fb-4351-b57d-75a9ea654fcf","title":"Associate Technical Support Engineer - Mexico","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Mexico","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T22:46:16.614+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Mexico"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/7d505347-c5fb-4351-b57d-75a9ea654fcf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/7d505347-c5fb-4351-b57d-75a9ea654fcf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an <strong>Associate Technical Support Engineer</strong> at Drata, you will help build trust by supporting customers as AI transforms compliance, risk, and assurance. This role is ideal for problem-solvers growing beyond tickets—building skills across APIs, integrations, identity, cloud infrastructure, and AI workflows while making <strong>agentic experiences useful and trusted</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will partner with Engineering, Product, and Customer Success to investigate issues, <strong>turn signals into insight</strong>, and create knowledge that helps people and AI work smarter. This is an opportunity to <strong>raise the bar</strong>, shape the future of trust, and grow with Drata as we build <strong>responsible AI at the center of GRC</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Before applying, please review the schedule &amp; coverage requirements: </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role supports customers across multiple time zones and requires coverage across <strong>two Pacific Time (PT) shifts</strong>. Candidates should be prepared to work <strong>one of the following assigned shifts</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overnight shift:</strong> 12:00 a.m. – 8:00 a.m. PT</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Day shift:</strong> 8:00 a.m.– 5:00 p.m. PT</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional team coverage include:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in Mexico and requires working the local hours that correspond to the assigned Pacific Time coverage window.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in a <strong>rotating weekend coverage schedule</strong> as needed. Weekend coverage is shared across the team and is <strong>not required every weekend</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in <strong>holiday coverage</strong> as part of the team’s support operating model. Holiday coverage will be shared across the team on a rotating basis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the primary interface for incoming support inquiries, assisting with the triage and resolution of standard technical challenges throughout the Drata ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide comprehensive support for Tier 1 and designated Tier 2 complexities by utilizing established operational guides and escalation frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze and remedy concerns regarding platform functionality, various integrations, and fundamental automation sequences alongside senior engineering mentorship.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Route sophisticated technical hurdles to advanced engineers or internal partners, delivering detailed documentation, replication procedures, and pertinent background info.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage support interactions involving REST APIs, identity management tools (Okta/Google), cloud providers (AWS/GCP/Azure), and secure authentication processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain professional and empathetic dialogue with our customers, ensuring they receive consistent status reports and transparent expectation management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage internal platforms like Intercom and Jira to oversee ticket lifecycles and preserve meticulous administrative records.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop content for the knowledge base, contributing to external help articles and internal procedural manuals to improve self-service resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform technical validation and testing to replicate bugs reported by users, aiding in quality assurance efforts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify emerging support patterns or recurring friction points and communicate these strategic insights to the internal team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate across Product and Engineering departments to continuously refine your technical expertise and elevate the overall user journey.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2+ years of experience</strong> in customer support, technical support, system administration, or other customer-facing technical roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Educational background</strong> in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related discipline is required (BA/BS/MS), or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Basic foundation in databases</strong>, including hands-on experience with database queries, management, and operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with web applications, APIs, and general software troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP), identity providers (Okta, Google Workspace), or SaaS tools is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using ticketing and support platforms like Intercom, Jira, or similar systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with scripting or automation tools (e.g., Python, Bash).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with REST APIs or developer tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic command line knowledge (e.g., Linux/Unix navigation).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Awareness of compliance, security, or audit-readiness concepts in a B2B SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to follow structured troubleshooting procedures and escalate issues appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear verbal and written communication skills, with a focus on delivering customer-first solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity, a strong sense of ownership, and a desire to grow in a technical environment<strong>.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, employees <em>and their dependents</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between MX$467,500–MX$577,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs an Associate Technical Support Engineer at Drata, you will help build trust by supporting customers as AI transforms compliance, risk, and assurance. This role is ideal for problem-solvers growing beyond tickets—building skills across APIs, integrations, identity, cloud infrastructure, and AI workflows while making agentic experiences useful and trusted.\n\nYou will partner with Engineering, Product, and Customer Success to investigate issues, turn signals into insight, and create knowledge that helps people and AI work smarter. This is an opportunity to raise the bar, shape the future of trust, and grow with Drata as we build responsible AI at the center of GRC.\n\n\n\nBefore applying, please review the schedule & coverage requirements: \n\nThis role supports customers across multiple time zones and requires coverage across two Pacific Time (PT) shifts. Candidates should be prepared to work one of the following assigned shifts:\n\n - Overnight shift: 12:00 a.m. – 8:00 a.m. PT\n\n - Day shift: 8:00 a.m.– 5:00 p.m. PT\n\nAdditional team coverage include:\n\n - This role is based in Mexico and requires working the local hours that correspond to the assigned Pacific Time coverage window.\n\n - Participate in a rotating weekend coverage schedule as needed. Weekend coverage is shared across the team and is not required every weekend.\n\n - Participate in holiday coverage as part of the team’s support operating model. Holiday coverage will be shared across the team on a rotating basis.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Act as the primary interface for incoming support inquiries, assisting with the triage and resolution of standard technical challenges throughout the Drata ecosystem.\n\n - Provide comprehensive support for Tier 1 and designated Tier 2 complexities by utilizing established operational guides and escalation frameworks.\n\n - Analyze and remedy concerns regarding platform functionality, various integrations, and fundamental automation sequences alongside senior engineering mentorship.\n\n - Route sophisticated technical hurdles to advanced engineers or internal partners, delivering detailed documentation, replication procedures, and pertinent background info.\n\n - Manage support interactions involving REST APIs, identity management tools (Okta/Google), cloud providers (AWS/GCP/Azure), and secure authentication processes.\n\n - Maintain professional and empathetic dialogue with our customers, ensuring they receive consistent status reports and transparent expectation management.\n\n - Leverage internal platforms like Intercom and Jira to oversee ticket lifecycles and preserve meticulous administrative records.\n\n - Develop content for the knowledge base, contributing to external help articles and internal procedural manuals to improve self-service resources.\n\n - Perform technical validation and testing to replicate bugs reported by users, aiding in quality assurance efforts.\n\n - Identify emerging support patterns or recurring friction points and communicate these strategic insights to the internal team.\n\n - Collaborate across Product and Engineering departments to continuously refine your technical expertise and elevate the overall user journey.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 2+ years of experience in customer support, technical support, system administration, or other customer-facing technical roles.\n\n - Educational background in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related discipline is required (BA/BS/MS), or equivalent practical experience.\n\n - Basic foundation in databases, including hands-on experience with database queries, management, and operations.\n\n - Familiarity with web applications, APIs, and general software troubleshooting.\n\n - Exposure to cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP), identity providers (Okta, Google Workspace), or SaaS tools is a plus.\n\n - Comfortable using ticketing and support platforms like Intercom, Jira, or similar systems.\n\n - Familiarity with scripting or automation tools (e.g., Python, Bash).\n\n - Experience working with REST APIs or developer tools.\n\n - Basic command line knowledge (e.g., Linux/Unix navigation).\n\n - Awareness of compliance, security, or audit-readiness concepts in a B2B SaaS environment.\n\n - Ability to follow structured troubleshooting procedures and escalate issues appropriately.\n\n - Clear verbal and written communication skills, with a focus on delivering customer-first solutions.\n\n - Curiosity, a strong sense of ownership, and a desire to grow in a technical environment.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, employees and their dependents\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. \n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between MX$467,500–MX$577,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b4fac986-dfce-4805-9102-f00706f7b53c","title":"Manager, Technical Support - Mexico","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - Mexico","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-24T23:09:58.889+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Mexico"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/b4fac986-dfce-4805-9102-f00706f7b53c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/b4fac986-dfce-4805-9102-f00706f7b53c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Technical Support Manager at Drata, you will lead a team responsible for delivering high-quality technical support to our customers across a growing and increasingly complex platform. You’ll oversee day-to-day support operations, coach and develop technical support talent, and drive continuous improvement across processes, escalations, tooling, and customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for a hands-on people leader who combines strong operational judgment with technical depth and a customer-first mindset. You’ll partner closely with Engineering, Product, Customer Success, and other cross-functional teams to ensure timely resolution of customer issues, scalable support practices, and strong alignment between customer needs and internal execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Drata, Technical Support plays a critical role in helping customers maintain trust, stay audit-ready, and confidently use our platform across integrations, automations, and compliance workflows. Our Technical Support team supports issues involving APIs, cloud infrastructure, identity systems, and evidence collection workflows, and collaborates closely with Engineering and Product to resolve bugs and improve supportability.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a team of Technical Support Engineers and/or Specialists, providing clear performance expectations, regular feedback, and career development support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage day-to-day support operations, including queue health, case quality, escalation handling, staffing coverage, and SLA adherence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a point of leadership escalation for high-priority customer issues, helping the team drive timely resolution and clear communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong partnerships with Engineering, Product, Customer Success, and other internal stakeholders to improve issue resolution, bug escalation, and customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and refine support processes, workflows, runbooks, and escalation paths that improve consistency, efficiency, and customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use support metrics and qualitative insights to identify trends, remove friction, and drive operational improvements across the support organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure the team is equipped to troubleshoot issues involving integrations, APIs, SSO/SCIM, cloud providers, and platform workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with leadership on hiring, onboarding, workforce planning, and organizational design as the team scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review customer escalations, incident patterns, and support feedback to surface product gaps, tooling needs, and enablement opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a culture of accountability, empathy, technical excellence, and continuous improvement.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in technical support, support engineering, solutions engineering, or a similar customer-facing technical function in a SaaS or B2B technology environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of people management experience leading technical support or customer-facing technical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience managing escalations, balancing customer urgency with operational rigor, and driving cross-functional resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of APIs, SaaS integrations, authentication protocols, identity systems, and cloud environments such as AWS, Azure, and GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to improve support operations through process design, metrics, documentation, training, and tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with customers, executives, and cross-functional partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success coaching team members, raising technical quality, and building a healthy, high-performing team culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A customer-obsessed, highly organized, and data-informed approach to problem solving and decision making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with evolving priorities and the opportunity to build.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting security, compliance, or GRC products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with frameworks such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, or similar regulatory environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with support platforms and internal tools such as Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, Slack, and knowledge base systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background building or scaling global support coverage models, technical escalation programs, or support enablement initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, employees <em>and their dependents</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between MX$850,000 - MX$1,150,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs a Technical Support Manager at Drata, you will lead a team responsible for delivering high-quality technical support to our customers across a growing and increasingly complex platform. You’ll oversee day-to-day support operations, coach and develop technical support talent, and drive continuous improvement across processes, escalations, tooling, and customer experience.\n\nThis role is ideal for a hands-on people leader who combines strong operational judgment with technical depth and a customer-first mindset. You’ll partner closely with Engineering, Product, Customer Success, and other cross-functional teams to ensure timely resolution of customer issues, scalable support practices, and strong alignment between customer needs and internal execution.\n\nAt Drata, Technical Support plays a critical role in helping customers maintain trust, stay audit-ready, and confidently use our platform across integrations, automations, and compliance workflows. Our Technical Support team supports issues involving APIs, cloud infrastructure, identity systems, and evidence collection workflows, and collaborates closely with Engineering and Product to resolve bugs and improve supportability.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a team of Technical Support Engineers and/or Specialists, providing clear performance expectations, regular feedback, and career development support.\n\n - Manage day-to-day support operations, including queue health, case quality, escalation handling, staffing coverage, and SLA adherence.\n\n - Serve as a point of leadership escalation for high-priority customer issues, helping the team drive timely resolution and clear communication.\n\n - Build strong partnerships with Engineering, Product, Customer Success, and other internal stakeholders to improve issue resolution, bug escalation, and customer outcomes.\n\n - Establish and refine support processes, workflows, runbooks, and escalation paths that improve consistency, efficiency, and customer experience.\n\n - Use support metrics and qualitative insights to identify trends, remove friction, and drive operational improvements across the support organization.\n\n - Ensure the team is equipped to troubleshoot issues involving integrations, APIs, SSO/SCIM, cloud providers, and platform workflows.\n\n - Partner with leadership on hiring, onboarding, workforce planning, and organizational design as the team scales.\n\n - Review customer escalations, incident patterns, and support feedback to surface product gaps, tooling needs, and enablement opportunities.\n\n - Foster a culture of accountability, empathy, technical excellence, and continuous improvement.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 5+ years of experience in technical support, support engineering, solutions engineering, or a similar customer-facing technical function in a SaaS or B2B technology environment.\n\n - 2+ years of people management experience leading technical support or customer-facing technical teams.\n\n - Strong experience managing escalations, balancing customer urgency with operational rigor, and driving cross-functional resolution.\n\n - Working knowledge of APIs, SaaS integrations, authentication protocols, identity systems, and cloud environments such as AWS, Azure, and GCP.\n\n - Proven ability to improve support operations through process design, metrics, documentation, training, and tooling.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with customers, executives, and cross-functional partners.\n\n - Demonstrated success coaching team members, raising technical quality, and building a healthy, high-performing team culture.\n\n - A customer-obsessed, highly organized, and data-informed approach to problem solving and decision making.\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with evolving priorities and the opportunity to build.\n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience supporting security, compliance, or GRC products.\n\n - Familiarity with frameworks such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, or similar regulatory environments.\n\n - Experience with support platforms and internal tools such as Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, Slack, and knowledge base systems.\n\n - Background building or scaling global support coverage models, technical escalation programs, or support enablement initiatives.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, employees and their dependents\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. \n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between MX$850,000 - MX$1,150,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b06ab8ed-0173-4e04-b76e-7ff7f1ef0eef","title":"Senior Manager, Enterprise Sales - West","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-08T22:19:14.547+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/b06ab8ed-0173-4e04-b76e-7ff7f1ef0eef","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/b06ab8ed-0173-4e04-b76e-7ff7f1ef0eef/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a highly strategic, results-oriented <strong>Senior Manager, Enterprise Sales</strong> with a strong track record of building high-performing teams, driving account-based execution, and instilling disciplined, multi-threaded deal strategy. This leader will manage a team of Account Executives while operating as a senior-level force multiplier—shaping strategy, influencing cross-functional alignment, and proactively owning initiatives that accelerate segment performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional candidates are proactive operators who elevate standards, solve ambiguous problems, and demonstrate the ability to scale both people and processes. If you're motivated by driving meaningful impact, owning outcomes, and playing a critical leadership role in a high-growth environment, this role is for you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><h3><strong>Drive High-Performance Sales Execution</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieve and consistently exceed sales targets through exceptional team leadership and selective individual contributions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a culture of account-based execution excellence, ensuring multi-threading rigor, clear activity expectations, and consistent accountability across the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement and maintain high-quality forecasting discipline, ensuring predictability and transparency into pipeline health and revenue expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive improvements in ACVs, win rates, sales cycle efficiency, and ramp time through coaching, enablement alignment, and process discipline.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Own Strategic Initiatives Across the Business</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively identify, define, and drive strategic initiatives that improve productivity, sales execution, segment performance, or how the org scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a key partner to Marketing, Product, RevOps, Enablement, and Solutions Engineering, ensuring tight alignment on GTM motions and surfacing customer and market insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence product roadmap, messaging, and market strategy by contributing meaningful, pattern-based feedback from the field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a cross-functional liaison to prioritize initiatives that impact win rates, deal velocity, and the enterprise customer decision process.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Lead with a Senior-Level Mindset</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operate as a thought leader within the Enterprise program, shaping how the segment scales and proactively identifying risks and opportunities before they surface.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Step up—without being asked—to solve ambiguous problems, bring clarity to the team, and deliver high-impact work that moves the business forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate executive presence in internal forums, customer and prospect conversations, and leadership discussions—representing the Enterprise segment credibly at the highest levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring forward actionable market and account-level observations, and recommend clear next steps that help the business scale responsibly and efficiently.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Coach, Develop, and Performance Manage</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set clear expectations for account-based execution, multi-threading, deal hygiene, and enterprise sales fundamentals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold the team accountable to activity, impact, and results, driving a culture of ownership and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement structured, data-informed performance management to elevate or exit reps based on consistent trends, not lagging indicators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor AEs to become exceptional operators—improving qualification rigor, account and territory planning, and executive engagement strategy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years leading quota-carrying enterprise/strategic sales teams, ideally in a high-growth B2B SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years in quota-carrying sales roles, with a track record of consistently exceeding targets in complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise deals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success building and scaling enterprise sales motions — including account planning, territory design, and multi-threaded engagement strategies with large organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coaching reps on navigating long, complex sales cycles: multi-stakeholder buying committees, procurement, legal, and executive-level negotiations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and strategic skill set, with experience in forecasting accuracy, account segmentation, and identifying levers to improve win rates and deal velocity at the enterprise level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to influence cross-functional partners (Marketing, Customer Success, Solutions Engineering, Legal) and drive alignment on enterprise go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High executive presence with the ability to engage and build trust with C-suite and senior buyer personas, both directly and in support of the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills and the ability to lead teams through organizational change, market shifts, or evolving go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of strong performance management, mentorship, and developing sellers capable of running strategic, high-value deal cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate independently, think strategically about account and territory strategy, and contribute to broader go-to-market planning as the business scales.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between $280,000 - $315,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are seeking a highly strategic, results-oriented Senior Manager, Enterprise Sales with a strong track record of building high-performing teams, driving account-based execution, and instilling disciplined, multi-threaded deal strategy. This leader will manage a team of Account Executives while operating as a senior-level force multiplier—shaping strategy, influencing cross-functional alignment, and proactively owning initiatives that accelerate segment performance.\n\nExceptional candidates are proactive operators who elevate standards, solve ambiguous problems, and demonstrate the ability to scale both people and processes. If you're motivated by driving meaningful impact, owning outcomes, and playing a critical leadership role in a high-growth environment, this role is for you.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n\nDRIVE HIGH-PERFORMANCE SALES EXECUTION\n\n - Achieve and consistently exceed sales targets through exceptional team leadership and selective individual contributions.\n\n - Build a culture of account-based execution excellence, ensuring multi-threading rigor, clear activity expectations, and consistent accountability across the team.\n\n - Implement and maintain high-quality forecasting discipline, ensuring predictability and transparency into pipeline health and revenue expectations.\n\n - Drive improvements in ACVs, win rates, sales cycle efficiency, and ramp time through coaching, enablement alignment, and process discipline.\n\n\nOWN STRATEGIC INITIATIVES ACROSS THE BUSINESS\n\n - Proactively identify, define, and drive strategic initiatives that improve productivity, sales execution, segment performance, or how the org scales.\n\n - Serve as a key partner to Marketing, Product, RevOps, Enablement, and Solutions Engineering, ensuring tight alignment on GTM motions and surfacing customer and market insights.\n\n - Influence product roadmap, messaging, and market strategy by contributing meaningful, pattern-based feedback from the field.\n\n - Act as a cross-functional liaison to prioritize initiatives that impact win rates, deal velocity, and the enterprise customer decision process.\n\n\nLEAD WITH A SENIOR-LEVEL MINDSET\n\n - Operate as a thought leader within the Enterprise program, shaping how the segment scales and proactively identifying risks and opportunities before they surface.\n\n - Step up—without being asked—to solve ambiguous problems, bring clarity to the team, and deliver high-impact work that moves the business forward.\n\n - Demonstrate executive presence in internal forums, customer and prospect conversations, and leadership discussions—representing the Enterprise segment credibly at the highest levels.\n\n - Bring forward actionable market and account-level observations, and recommend clear next steps that help the business scale responsibly and efficiently.\n\n\nCOACH, DEVELOP, AND PERFORMANCE MANAGE\n\n - Set clear expectations for account-based execution, multi-threading, deal hygiene, and enterprise sales fundamentals.\n\n - Hold the team accountable to activity, impact, and results, driving a culture of ownership and continuous improvement.\n\n - Implement structured, data-informed performance management to elevate or exit reps based on consistent trends, not lagging indicators.\n\n - Mentor AEs to become exceptional operators—improving qualification rigor, account and territory planning, and executive engagement strategy.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 5+ years leading quota-carrying enterprise/strategic sales teams, ideally in a high-growth B2B SaaS environment.\n\n - 10+ years in quota-carrying sales roles, with a track record of consistently exceeding targets in complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise deals.\n\n - Demonstrated success building and scaling enterprise sales motions — including account planning, territory design, and multi-threaded engagement strategies with large organizations.\n\n - Experience coaching reps on navigating long, complex sales cycles: multi-stakeholder buying committees, procurement, legal, and executive-level negotiations.\n\n - Strong analytical and strategic skill set, with experience in forecasting accuracy, account segmentation, and identifying levers to improve win rates and deal velocity at the enterprise level.\n\n - Proven ability to influence cross-functional partners (Marketing, Customer Success, Solutions Engineering, Legal) and drive alignment on enterprise go-to-market strategy.\n\n - High executive presence with the ability to engage and build trust with C-suite and senior buyer personas, both directly and in support of the team.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills and the ability to lead teams through organizational change, market shifts, or evolving go-to-market strategy.\n\n - A track record of strong performance management, mentorship, and developing sellers capable of running strategic, high-value deal cycles.\n\n - Ability to operate independently, think strategically about account and territory strategy, and contribute to broader go-to-market planning as the business scales.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between $280,000 - $315,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1f9f0aff-d60f-4e0d-8d6f-333551826251","title":"Senior Director, Demand Generation","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-08T19:16:06.500+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/1f9f0aff-d60f-4e0d-8d6f-333551826251","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/1f9f0aff-d60f-4e0d-8d6f-333551826251/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a Senior Director of Demand Generation to lead the strategy, execution, and performance of our demand engine. This role owns pipeline creation across digital, integrated campaigns and account based programs and is responsible for building a high-performing demand generation system that supports global pipeline generation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will be a hands-on leader who actively builds, executes, and optimizes programs across the funnel while advancing how we leverage AI as an integrated system to improve targeting, engagement, and conversion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">End-to-end demand generation strategy across digital, integrated campaigns, and scalable multi-channel programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pipeline creation and acceleration aligned to revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Campaign planning and execution across personas, segments, and buying stages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Budget allocation, channel mix optimization, and performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Funnel performance improvements across volume, conversion rates, and pipeline velocity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Alignment with Sales, SDR, RevOps, and Partner teams to ensure pipeline quality and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribution to global pipegen efforts across regions, segments, and go-to-market priorities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Core Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and execute AI systems for multi-channel demand programs that drive measurable pipeline and revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own digital channel performance and campaign orchestration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead testing and optimization strategies across creative, targeting, landing pages, and conversion paths.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with content and product marketing to develop high-performing messaging and offers for integrated campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish clear reporting on pipeline contribution, ROI, and channel performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and develop a high-performing demand generation team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI as a Demand Generation System</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advance our use of AI as a connected system within demand generation, moving beyond individual use cases to more integrated, scalable workflows and agents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and optimize AI-driven processes across campaign execution, personalization, lead management, and sales handoff.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with RevOps and Marketing Ops to deepen AI integration into core GTM systems such as scoring, routing, enrichment, and forecasting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to increase efficiency, testing velocity, and conversion through AI-enabled workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure AI systems are measurable, repeatable, and tied to pipeline performance and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute hands-on to evolving how AI is applied across the demand generation function.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8–12+ years in B2B SaaS demand generation or growth marketing, with leadership experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success driving pipeline through digital, integrated, and multi-channel programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of funnel dynamics, conversion optimization, and performance analytics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing budgets and optimizing for ROI across multiple programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience partnering with Sales and RevOps in a pipeline-driven organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI &amp; Technical Experience</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with AI-driven marketing workflows, systems, or automations in a production environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think in systems, including inputs, workflows, outputs, and feedback loops.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CRM, marketing automation, and data systems such as Salesforce, HubSpot.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort evaluating and operationalizing new approaches that improve performance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leadership Profile</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic and execution-oriented, with a strong operator mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-driven and focused on measurable business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder mentality with a focus on scalability and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional collaborator and communicator.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating in an environment that is continuously evolving and improving.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $180,000 - $276,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are seeking a Senior Director of Demand Generation to lead the strategy, execution, and performance of our demand engine. This role owns pipeline creation across digital, integrated campaigns and account based programs and is responsible for building a high-performing demand generation system that supports global pipeline generation.\n\nYou will be a hands-on leader who actively builds, executes, and optimizes programs across the funnel while advancing how we leverage AI as an integrated system to improve targeting, engagement, and conversion.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - End-to-end demand generation strategy across digital, integrated campaigns, and scalable multi-channel programs.\n\n - Pipeline creation and acceleration aligned to revenue targets.\n\n - Campaign planning and execution across personas, segments, and buying stages.\n\n - Budget allocation, channel mix optimization, and performance management.\n\n - Funnel performance improvements across volume, conversion rates, and pipeline velocity.\n\n - Alignment with Sales, SDR, RevOps, and Partner teams to ensure pipeline quality and follow-up.\n\n - Contribution to global pipegen efforts across regions, segments, and go-to-market priorities.\n\nCore Responsibilities\n\n - Build and execute AI systems for multi-channel demand programs that drive measurable pipeline and revenue.\n\n - Own digital channel performance and campaign orchestration.\n\n - Lead testing and optimization strategies across creative, targeting, landing pages, and conversion paths.\n\n - Partner with content and product marketing to develop high-performing messaging and offers for integrated campaigns.\n\n - Establish clear reporting on pipeline contribution, ROI, and channel performance.\n\n - Manage and develop a high-performing demand generation team.\n\nAI as a Demand Generation System\n\n - Advance our use of AI as a connected system within demand generation, moving beyond individual use cases to more integrated, scalable workflows and agents.\n\n - Build and optimize AI-driven processes across campaign execution, personalization, lead management, and sales handoff.\n\n - Partner with RevOps and Marketing Ops to deepen AI integration into core GTM systems such as scoring, routing, enrichment, and forecasting.\n\n - Identify opportunities to increase efficiency, testing velocity, and conversion through AI-enabled workflows.\n\n - Ensure AI systems are measurable, repeatable, and tied to pipeline performance and business outcomes.\n\n - Contribute hands-on to evolving how AI is applied across the demand generation function.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 8–12+ years in B2B SaaS demand generation or growth marketing, with leadership experience.\n\n - Proven success driving pipeline through digital, integrated, and multi-channel programs.\n\n - Strong understanding of funnel dynamics, conversion optimization, and performance analytics.\n\n - Experience managing budgets and optimizing for ROI across multiple programs.\n\n - Deep experience partnering with Sales and RevOps in a pipeline-driven organization.\n\nAI & Technical Experience\n\n - Experience working with AI-driven marketing workflows, systems, or automations in a production environment.\n\n - Ability to think in systems, including inputs, workflows, outputs, and feedback loops.\n\n - Familiarity with CRM, marketing automation, and data systems such as Salesforce, HubSpot.\n\n - Comfort evaluating and operationalizing new approaches that improve performance.\n\nLeadership Profile\n\n - Strategic and execution-oriented, with a strong operator mindset.\n\n - Data-driven and focused on measurable business outcomes.\n\n - Builder mentality with a focus on scalability and efficiency.\n\n - Strong cross-functional collaborator and communicator.\n\n - Comfortable operating in an environment that is continuously evolving and improving.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $180,000 - $276,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cfce09b0-36e4-4849-b7be-1dd81f4ee83c","title":"Enterprise Account Executive - Southeast","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T17:46:43.574+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/cfce09b0-36e4-4849-b7be-1dd81f4ee83c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/cfce09b0-36e4-4849-b7be-1dd81f4ee83c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a passionate sales professional with 7+ years of experience in a customer facing role selling SaaS or consulting with an ability to focus on the Enterprise space - not necessarily in the security and compliance space. Exceptional candidates are hungry to work in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment, and have a proven track record of success in their past roles and experiences! <strong>We are seeking candidates who reside in Georgia or Florida to cover this Southeast Territory. </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsible for bringing new partners on board and consistently growing revenue by exceeding revenue targets/quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify prospects based on their mission alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute strategies for driving partnerships and revenue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and manage your pipeline of prospects; become an expert on a region and understanding the complexities of that specific market</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consult senior executives to discover their needs and educate them through an accelerated buying process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve our product offering based on deep understanding of the needs of our partners</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in a customer-facing B2B SaaS Sales role, with at least 2 years in a closing new business capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to focus on bringing in Enterprise accounts with 1K+ full time employees</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred background in the start-up space</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-starter who brings ideas to life and takes pride in results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resourceful, finding ways to get things done regardless of the obstacles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mission-Driven and focused on using talents to make the world a better place</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and detail-oriented with an ability to handle a variety of different projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A talented communicator and a “people person” who enjoys working with others. You are thoughtful about the ways you communicate and the impact that may have on a customer. You have the ability to sense when a conversation is progressing in a positive or negative way and have the confidence to address concerns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident but always striving to do better. You are not afraid to ask for help. You value honest, action-oriented feedback and believe it is a tool to improve as a team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between  $270,000 - $315,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for a passionate sales professional with 7+ years of experience in a customer facing role selling SaaS or consulting with an ability to focus on the Enterprise space - not necessarily in the security and compliance space. Exceptional candidates are hungry to work in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment, and have a proven track record of success in their past roles and experiences! We are seeking candidates who reside in Georgia or Florida to cover this Southeast Territory. \n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Responsible for bringing new partners on board and consistently growing revenue by exceeding revenue targets/quota\n\n - Identify prospects based on their mission alignment\n\n - Develop and execute strategies for driving partnerships and revenue\n\n - Build and manage your pipeline of prospects; become an expert on a region and understanding the complexities of that specific market\n\n - Consult senior executives to discover their needs and educate them through an accelerated buying process\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve our product offering based on deep understanding of the needs of our partners\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 7+ years of experience in a customer-facing B2B SaaS Sales role, with at least 2 years in a closing new business capacity\n\n - Ability to focus on bringing in Enterprise accounts with 1K+ full time employees\n\n - Preferred background in the start-up space\n\n - Self-starter who brings ideas to life and takes pride in results\n\n - Resourceful, finding ways to get things done regardless of the obstacles\n\n - Mission-Driven and focused on using talents to make the world a better place\n\n - Organized and detail-oriented with an ability to handle a variety of different projects\n\n - A talented communicator and a “people person” who enjoys working with others. You are thoughtful about the ways you communicate and the impact that may have on a customer. You have the ability to sense when a conversation is progressing in a positive or negative way and have the confidence to address concerns.\n\n - Confident but always striving to do better. You are not afraid to ask for help. You value honest, action-oriented feedback and believe it is a tool to improve as a team.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between  $270,000 - $315,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"84019da9-a394-4dec-a7e7-bbf0bb941b30","title":"Sales Development Representative - EMEA","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T13:46:35.887+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/84019da9-a394-4dec-a7e7-bbf0bb941b30","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/84019da9-a394-4dec-a7e7-bbf0bb941b30/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for rockstar SDR's to join an unmatched team! Drata is the fastest growing, B2B SaaS startups <em>ever</em> to achieve unicorn status and currently taking over the security and compliance automation space. As a member of the Drata SDR team, you will be a critical component to an innovative fast-paced Sales Team. You will drive outbound prospecting campaigns (email, phone calls, &amp; social media) to identify potential customers that would benefit from Drata’s solution. You will often be the first point of contact with potential customers with the objective to set qualified meetings for a team of Account Executives. This is an exciting opportunity for SDR's to be a part of an inclusive team, and experience tremendous career growth.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This position is a Hybrid role with two days per week in office and candidates must reside in the London Metro area. We are ideally targeting candidates who are professionally proficient/fluent in both English and German at this time. </strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research accounts, identify key players and generate interest through cold discovery calls, and email campaigns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Methodically qualify, build, and manage an accurate sales pipeline; maintain a high volume of activity including outbound cold calls, emails, &amp; social selling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discovering new leads through internet research and social media monitoring/messaging, using tools such as LinkedIn Navigator, Twitter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responding to inbound customer interest and developing these accounts to create opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize your active listening skills to understand and uncover customer needs and business problems to effectively communicate how Drata can solve them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Achieving, and exceeding, weekly/monthly metrics (meetings, qualified opportunities, new contacts, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsible for accurately tracking customer interactions and information in our CRM, Salesforce</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct high-level conversations with C-Suite executives in prospect accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thrive on change while remaining highly organized, optimistic, and coachable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This position is a Hybrid role with two days per week in office and candidates must reside in the London Metro area.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Proven Track Record: 6+ months of experience in a sales development associate or inside sales role; sales experience in the SaaS space is a plus. We are looking for candidates who thrive in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial business environment and who have a proven track record of success in their past roles and experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional proficient/Fluent in German and English.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Intensely Curious: You thrive on learning new concepts, technologies, personas, and can rapidly absorb and integrate that material into your day to day role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Doer: You are driven, self-motivated and a self-starter who brings your ideas to life and takes pride in results. You are resourceful and find ways to get things done regardless of the obstacles. You are not fearful of failure and realize that failure is often a step closer to figuring out what works. Taking on complex challenges excites you, even if you need to ask for help or spend some time figuring out where to begin.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized: You are detail-oriented and can juggle having a variety of different projects on your plate at one time because you are good at keeping track of them. You can create structure for yourself to be the most successful.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A Talented Communicator: You are a “people person” who enjoys communicating with people and has a strong awareness of those around you. You are thoughtful about the ways you communicate and the impression that may have on a client.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mission-Driven: You want to use your talents to make the world a better place and you are in a rush to do it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident but Self-Critical: You are confident in your skills and the quality of your work product. At the same time, you are not afraid to ask for help and want to constantly be improving. You value honest, action-oriented feedback and believe that we can use it as a tool to improve as a team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, employees <em>and their dependents</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between £56,000 – £59,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for rockstar SDR's to join an unmatched team! Drata is the fastest growing, B2B SaaS startups ever to achieve unicorn status and currently taking over the security and compliance automation space. As a member of the Drata SDR team, you will be a critical component to an innovative fast-paced Sales Team. You will drive outbound prospecting campaigns (email, phone calls, & social media) to identify potential customers that would benefit from Drata’s solution. You will often be the first point of contact with potential customers with the objective to set qualified meetings for a team of Account Executives. This is an exciting opportunity for SDR's to be a part of an inclusive team, and experience tremendous career growth.\n\nThis position is a Hybrid role with two days per week in office and candidates must reside in the London Metro area. We are ideally targeting candidates who are professionally proficient/fluent in both English and German at this time. \n\n \n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Research accounts, identify key players and generate interest through cold discovery calls, and email campaigns\n\n - Methodically qualify, build, and manage an accurate sales pipeline; maintain a high volume of activity including outbound cold calls, emails, & social selling\n\n - Discovering new leads through internet research and social media monitoring/messaging, using tools such as LinkedIn Navigator, Twitter\n\n - Responding to inbound customer interest and developing these accounts to create opportunities\n\n - Utilize your active listening skills to understand and uncover customer needs and business problems to effectively communicate how Drata can solve them\n\n - Achieving, and exceeding, weekly/monthly metrics (meetings, qualified opportunities, new contacts, etc.)\n\n - Responsible for accurately tracking customer interactions and information in our CRM, Salesforce\n\n - Conduct high-level conversations with C-Suite executives in prospect accounts\n\n - Thrive on change while remaining highly organized, optimistic, and coachable\n\n - This position is a Hybrid role with two days per week in office and candidates must reside in the London Metro area.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - A Proven Track Record: 6+ months of experience in a sales development associate or inside sales role; sales experience in the SaaS space is a plus. We are looking for candidates who thrive in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial business environment and who have a proven track record of success in their past roles and experiences.\n\n - Professional proficient/Fluent in German and English.\n\n - Intensely Curious: You thrive on learning new concepts, technologies, personas, and can rapidly absorb and integrate that material into your day to day role\n\n - A Doer: You are driven, self-motivated and a self-starter who brings your ideas to life and takes pride in results. You are resourceful and find ways to get things done regardless of the obstacles. You are not fearful of failure and realize that failure is often a step closer to figuring out what works. Taking on complex challenges excites you, even if you need to ask for help or spend some time figuring out where to begin.\n\n - Organized: You are detail-oriented and can juggle having a variety of different projects on your plate at one time because you are good at keeping track of them. You can create structure for yourself to be the most successful.\n\n - A Talented Communicator: You are a “people person” who enjoys communicating with people and has a strong awareness of those around you. You are thoughtful about the ways you communicate and the impression that may have on a client.\n\n - Mission-Driven: You want to use your talents to make the world a better place and you are in a rush to do it.\n\n - Confident but Self-Critical: You are confident in your skills and the quality of your work product. At the same time, you are not afraid to ask for help and want to constantly be improving. You value honest, action-oriented feedback and believe that we can use it as a tool to improve as a team.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, employees and their dependents\n\n - Financial Well-being: To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between £56,000 – £59,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"80438271-faab-484a-8452-e5a35fbbbecb","title":"Field CISO","department":"Security","team":"Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-23T22:36:32.285+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/80438271-faab-484a-8452-e5a35fbbbecb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/80438271-faab-484a-8452-e5a35fbbbecb/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Drata scales, we want our security and GRC leadership to be able to meet our customers’ needs in more places at once—in strategic customer conversations, on stage at industry events, and in the broader conversations happening across our security and GRC communities. We’re looking for a Field Chief Information Security Officer to join Drata’s Security &amp; GRC organization, reporting directly to our SVP, Security &amp; CISO, to help carry our vision to a wider audience. Your primary mission: be Drata's credible, practitioner-level security and GRC voice in the field.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a senior, remote, U.S.-based security and GRC leadership role, ideally based on the East Coast to cover both the Americas and EMEA regions. As one of the most senior individual contributor roles in Drata's Security &amp; Trust organization, this role shapes how Drata responds to the industry, informs the product experience, and aids in the strategic positioning of Drata’s future to acutely meet industry needs. This position is built for someone who has led security and GRC programs before and is excited to bring that experience directly to our customers, prospects, and industry peers. You’ll work closely with our go-to-market, customer success, and marketing teams, but your foundations are still rooted in technical security and GRC leadership—that is what will make you credible in the room among peers and is critical to the success of this role. Given the nature of our platform, this person will spend as much time in GRC conversations as in traditional security conversations due the complementary nature and inseparability of these functions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with our amazing Sales, Customer Success, and Marketing teams on our most strategic enterprise and F500/G2000 opportunities—bringing tried-and-true security and GRC expertise into the conversation when customers need it most.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead executive briefings and CISO-to-CISO conversations that build trust and help prospective customers feel confident in their decision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent Drata at industry conferences, CISO dinners, and regional roundtables across the Americas, EMEA, and APAC regions, building genuine relationships across the security and GRC community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share what you’re hearing in the field through webinars, panels, bylines, and press opportunities that build Drata’s voice and credibility in the security and GRC market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise our CISO, CMO, CRO, and executive leadership team members directly on emerging regulatory shifts, systemic industry risk, and where Drata's security and GRC strategy needs to head next.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide strategy and direction to company-wide responses to major shifts in our industry, such as new regulatory regimes, major certifications, systemic risk events surfaced by our customers, reaffirming the direction set has a lasting effect on Drata's market position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the overall security and GRC bar across Drata and industry-wide through knowledge sharing, internal and external forums, and pattern-setting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equip our sales teams with the security and GRC context and talking points they need to navigate technical conversations with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draw on your own relationships and reputation in the security and GRC community to open doors and build trust for Drata.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Marketing and GTM leadership to help plan executive events, speaking engagements, dinners, and roundtables throughout the year.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a real, ongoing influence on our product roadmap and go-to-market growth strategy — not just relaying field feedback, but helping shape the decisions themselves based on hands on experience corroborated with customer needs..</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Step in on the highest-stakes, least-defined security and GRC questions facing the business—the ones without an existing playbook—and provide the strategic direction to resolve them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Approach every external conversation as an extension of Drata’s security and GRC program, with the same care and integrity you’d bring internally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work alongside our own internal security and GRC team members to support any critical company initiatives as deemed necessary.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with our CISO to set priority on the industry events calendar, deciding together who leads, who supports, and who owns each engagement outright.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15+ years of progressive experience in security and GRC, including 10+ years leading and managing teams and 5+ years in the CISO seat (as a CISO, Deputy CISO, or equivalent senior security and GRC leader).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong grasp of the compliance frameworks our customers care about — including ISO 27001, SOC 2, HIPAA, FedRAMP, GDPR, NIST CSF, PCI DSS, and CCPA — and the practical experience to speak to them with real depth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills, with the ability to move comfortably between boardroom conversations and technical deep-dives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine reputation and network within the security and GRC community, built through your own experience leading programs and engaging with peers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of operating at the most senior individual contributor level of a security or GRC organization, where leadership and peers already come to you for strategic direction, not just execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working with ambiguity — turning undefined, fast-moving problems like regulatory direction, market shifts, or systemic risk into clear strategy, not just talking points.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with go-to-market teams in customer-facing conversations, and comfort with the pace and cadence of enterprise sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of thought leadership—speaking, writing, or other public and social engagement that reflects your experience and perspective.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SaaS and cloud-native environments, along with a thoughtful perspective on how AI is shaping both security and GRC risk and practice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with compliance automation platforms like Drata, so you can speak to our own product with the same credibility you bring to security and GRC itself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Openness to travel regularly and represent Drata’s security and GRC program in a public-facing capacity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A curious, thoughtful approach to using AI in your own work, with the judgment to apply it responsibly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15+ years in security and GRC, including 10+ years leading and managing security and GRC teams and 5+ years in the CISO seat (as a CISO, Deputy CISO, or equivalent senior security and GRC leader).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideally either based on the East Coast of the U.S. or willing to work EST hours to support coverage across the Americas and EMEA time zones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel regularly - 30-50% (including international travel) for customer meetings, conferences, and field events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional certifications such as CISSP, CISM, CRISC, or CCSP are a plus (though real, tenured experience carries more weight).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $210,000 - $350,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs Drata scales, we want our security and GRC leadership to be able to meet our customers’ needs in more places at once—in strategic customer conversations, on stage at industry events, and in the broader conversations happening across our security and GRC communities. We’re looking for a Field Chief Information Security Officer to join Drata’s Security & GRC organization, reporting directly to our SVP, Security & CISO, to help carry our vision to a wider audience. Your primary mission: be Drata's credible, practitioner-level security and GRC voice in the field.\n\n\n\nThis role is a senior, remote, U.S.-based security and GRC leadership role, ideally based on the East Coast to cover both the Americas and EMEA regions. As one of the most senior individual contributor roles in Drata's Security & Trust organization, this role shapes how Drata responds to the industry, informs the product experience, and aids in the strategic positioning of Drata’s future to acutely meet industry needs. This position is built for someone who has led security and GRC programs before and is excited to bring that experience directly to our customers, prospects, and industry peers. You’ll work closely with our go-to-market, customer success, and marketing teams, but your foundations are still rooted in technical security and GRC leadership—that is what will make you credible in the room among peers and is critical to the success of this role. Given the nature of our platform, this person will spend as much time in GRC conversations as in traditional security conversations due the complementary nature and inseparability of these functions.\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n\n\n - Partner with our amazing Sales, Customer Success, and Marketing teams on our most strategic enterprise and F500/G2000 opportunities—bringing tried-and-true security and GRC expertise into the conversation when customers need it most.\n\n - Lead executive briefings and CISO-to-CISO conversations that build trust and help prospective customers feel confident in their decision.\n\n - Represent Drata at industry conferences, CISO dinners, and regional roundtables across the Americas, EMEA, and APAC regions, building genuine relationships across the security and GRC community.\n\n - Share what you’re hearing in the field through webinars, panels, bylines, and press opportunities that build Drata’s voice and credibility in the security and GRC market.\n\n - Advise our CISO, CMO, CRO, and executive leadership team members directly on emerging regulatory shifts, systemic industry risk, and where Drata's security and GRC strategy needs to head next.\n\n - Provide strategy and direction to company-wide responses to major shifts in our industry, such as new regulatory regimes, major certifications, systemic risk events surfaced by our customers, reaffirming the direction set has a lasting effect on Drata's market position.\n\n - Raise the overall security and GRC bar across Drata and industry-wide through knowledge sharing, internal and external forums, and pattern-setting.\n\n - Equip our sales teams with the security and GRC context and talking points they need to navigate technical conversations with confidence.\n\n - Draw on your own relationships and reputation in the security and GRC community to open doors and build trust for Drata.\n\n - Partner with Marketing and GTM leadership to help plan executive events, speaking engagements, dinners, and roundtables throughout the year.\n\n - Act as a real, ongoing influence on our product roadmap and go-to-market growth strategy — not just relaying field feedback, but helping shape the decisions themselves based on hands on experience corroborated with customer needs..\n\n - Step in on the highest-stakes, least-defined security and GRC questions facing the business—the ones without an existing playbook—and provide the strategic direction to resolve them.\n\n - Approach every external conversation as an extension of Drata’s security and GRC program, with the same care and integrity you’d bring internally.\n\n - Work alongside our own internal security and GRC team members to support any critical company initiatives as deemed necessary.\n\n - Collaborate with our CISO to set priority on the industry events calendar, deciding together who leads, who supports, and who owns each engagement outright.\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 15+ years of progressive experience in security and GRC, including 10+ years leading and managing teams and 5+ years in the CISO seat (as a CISO, Deputy CISO, or equivalent senior security and GRC leader).\n\n - A strong grasp of the compliance frameworks our customers care about — including ISO 27001, SOC 2, HIPAA, FedRAMP, GDPR, NIST CSF, PCI DSS, and CCPA — and the practical experience to speak to them with real depth.\n\n - Excellent communication skills, with the ability to move comfortably between boardroom conversations and technical deep-dives.\n\n - A genuine reputation and network within the security and GRC community, built through your own experience leading programs and engaging with peers.\n\n - A track record of operating at the most senior individual contributor level of a security or GRC organization, where leadership and peers already come to you for strategic direction, not just execution.\n\n - Comfort working with ambiguity — turning undefined, fast-moving problems like regulatory direction, market shifts, or systemic risk into clear strategy, not just talking points.\n\n - Experience partnering with go-to-market teams in customer-facing conversations, and comfort with the pace and cadence of enterprise sales cycles.\n\n - A track record of thought leadership—speaking, writing, or other public and social engagement that reflects your experience and perspective.\n\n - Familiarity with SaaS and cloud-native environments, along with a thoughtful perspective on how AI is shaping both security and GRC risk and practice.\n\n - Familiarity with compliance automation platforms like Drata, so you can speak to our own product with the same credibility you bring to security and GRC itself.\n\n - Openness to travel regularly and represent Drata’s security and GRC program in a public-facing capacity.\n\n - A curious, thoughtful approach to using AI in your own work, with the judgment to apply it responsibly.\n\nRequirements:\n\n - 15+ years in security and GRC, including 10+ years leading and managing security and GRC teams and 5+ years in the CISO seat (as a CISO, Deputy CISO, or equivalent senior security and GRC leader).\n\n - Ideally either based on the East Coast of the U.S. or willing to work EST hours to support coverage across the Americas and EMEA time zones.\n\n - Willingness to travel regularly - 30-50% (including international travel) for customer meetings, conferences, and field events.\n\n - Professional certifications such as CISSP, CISM, CRISC, or CCSP are a plus (though real, tenured experience carries more weight).\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $210,000 - $350,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2ca6f8c9-c73b-4b1a-b238-5190f08b4e9c","title":"Director, Strategic Finance - GTM","department":"Finance & Accounting","team":"Finance & Accounting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T14:25:46.053+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/2ca6f8c9-c73b-4b1a-b238-5190f08b4e9c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/2ca6f8c9-c73b-4b1a-b238-5190f08b4e9c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Director of Strategic Finance - GTM is the embedded finance partner to Drata’s GTM org, working directly with the CRO, CMO, SVP of CS, and SVP of BD. This role owns ARR forecasting, capacity planning, investment allocation and ROI. You will partner with the VP of RevOps and be a trusted advisor in the room with GTM leadership, not a downstream reporting function and significantly beyond budget stewardship. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the dedicated finance business partner to the GTM leadership team, embedded in the organization's day-to-day operating rhythms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop deep expertise in our GTM engine, proactively identifying risks and opportunities and grounding recommendations in data-driven insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape GTM strategy by providing financial guidance on new initiatives, resource allocation, and investment tradeoffs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI to continuously evolve ARR forecasting models and deepen insights into key business drivers, including sales productivity, pipeline generation and conversion, and retention and expansion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide investment decisions using GTM unit economics and ROI frameworks, including CAC, LTV, payback period, Magic Number, and marketing efficiency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead GTM capacity planning and headcount forecasting for the long-range plan, annual budget, and quarterly reforecasts, ensuring alignment across GTM, RevOps, Finance, and People</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adopt an AI-first approach by automating spreadsheet-driven work and building scalable workflows, enabling greater focus on strategic partnership and decision-making</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of progressive experience in FP&amp;A, Strategic Finance, GTM Finance, Investment Banking, Consulting, or a related finance discipline within high-growth technology or SaaS environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience operating as a senior finance partner to executive GTM leaders, with the credibility and judgment to influence strategy, investment decisions, and resource allocation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience owning core GTM finance processes, including forecasting, annual planning, long-range planning, headcount and capacity planning, and performance analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thinks from first principles, building from the ground up while challenging assumptions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of SaaS and recurring revenue metrics, with the ability to translate complex data into clear, executive-ready insights and recommendations; experience with usage-based model is a bonus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success solving ambiguous, unstructured business problems and building scalable financial frameworks, operating cadences, and decision-support models</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of driving cross-functional alignment across Finance, GTM, and RevOps, while improving efficiency and decision-making through automation, systems, and process design</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $165,000 - $253,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Director of Strategic Finance - GTM is the embedded finance partner to Drata’s GTM org, working directly with the CRO, CMO, SVP of CS, and SVP of BD. This role owns ARR forecasting, capacity planning, investment allocation and ROI. You will partner with the VP of RevOps and be a trusted advisor in the room with GTM leadership, not a downstream reporting function and significantly beyond budget stewardship. \n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Serve as the dedicated finance business partner to the GTM leadership team, embedded in the organization's day-to-day operating rhythms\n\n - Develop deep expertise in our GTM engine, proactively identifying risks and opportunities and grounding recommendations in data-driven insights\n\n - Shape GTM strategy by providing financial guidance on new initiatives, resource allocation, and investment tradeoffs\n\n - Leverage AI to continuously evolve ARR forecasting models and deepen insights into key business drivers, including sales productivity, pipeline generation and conversion, and retention and expansion\n\n - Guide investment decisions using GTM unit economics and ROI frameworks, including CAC, LTV, payback period, Magic Number, and marketing efficiency\n\n - Lead GTM capacity planning and headcount forecasting for the long-range plan, annual budget, and quarterly reforecasts, ensuring alignment across GTM, RevOps, Finance, and People\n\n - Adopt an AI-first approach by automating spreadsheet-driven work and building scalable workflows, enabling greater focus on strategic partnership and decision-making\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 10+ years of progressive experience in FP&A, Strategic Finance, GTM Finance, Investment Banking, Consulting, or a related finance discipline within high-growth technology or SaaS environments\n\n - Proven experience operating as a senior finance partner to executive GTM leaders, with the credibility and judgment to influence strategy, investment decisions, and resource allocation\n\n - Deep experience owning core GTM finance processes, including forecasting, annual planning, long-range planning, headcount and capacity planning, and performance analysis\n\n - Thinks from first principles, building from the ground up while challenging assumptions\n\n - Strong command of SaaS and recurring revenue metrics, with the ability to translate complex data into clear, executive-ready insights and recommendations; experience with usage-based model is a bonus\n\n - Demonstrated success solving ambiguous, unstructured business problems and building scalable financial frameworks, operating cadences, and decision-support models\n\n - Track record of driving cross-functional alignment across Finance, GTM, and RevOps, while improving efficiency and decision-making through automation, systems, and process design\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $165,000 - $253,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0851570c-afd8-403f-9eb8-0bd23a6d0438","title":"Senior Product Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T16:37:28.568+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0851570c-afd8-403f-9eb8-0bd23a6d0438","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0851570c-afd8-403f-9eb8-0bd23a6d0438/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team?</strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\"><u>what they say here</u></a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Product Manager is a key position to support our growth, and we are looking for an experienced product manager to join us! As the Senior Product Manager, you will be working cross-functionally to design, build, and roll-out products and features that align with Drata’s strategy and vision. A top-notch senior product manager will have worked on numerous projects and have a firm grasp of how to satisfy consumers’ needs. Ideal candidates will be equally analytical and creative, and able to justify decisions to a range of stakeholders. This is an ideal position for someone who thrives in changing environments and can build the roadmap to create innovative product offerings.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define roadmap and requirements to solve big customers problems in the Enterprise space</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define an MVP experience and quickly learn and iterate based on feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Form hypotheses and run experiments using lean methodologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with engineering and design teams to define, build, and maintain products/features which are critical to growth and retention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with cross-functional teams on release plans and documentation to deliver value to our customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively partner across teams to anticipate and address risks and dependencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate progress and plan to leadership, peers, etc.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years designing and delivering world-class software products in a Product Management role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep customer empathy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for identifying and solving problems with the ability to conduct effective customer interviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capable of breaking down a big vision into small deliverables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ruthless prioritization of the backlog</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-starter with an entrepreneurial mindset and the drive to pursue opportunities beyond current constraints</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional collaboration skills working with PMs, engineers, designers, marketers, and customer success teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth mindset with a desire for continuous improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong verbal and written communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills paired with a data-informed mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience launching a new product offering from 0-1 strongly preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building complex products for Enterprise customers strongly preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in the Procurement, Vendors, Third-Party Risk or Risk space strongly preferred</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $157,000 - $252,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team?\nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Senior Product Manager is a key position to support our growth, and we are looking for an experienced product manager to join us! As the Senior Product Manager, you will be working cross-functionally to design, build, and roll-out products and features that align with Drata’s strategy and vision. A top-notch senior product manager will have worked on numerous projects and have a firm grasp of how to satisfy consumers’ needs. Ideal candidates will be equally analytical and creative, and able to justify decisions to a range of stakeholders. This is an ideal position for someone who thrives in changing environments and can build the roadmap to create innovative product offerings.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Define roadmap and requirements to solve big customers problems in the Enterprise space\n\n - Define an MVP experience and quickly learn and iterate based on feedback\n\n - Form hypotheses and run experiments using lean methodologies\n\n - Partner closely with engineering and design teams to define, build, and maintain products/features which are critical to growth and retention\n\n - Partner closely with cross-functional teams on release plans and documentation to deliver value to our customers\n\n - Proactively partner across teams to anticipate and address risks and dependencies\n\n - Communicate progress and plan to leadership, peers, etc.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 5+ years designing and delivering world-class software products in a Product Management role\n\n - Deep customer empathy\n\n - Passion for identifying and solving problems with the ability to conduct effective customer interviews\n\n - Capable of breaking down a big vision into small deliverables\n\n - Ruthless prioritization of the backlog\n\n - Self-starter with an entrepreneurial mindset and the drive to pursue opportunities beyond current constraints\n\n - Exceptional collaboration skills working with PMs, engineers, designers, marketers, and customer success teams\n\n - Growth mindset with a desire for continuous improvement\n\n - Strong verbal and written communication skills\n\n - Strong analytical skills paired with a data-informed mindset\n\n - Experience launching a new product offering from 0-1 strongly preferred\n\n - Experience building complex products for Enterprise customers strongly preferred\n\n - Experience in the Procurement, Vendors, Third-Party Risk or Risk space strongly preferred\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $157,000 - $252,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"82e7772f-562d-4089-b62e-f9907f3086ed","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Monetization Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T21:11:14.573+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/82e7772f-562d-4089-b62e-f9907f3086ed","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/82e7772f-562d-4089-b62e-f9907f3086ed/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team?</strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\"><u>what they say here</u></a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Staff Software Engineer, Monetization Platform serves as a technical leader with a primary focus on the systems that turn product usage, subscriptions, credits, commitments, and contracts into accurate customer outcomes and clean financial operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This person will architect and evolve the core billing domain for Drata: usage event ingestion, billable metrics, pricing and packaging, invoice generation, entitlement enforcement, and the integrations that connect engineering to Accounting, Finance, RevOps, Salesforce, CPQ, and ERP systems like NetSuite.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">They should be equally comfortable designing event-driven systems, shaping commercial flexibility with business stakeholders, and building operationally trustworthy software where correctness, audit-ability, and scale matter. Modern billing is no longer just “charge a credit card once a month” — it is a real-time product control plane that must support evolving pricing models without turning the codebase into a fragile mess.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Finance, Accounting, RevOps, and Engineering leadership to shape Drata’s long-term billing architecture and commercial flexibility across self-serve and enterprise motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design the primitives of a modern billing platform: usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, subscriptions, overages, and invoice workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect a system that can accurately meter product usage at scale, transform raw events into billable quantities, and support pricing changes without requiring constant product rework.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve the entitlement layer that separates pricing and packaging from product behavior, so feature access, limits, credits, and plan controls are programmable rather than hardcoded.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with SFDC admins, CPQ owners, and Finance systems stakeholders to ensure quote-to-cash flows are coherent across CRM, product, billing, ERP, and downstream reporting systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure billing systems are operationally trustworthy: idempotent event handling, strong reconciliation paths, reliable notifications, auditability, and clear observability for engineers and business teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review architecture and code for billing-related projects to ensure correctness, scale, security, and maintainability while empowering teams to own implementation details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot the hard problems: invoice discrepancies, usage drift, contract edge cases, entitlement bugs, migration failures, and cross-system data mismatches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-team initiatives such as introducing a usage-based billing foundation, rationalizing packaging models, improving billing developer experience, or migrating from brittle homegrown logic to more composable billing and entitlement systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers across teams on domain modeling, distributed systems tradeoffs, financial correctness, and the realities of building software where product behavior and revenue recognition are tightly coupled.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience as a software engineer, including meaningful time owning business-critical backend systems in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience architecting billing, payments, pricing, or quote-to-cash systems for a B2B SaaS company at meaningful scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience designing APIs and event-driven systems that ingest, validate, aggregate, and reconcile high-volume operational data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of modern billing models, including usage-based pricing, subscriptions, prepaid credits, commitments, overages, hybrid packaging, and enterprise-specific commercial terms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working directly with Accounting, Finance, RevOps, and GTM systems where data quality, auditability, and timing matter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience integrating with systems like Salesforce, CPQ, NetSuite, payment platforms, and downstream finance/reporting tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JavaScript/TypeScript and object-oriented programming</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building and consuming RESTful web services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relational databases, data modeling, and transactional workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Distributed systems and asynchronous processing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Writing unit, integration, and end-to-end tests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Logging, telemetry, and production debugging</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Git and modern CI/CD practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least one major cloud platform and modern infrastructure tooling</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong product and systems mindset: you can model the commercial domain cleanly, but you also know billing architecture is ultimately customer experience architecture.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Usage-based billing platforms such as Metronome, especially concepts like usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, and programmable invoice workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entitlement and monetization platforms such as Stigg, especially entitlements as a system of record for feature access, limits, credits, and packaging logic.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building systems that support both PLG/self-serve and enterprise sales motions on the same technical foundation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit logs, RBAC, webhooks, durable queues, and other patterns that make billing and monetization systems reliable and debuggable in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-assisted development tools</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ve had success in roles where you:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architected or modernized a billing system that had to support real usage metering, invoice correctness, and flexible commercial models rather than a single static subscription plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built systems where raw product activity was transformed into durable billing inputs and surfaced in customer-facing or internal financial workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Worked through pricing and packaging changes without repeatedly hardcoding logic into application code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supported models like prepaid credits, subscriptions with overage, enterprise commitments, or hybrid contracts for different customer segments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partnered directly with Finance, Accounting, and RevOps to close gaps between what the product did, what the customer bought, and what the company invoiced.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Led engineers through ambiguous, cross-functional initiatives where the right answer required balancing correctness, flexibility, speed, and operational simplicity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicated complex architectural decisions clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balanced individual contributor depth with mentoring and unblocking other engineers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $200,000 - $271,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team?\nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nThe Staff Software Engineer, Monetization Platform serves as a technical leader with a primary focus on the systems that turn product usage, subscriptions, credits, commitments, and contracts into accurate customer outcomes and clean financial operations.\n\nThis person will architect and evolve the core billing domain for Drata: usage event ingestion, billable metrics, pricing and packaging, invoice generation, entitlement enforcement, and the integrations that connect engineering to Accounting, Finance, RevOps, Salesforce, CPQ, and ERP systems like NetSuite.\n\nThey should be equally comfortable designing event-driven systems, shaping commercial flexibility with business stakeholders, and building operationally trustworthy software where correctness, audit-ability, and scale matter. Modern billing is no longer just “charge a credit card once a month” — it is a real-time product control plane that must support evolving pricing models without turning the codebase into a fragile mess.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Partner with Product, Finance, Accounting, RevOps, and Engineering leadership to shape Drata’s long-term billing architecture and commercial flexibility across self-serve and enterprise motions.\n\n - Design the primitives of a modern billing platform: usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, subscriptions, overages, and invoice workflows.\n\n - Architect a system that can accurately meter product usage at scale, transform raw events into billable quantities, and support pricing changes without requiring constant product rework.\n\n - Build and evolve the entitlement layer that separates pricing and packaging from product behavior, so feature access, limits, credits, and plan controls are programmable rather than hardcoded.\n\n - Work closely with SFDC admins, CPQ owners, and Finance systems stakeholders to ensure quote-to-cash flows are coherent across CRM, product, billing, ERP, and downstream reporting systems.\n\n - Ensure billing systems are operationally trustworthy: idempotent event handling, strong reconciliation paths, reliable notifications, auditability, and clear observability for engineers and business teams.\n\n - Review architecture and code for billing-related projects to ensure correctness, scale, security, and maintainability while empowering teams to own implementation details.\n\n - Troubleshoot the hard problems: invoice discrepancies, usage drift, contract edge cases, entitlement bugs, migration failures, and cross-system data mismatches.\n\n - Lead cross-team initiatives such as introducing a usage-based billing foundation, rationalizing packaging models, improving billing developer experience, or migrating from brittle homegrown logic to more composable billing and entitlement systems.\n\n - Mentor engineers across teams on domain modeling, distributed systems tradeoffs, financial correctness, and the realities of building software where product behavior and revenue recognition are tightly coupled.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 10+ years of experience as a software engineer, including meaningful time owning business-critical backend systems in production.\n\n - Deep experience architecting billing, payments, pricing, or quote-to-cash systems for a B2B SaaS company at meaningful scale.\n\n - Strong experience designing APIs and event-driven systems that ingest, validate, aggregate, and reconcile high-volume operational data.\n\n - Strong understanding of modern billing models, including usage-based pricing, subscriptions, prepaid credits, commitments, overages, hybrid packaging, and enterprise-specific commercial terms.\n\n - Experience working directly with Accounting, Finance, RevOps, and GTM systems where data quality, auditability, and timing matter.\n\n - Strong experience integrating with systems like Salesforce, CPQ, NetSuite, payment platforms, and downstream finance/reporting tooling.\n\n - Strong proficiency with:\n   \n   - JavaScript/TypeScript and object-oriented programming\n   \n   - Building and consuming RESTful web services\n   \n   - Relational databases, data modeling, and transactional workflows\n   \n   - Distributed systems and asynchronous processing\n   \n   - Writing unit, integration, and end-to-end tests\n   \n   - Logging, telemetry, and production debugging\n   \n   - Git and modern CI/CD practices\n   \n   - At least one major cloud platform and modern infrastructure tooling\n\n - A strong product and systems mindset: you can model the commercial domain cleanly, but you also know billing architecture is ultimately customer experience architecture.\n\nBonus Qualifications\n\n - Usage-based billing platforms such as Metronome, especially concepts like usage events, billable metrics, products, rate cards, contracts, credits, and programmable invoice workflows.\n\n - Entitlement and monetization platforms such as Stigg, especially entitlements as a system of record for feature access, limits, credits, and packaging logic.\n\n - Building systems that support both PLG/self-serve and enterprise sales motions on the same technical foundation.\n\n - Audit logs, RBAC, webhooks, durable queues, and other patterns that make billing and monetization systems reliable and debuggable in production.\n\n - AI-assisted development tools\n\nYou’ve had success in roles where you:\n\n - Architected or modernized a billing system that had to support real usage metering, invoice correctness, and flexible commercial models rather than a single static subscription plan.\n\n - Built systems where raw product activity was transformed into durable billing inputs and surfaced in customer-facing or internal financial workflows.\n\n - Worked through pricing and packaging changes without repeatedly hardcoding logic into application code.\n\n - Supported models like prepaid credits, subscriptions with overage, enterprise commitments, or hybrid contracts for different customer segments.\n\n - Partnered directly with Finance, Accounting, and RevOps to close gaps between what the product did, what the customer bought, and what the company invoiced.\n\n - Led engineers through ambiguous, cross-functional initiatives where the right answer required balancing correctness, flexibility, speed, and operational simplicity.\n\n - Communicated complex architectural decisions clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - Balanced individual contributor depth with mentoring and unblocking other engineers.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $200,000 - $271,500 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0ad403d1-e667-4b82-aac2-c6bd3f898cab","title":"Senior Field Marketing Manager, East Coast, US","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T19:18:43.075+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0ad403d1-e667-4b82-aac2-c6bd3f898cab","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/0ad403d1-e667-4b82-aac2-c6bd3f898cab/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is looking for a Senior Field Marketing Manager to build and execute regional field marketing programs that drive pipeline and revenue impact across our Commercial and Enterprise business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is suited for a results-oriented, savvy field marketer who understands how to build programs that contribute to pipeline growth and measurable business impact. The right candidate brings strong commercial judgment, creative ideas, and the ability to turn strategy into high-impact programs that perform. They know how to build trust across sales, vendors, and partners, tailor experiences for executive and practitioner audiences, and see programs through from idea to follow-up with a clear focus on results.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own field marketing strategy and execution for a defined AMER region, setting market priorities, regional coverage, and program mix across the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate strategy into a regional field marketing plan that supports Commercial and Enterprise growth in priority markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage programs across trade shows, vendor-led executive programs, Drata-led account-focused events, hospitality events with partners, and partner-supported sponsorship opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design programs for executive and practitioner audiences, adapting format, messaging, and experience by segment, persona, and market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pilot differentiated event ideas and determine what to refine, repeat, scale, or stop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships across SDRs, AEs, sales leaders, vendors, and partners to drive alignment and program success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end execution, including planning, promotion, logistics, follow-up, and post-program optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Measure performance through meetings, engagement, pipeline contribution, and overall program effectiveness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring clear recommendations to leadership on where to invest, what to test, and how to improve regional field performance over time.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in B2B field marketing, regional marketing, event marketing, or integrated marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of leading in-person and virtual programs that drive pipeline and revenue growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building programs for executive and practitioner audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong relationship-building skills and the ability to earn trust quickly across sales, marketing, vendors, and external partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sound judgment on program mix, audience strategy, and where to invest time and budget for the greatest impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A creative mindset paired with strong execution, follow-through, and measurable results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment where some processes are still being built or refined.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role requires travel across the assigned region based on event cadence and business needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication, organization, and project management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in B2B SaaS, cybersecurity, compliance, or a related technology space is preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel 25–35% for Drata and partner events, conferences, team offsites, and other in-person company engagements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $135,000 - $207,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is looking for a Senior Field Marketing Manager to build and execute regional field marketing programs that drive pipeline and revenue impact across our Commercial and Enterprise business.\n\nThis role is suited for a results-oriented, savvy field marketer who understands how to build programs that contribute to pipeline growth and measurable business impact. The right candidate brings strong commercial judgment, creative ideas, and the ability to turn strategy into high-impact programs that perform. They know how to build trust across sales, vendors, and partners, tailor experiences for executive and practitioner audiences, and see programs through from idea to follow-up with a clear focus on results.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Own field marketing strategy and execution for a defined AMER region, setting market priorities, regional coverage, and program mix across the U.S.\n\n - Translate strategy into a regional field marketing plan that supports Commercial and Enterprise growth in priority markets.\n\n - Develop and manage programs across trade shows, vendor-led executive programs, Drata-led account-focused events, hospitality events with partners, and partner-supported sponsorship opportunities.\n\n - Design programs for executive and practitioner audiences, adapting format, messaging, and experience by segment, persona, and market.\n\n - Pilot differentiated event ideas and determine what to refine, repeat, scale, or stop.\n\n - Build strong relationships across SDRs, AEs, sales leaders, vendors, and partners to drive alignment and program success.\n\n - Own end-to-end execution, including planning, promotion, logistics, follow-up, and post-program optimization.\n\n - Measure performance through meetings, engagement, pipeline contribution, and overall program effectiveness.\n\n - Bring clear recommendations to leadership on where to invest, what to test, and how to improve regional field performance over time.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 7+ years of experience in B2B field marketing, regional marketing, event marketing, or integrated marketing.\n\n - A track record of leading in-person and virtual programs that drive pipeline and revenue growth.\n\n - Experience building programs for executive and practitioner audiences.\n\n - Strong relationship-building skills and the ability to earn trust quickly across sales, marketing, vendors, and external partners.\n\n - Sound judgment on program mix, audience strategy, and where to invest time and budget for the greatest impact.\n\n - A creative mindset paired with strong execution, follow-through, and measurable results.\n\n - Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment where some processes are still being built or refined.\n\n - This role requires travel across the assigned region based on event cadence and business needs.\n\n - Excellent communication, organization, and project management skills.\n\n - Experience in B2B SaaS, cybersecurity, compliance, or a related technology space is preferred.\n\n - Willingness to travel 25–35% for Drata and partner events, conferences, team offsites, and other in-person company engagements.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $135,000 - $207,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"803bebd0-0c94-4092-a219-a681aef788cc","title":"Principal Product Operations Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T20:06:24.085+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/803bebd0-0c94-4092-a219-a681aef788cc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/803bebd0-0c94-4092-a219-a681aef788cc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Principal Product Operations, you will define and scale the operating model that enables Product, Design, and Engineering to execute with clarity, rigor, and speed. This is a highly strategic, cross-functional leadership role responsible for shaping how product investments are prioritized, planned, measured, and communicated across the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will partner closely with executive leaders across Product, Design, Engineering, Customer Success, Sales, and Operations to drive alignment on product strategy, annual and quarterly planning, roadmap governance, portfolio health, experimentation, and business outcomes. You will serve as a force multiplier for the product organization by establishing the systems, cadences, and insights that help teams make better decisions and deliver greater impact at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve the product operating model, including planning frameworks, prioritization practices, governance mechanisms, decision-making cadences, and cross-functional collaboration norms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead company-level product planning and roadmap operations, partnering with senior leaders to drive annual planning, quarterly planning, investment tradeoff discussions, commitment tracking, and executive communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish scalable mechanisms to improve visibility, accountability, and execution across the product development lifecycle, from idea intake through launch and post-launch measurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive portfolio-level insight and operational rigor by defining and tracking the health of strategic initiatives, product bets, delivery risks, and outcome attainment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Design, Engineering, GTM, and Customer teams to improve how customer feedback, market signals, and business priorities inform product decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and operationalize executive-ready reporting on roadmap progress, product performance, organizational throughput, experimentation results, and key operational metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify structural inefficiencies and lead high-impact initiatives to improve planning quality, process consistency, speed of execution, and cross-functional alignment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, implement, and optimize tooling, systems, and workflows that support product planning, collaboration, experimentation, analytics, and knowledge management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable frameworks for experimentation and learning, enabling teams to run effective tests, measure impact, and incorporate findings into product strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain durable documentation, standards, playbooks, and best practices for product and design operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence leaders at all levels through data-driven recommendations, strong operational judgment, and a clear point of view on how to improve organizational effectiveness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a thought partner to product and functional leaders on organizational design, process maturity, and operational excellence.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years of experience in product operations, product management, strategy and operations, business operations, or a related discipline, with significant experience in high-growth SaaS and AI-first environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success operating at principal or director level or equivalent, influencing senior leaders and driving cross-functional change across complex organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in product development lifecycles, product management practices, design collaboration models, and engineering partnership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience leading portfolio planning, roadmap operations, prioritization processes, and executive-level business reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional analytical and systems thinking skills, with the ability to translate data into strategic insights, operational recommendations, and clear decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of product and business analytics ecosystems, including tools such as Segment, Amplitude, Productboard, Linear, Jira, BI platforms, and experimentation frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing scalable workflows and automations using tools such as Zapier, Retool, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent program leadership skills, including the ability to drive alignment across multiple stakeholders, manage ambiguity, and execute through influence rather than authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to tailor messaging for executives, technical partners, and cross-functional audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Technology, Design, or a related field; advanced degree is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Personal attributes</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic: Sees around corners, connects operational details to broader business outcomes, and brings a long-term perspective to organizational scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influential: Builds trust quickly, aligns diverse stakeholders, and drives change across functions and levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured: Brings clarity, discipline, and strong judgment to ambiguous, fast-moving environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-Centric: Keeps customer outcomes at the center of planning, prioritization, and process design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curious: Uses data, experimentation, and continuous learning to improve systems and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative: Operates as a true partner across Product, Design, Engineering, and GTM teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $180,000 - $276,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs Principal Product Operations, you will define and scale the operating model that enables Product, Design, and Engineering to execute with clarity, rigor, and speed. This is a highly strategic, cross-functional leadership role responsible for shaping how product investments are prioritized, planned, measured, and communicated across the company.\n\nYou will partner closely with executive leaders across Product, Design, Engineering, Customer Success, Sales, and Operations to drive alignment on product strategy, annual and quarterly planning, roadmap governance, portfolio health, experimentation, and business outcomes. You will serve as a force multiplier for the product organization by establishing the systems, cadences, and insights that help teams make better decisions and deliver greater impact at scale.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Own and evolve the product operating model, including planning frameworks, prioritization practices, governance mechanisms, decision-making cadences, and cross-functional collaboration norms.\n\n - Lead company-level product planning and roadmap operations, partnering with senior leaders to drive annual planning, quarterly planning, investment tradeoff discussions, commitment tracking, and executive communication.\n\n - Establish scalable mechanisms to improve visibility, accountability, and execution across the product development lifecycle, from idea intake through launch and post-launch measurement.\n\n - Drive portfolio-level insight and operational rigor by defining and tracking the health of strategic initiatives, product bets, delivery risks, and outcome attainment.\n\n - Partner with Product, Design, Engineering, GTM, and Customer teams to improve how customer feedback, market signals, and business priorities inform product decisions.\n\n - Build and operationalize executive-ready reporting on roadmap progress, product performance, organizational throughput, experimentation results, and key operational metrics.\n\n - Identify structural inefficiencies and lead high-impact initiatives to improve planning quality, process consistency, speed of execution, and cross-functional alignment.\n\n - Evaluate, implement, and optimize tooling, systems, and workflows that support product planning, collaboration, experimentation, analytics, and knowledge management.\n\n - Develop scalable frameworks for experimentation and learning, enabling teams to run effective tests, measure impact, and incorporate findings into product strategy.\n\n - Create and maintain durable documentation, standards, playbooks, and best practices for product and design operations.\n\n - Influence leaders at all levels through data-driven recommendations, strong operational judgment, and a clear point of view on how to improve organizational effectiveness.\n\n - Serve as a thought partner to product and functional leaders on organizational design, process maturity, and operational excellence.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 10+ years of experience in product operations, product management, strategy and operations, business operations, or a related discipline, with significant experience in high-growth SaaS and AI-first environments.\n\n - Demonstrated success operating at principal or director level or equivalent, influencing senior leaders and driving cross-functional change across complex organizations.\n\n - Deep expertise in product development lifecycles, product management practices, design collaboration models, and engineering partnership.\n\n - Strong experience leading portfolio planning, roadmap operations, prioritization processes, and executive-level business reviews.\n\n - Exceptional analytical and systems thinking skills, with the ability to translate data into strategic insights, operational recommendations, and clear decisions.\n\n - Strong command of product and business analytics ecosystems, including tools such as Segment, Amplitude, Productboard, Linear, Jira, BI platforms, and experimentation frameworks.\n\n - Experience designing scalable workflows and automations using tools such as Zapier, Retool, or similar platforms.\n\n - Excellent program leadership skills, including the ability to drive alignment across multiple stakeholders, manage ambiguity, and execute through influence rather than authority.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to tailor messaging for executives, technical partners, and cross-functional audiences.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Technology, Design, or a related field; advanced degree is a plus.\n\nPersonal attributes\n\n - Strategic: Sees around corners, connects operational details to broader business outcomes, and brings a long-term perspective to organizational scale.\n\n - Influential: Builds trust quickly, aligns diverse stakeholders, and drives change across functions and levels.\n\n - Structured: Brings clarity, discipline, and strong judgment to ambiguous, fast-moving environments.\n\n - Customer-Centric: Keeps customer outcomes at the center of planning, prioritization, and process design.\n\n - Curious: Uses data, experimentation, and continuous learning to improve systems and outcomes.\n\n - Collaborative: Operates as a true partner across Product, Design, Engineering, and GTM teams.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $180,000 - $276,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"44ee8015-05aa-405b-8fb5-a71d13da987a","title":"Total Rewards Analyst","department":"People Operations","team":"People Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T20:59:49.367+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/44ee8015-05aa-405b-8fb5-a71d13da987a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/44ee8015-05aa-405b-8fb5-a71d13da987a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is looking for a <strong>Total Rewards Analyst</strong> to strengthen the accuracy, scalability, and insightfulness of our compensation programs while providing reliable support across benefits and broader total rewards operations. This compensation-led role will turn market data and employee data into clear recommendations, support annual compensation and equity cycles, and help leaders make consistent, equitable pay decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A key part of the role is AI enablement: you will identify repetitive, manual, or error-prone workflows and use approved AI and automation tools to make them faster, more accurate, and easier to scale. You will combine strong compensation fundamentals with sound judgment, data discipline, and a high standard for confidentiality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze internal compensation data and external market data to support salary ranges, job leveling, compa-ratio analysis, pay equity reviews, and compensation recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the planning and execution of annual merit, bonus, and equity review processes, including modeling, budgeting, manager guidance, system preparation, testing, communications, and post-cycle audits.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare analyses and recommendations for new hires, promotions, transfers, off-cycle adjustments, and other pay actions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the administration and continuous improvement of base pay, incentive, equity, and recognition programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate job, level, range, and compensation data across relevant systems and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate compensation changes and equity inputs for accuracy, consistency, policy alignment, and internal equity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide operational support for health and welfare, retirement, leave, wellness, and other benefits programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with benefits vendors and internal stakeholders to investigate employee questions, resolve data discrepancies, and monitor service delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support benefits eligibility, enrollment, invoice, utilization, and renewal analyses as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to automate recurring workflows, such as data validation, reconciliation, reporting, survey preparation, communications, and intake triage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use approved AI tools to accelerate analysis, generate first drafts, summarize trends, and improve self-service—while applying human review to all outputs and decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build or improve lightweight automations, templates, prompts, and operating procedures that reduce manual effort and improve accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with HRIS, People Operations, Finance, and appropriate technical partners to improve integrations, reporting, controls, and workflow design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support compliance with applicable compensation, pay transparency, pay equity, benefits, and recordkeeping requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform regular audits and reconciliations across HRIS, compensation, equity, payroll, benefits, and reporting data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate data issues, policy exceptions, and potential compliance risks promptly and thoughtfully.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle sensitive questions with discretion, empathy, and sound judgment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment while meeting deadlines and maintaining a high bar for accuracy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–4 years of experience in compensation, total rewards, benefits, HR analytics, HRIS, or a closely related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience analyzing compensation data, interpreting market benchmarks, and building recommendations from quantitative information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills, including pivot tables, lookups, data validation, and financial or compensation modeling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting an annual compensation, bonus, equity, or benefits cycle from planning through audit and closeout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with HRIS, compensation planning, benefits administration, or market-pricing systems; Workday experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to improve processes through automation, reporting, workflow design, or approved AI tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and a track record of handling confidential data responsibly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain data and recommendations to non-specialist audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization, problem-solving, and project-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Finance, Economics, Statistics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a high-growth technology or SaaS company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to salary architecture, job leveling, pay equity, equity compensation, incentive plans, or compensation philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with compensation survey sources or market-pricing tools such as Radford, Mercer, WTW, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with reporting or visualization tools such as Tableau, Looker, Power BI, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting multi-state or global compensation and benefits programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CCP, CBP, CEBS, or progress toward a relevant certification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Examples of using AI or automation to improve data quality, reporting, employee support, or operational efficiency.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $99,500 - $122,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is looking for a Total Rewards Analyst to strengthen the accuracy, scalability, and insightfulness of our compensation programs while providing reliable support across benefits and broader total rewards operations. This compensation-led role will turn market data and employee data into clear recommendations, support annual compensation and equity cycles, and help leaders make consistent, equitable pay decisions.\n\nA key part of the role is AI enablement: you will identify repetitive, manual, or error-prone workflows and use approved AI and automation tools to make them faster, more accurate, and easier to scale. You will combine strong compensation fundamentals with sound judgment, data discipline, and a high standard for confidentiality.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\n - Analyze internal compensation data and external market data to support salary ranges, job leveling, compa-ratio analysis, pay equity reviews, and compensation recommendations.\n\n - Support the planning and execution of annual merit, bonus, and equity review processes, including modeling, budgeting, manager guidance, system preparation, testing, communications, and post-cycle audits.\n\n - Prepare analyses and recommendations for new hires, promotions, transfers, off-cycle adjustments, and other pay actions.\n\n - Support the administration and continuous improvement of base pay, incentive, equity, and recognition programs.\n\n - Maintain accurate job, level, range, and compensation data across relevant systems and documentation.\n\n - Validate compensation changes and equity inputs for accuracy, consistency, policy alignment, and internal equity.\n\n - Provide operational support for health and welfare, retirement, leave, wellness, and other benefits programs.\n\n - Partner with benefits vendors and internal stakeholders to investigate employee questions, resolve data discrepancies, and monitor service delivery.\n\n - Support benefits eligibility, enrollment, invoice, utilization, and renewal analyses as needed.\n\n - Identify opportunities to automate recurring workflows, such as data validation, reconciliation, reporting, survey preparation, communications, and intake triage.\n\n - Use approved AI tools to accelerate analysis, generate first drafts, summarize trends, and improve self-service—while applying human review to all outputs and decisions.\n\n - Build or improve lightweight automations, templates, prompts, and operating procedures that reduce manual effort and improve accuracy.\n\n - Partner with HRIS, People Operations, Finance, and appropriate technical partners to improve integrations, reporting, controls, and workflow design.\n\n - Support compliance with applicable compensation, pay transparency, pay equity, benefits, and recordkeeping requirements.\n\n - Perform regular audits and reconciliations across HRIS, compensation, equity, payroll, benefits, and reporting data.\n\n - Escalate data issues, policy exceptions, and potential compliance risks promptly and thoughtfully.\n\n - Handle sensitive questions with discretion, empathy, and sound judgment.\n\n - Manage multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment while meeting deadlines and maintaining a high bar for accuracy.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 2–4 years of experience in compensation, total rewards, benefits, HR analytics, HRIS, or a closely related field.\n\n - Experience analyzing compensation data, interpreting market benchmarks, and building recommendations from quantitative information.\n\n - Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills, including pivot tables, lookups, data validation, and financial or compensation modeling.\n\n - Experience supporting an annual compensation, bonus, equity, or benefits cycle from planning through audit and closeout.\n\n - Familiarity with HRIS, compensation planning, benefits administration, or market-pricing systems; Workday experience is a plus.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to improve processes through automation, reporting, workflow design, or approved AI tools.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and a track record of handling confidential data responsibly.\n\n - Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain data and recommendations to non-specialist audiences.\n\n - Strong organization, problem-solving, and project-management skills.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Finance, Economics, Statistics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\n\nNice to have\n\n - Experience in a high-growth technology or SaaS company.\n\n - Exposure to salary architecture, job leveling, pay equity, equity compensation, incentive plans, or compensation philosophy.\n\n - Experience with compensation survey sources or market-pricing tools such as Radford, Mercer, WTW, or similar.\n\n - Experience with reporting or visualization tools such as Tableau, Looker, Power BI, or similar.\n\n - Experience supporting multi-state or global compensation and benefits programs.\n\n - CCP, CBP, CEBS, or progress toward a relevant certification.\n\n - Examples of using AI or automation to improve data quality, reporting, employee support, or operational efficiency.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $99,500 - $122,800 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"20db37fa-f83e-4328-bb56-052415c00fd8","title":"Enterprise Account Executive - EMEA","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - EMEA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T23:13:43.334+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/20db37fa-f83e-4328-bb56-052415c00fd8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/20db37fa-f83e-4328-bb56-052415c00fd8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a passionate sales professional with 7+ years of experience in a customer facing role selling SaaS or consulting with an ability to focus on the Enterprise space - not necessarily in the security and compliance space. Exceptional candidates are hungry to work in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment, and have a proven track record of success in their past roles and experiences! <strong>Please note, we are only considering candidates who reside in the United Kingdom who are professionally proficient/fluent in English as well as either French or German at this time. </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsible for bringing new customers on board and consistently growing revenue by exceeding revenue targets/quota</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute strategies for driving partnerships and revenue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and manage your pipeline of prospects; become an expert on a region and understanding the complexities of that specific market</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consult senior executives to discover their needs and educate them through an accelerated buying process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve our product offering based on deep understanding of the needs of our customers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience in a customer-facing B2B SaaS Sales role, with at least 2 years in a closing new business capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professionally Proficient/Fluent in English as well as either French or German</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to focus on bringing in Enterprise accounts with 1K+ full time employees</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred background in the start-up space</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-starter who brings ideas to life and takes pride in results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resourceful, finding ways to get things done regardless of the obstacles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and detail-oriented with an ability to handle a variety of different projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A talented communicator and a “people person” who enjoys working with others. You are thoughtful about the ways you communicate and the impact that may have on a customer. You have the ability to sense when a conversation is progressing in a positive or negative way and have the confidence to address concerns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident but always striving to do better. You are not afraid to ask for help. You value honest, action-oriented feedback and believe it is a tool to improve as a team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, employees <em>and their dependents</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between </em>£193,500 - £225,800 (UK), <em> </em>€232,050 - €273,000 (EMEA), <em>and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for a passionate sales professional with 7+ years of experience in a customer facing role selling SaaS or consulting with an ability to focus on the Enterprise space - not necessarily in the security and compliance space. Exceptional candidates are hungry to work in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment, and have a proven track record of success in their past roles and experiences! Please note, we are only considering candidates who reside in the United Kingdom who are professionally proficient/fluent in English as well as either French or German at this time. \n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Responsible for bringing new customers on board and consistently growing revenue by exceeding revenue targets/quota\n\n - Develop and execute strategies for driving partnerships and revenue\n\n - Build and manage your pipeline of prospects; become an expert on a region and understanding the complexities of that specific market\n\n - Consult senior executives to discover their needs and educate them through an accelerated buying process\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve our product offering based on deep understanding of the needs of our customers\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 7+ years of experience in a customer-facing B2B SaaS Sales role, with at least 2 years in a closing new business capacity\n\n - Professionally Proficient/Fluent in English as well as either French or German\n\n - Ability to focus on bringing in Enterprise accounts with 1K+ full time employees\n\n - Preferred background in the start-up space\n\n - Self-starter who brings ideas to life and takes pride in results\n\n - Resourceful, finding ways to get things done regardless of the obstacles\n\n - Organized and detail-oriented with an ability to handle a variety of different projects\n\n - A talented communicator and a “people person” who enjoys working with others. You are thoughtful about the ways you communicate and the impact that may have on a customer. You have the ability to sense when a conversation is progressing in a positive or negative way and have the confidence to address concerns.\n\n - Confident but always striving to do better. You are not afraid to ask for help. You value honest, action-oriented feedback and believe it is a tool to improve as a team.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, employees and their dependents\n\n - Financial Well-being: To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between £193,500 - £225,800 (UK),  €232,050 - €273,000 (EMEA), and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role.\n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c5d24acf-cdd4-424f-833c-6903e7610938","title":"Sales Engineer - London","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T23:22:49.850+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/c5d24acf-cdd4-424f-833c-6903e7610938","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/c5d24acf-cdd4-424f-833c-6903e7610938/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a motivated, curious, and solutions-driven Sales Engineer with a passion for helping customers solve complex challenges through technology. In this role, you will support the sales and channel team in engaging prospects and customers, demonstrating technical value, and driving successful outcomes. You will play a key role in both new customer acquisition and expanding relationships with existing customers. Measures of success include contribution to deal progression and overall impact on sales team efficiency and success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a hybrid role with the expectation of working in the London office 1-2 days per week.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Account Executives to support prospective customers as they evaluate the Drata platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support technical proof of concepts and demonstrations, helping to simplify the buyer’s journey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align customer pain points and requirements with proposed solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and deliver compelling product demonstrations and help win new channel partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and communicate customer needs to product and engineering teams for future enhancements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct competitive research to inform positioning and strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in building financial business cases for prospective customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage technical aspects of RFP/RFI responses and documentation</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Curiosity</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to understand customer challenges, industry trends, and evolving technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to quickly learn and adapt to new technologies and solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to problem-solving, always looking for creative ways to add value</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaboration</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work closely with sales, channel, product, and engineering teams to deliver the best solutions for customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to share knowledge and contribute to team success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A mindset of continuous learning and improvement through feedback and shared experiences</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Solutions-Oriented Mindset</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive approach to identifying challenges and proposing effective solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to translate technical capabilities into business value for customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical thinking to support decision-making and sales strategy</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impactful Communication</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to clearly articulate complex technical concepts in an easy-to-understand manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills for presentations, customer interactions, and internal collaboration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidence in delivering demonstrations and engaging with stakeholders at all levels</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Skills &amp; Experience:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience as a Sales / Solutions Engineer preferably in the SaaS space.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of common cloud providers across tools including:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Infrastructure - AWS, GCP, Azure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identity Management - Okta, Google Workspace, Entra ID</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Version Control - GitHub, BitBucket, GitLab</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running trials and POCs and serving as the technical partner of the prospective customer throughout their evaluation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in integrating cloud systems and API workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy to understand manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a fast-paced, constantly changing environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent presentation and creativity skills</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, employees <em>and their dependents</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between £126,800 - £156,700 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for a motivated, curious, and solutions-driven Sales Engineer with a passion for helping customers solve complex challenges through technology. In this role, you will support the sales and channel team in engaging prospects and customers, demonstrating technical value, and driving successful outcomes. You will play a key role in both new customer acquisition and expanding relationships with existing customers. Measures of success include contribution to deal progression and overall impact on sales team efficiency and success.\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation of working in the London office 1-2 days per week.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Partner with Account Executives to support prospective customers as they evaluate the Drata platform\n\n - Support technical proof of concepts and demonstrations, helping to simplify the buyer’s journey\n\n - Align customer pain points and requirements with proposed solutions\n\n - Develop and deliver compelling product demonstrations and help win new channel partners.\n\n - Gather and communicate customer needs to product and engineering teams for future enhancements\n\n - Conduct competitive research to inform positioning and strategy\n\n - Assist in building financial business cases for prospective customers\n\n - Manage technical aspects of RFP/RFI responses and documentation\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\nCuriosity\n\n - A strong desire to understand customer challenges, industry trends, and evolving technologies\n\n - Ability to quickly learn and adapt to new technologies and solutions\n\n - Proactive approach to problem-solving, always looking for creative ways to add value\n\nCollaboration\n\n - Ability to work closely with sales, channel, product, and engineering teams to deliver the best solutions for customers\n\n - Willingness to share knowledge and contribute to team success\n\n - A mindset of continuous learning and improvement through feedback and shared experiences\n\nSolutions-Oriented Mindset\n\n - A proactive approach to identifying challenges and proposing effective solutions\n\n - Ability to translate technical capabilities into business value for customers\n\n - Strong analytical thinking to support decision-making and sales strategy\n\nImpactful Communication\n\n - Ability to clearly articulate complex technical concepts in an easy-to-understand manner\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills for presentations, customer interactions, and internal collaboration\n\n - Confidence in delivering demonstrations and engaging with stakeholders at all levels\n\nPreferred Skills & Experience:\n\n - 2+ years of experience as a Sales / Solutions Engineer preferably in the SaaS space.\n\n - Working knowledge of common cloud providers across tools including:\n   \n   - Infrastructure - AWS, GCP, Azure\n   \n   - Identity Management - Okta, Google Workspace, Entra ID\n   \n   - Version Control - GitHub, BitBucket, GitLab\n\n - Experience running trials and POCs and serving as the technical partner of the prospective customer throughout their evaluation.\n\n - Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in integrating cloud systems and API workflows\n\n - Ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy to understand manner\n\n - Experience working in a fast-paced, constantly changing environment\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Excellent presentation and creativity skills\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, employees and their dependents\n\n - Financial Well-being: To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between £126,800 - £156,700 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9c426423-5cc0-4765-95ef-f1910ded980a","title":"Senior Sales Engineer - London","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - London","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T23:29:30.369+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/9c426423-5cc0-4765-95ef-f1910ded980a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/9c426423-5cc0-4765-95ef-f1910ded980a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a seasoned, hardworking, smart and over achieving Senior Sales Engineer with proven experience and a passion for selling technology solutions to senior executives. You will be responsible for selling into new prospects as well as farming back into existing customers to ensure high renewal and customer satisfaction levels. Measures of success include new customer acquisition rates, up-selling, cross-selling, customer satisfaction and contribution to overall sales team and business success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a hybrid role with the expectation of working in the London office 1-2 days per week.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with sales executives to plan, prepare and execute on strategic deals in sales cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create a process from the ground-up to streamline the communication and increase efficiencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage all technical aspects of RFP / RFI responses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively communicate client needs to the R&amp;D teams for future product enhancements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Focus on shortening the sales cycles while providing technical support on proof of concepts without overcomplicating the buyer’s journey.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support sales executives with solution selling into prospect account base</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successfully match customer pain/requirements to proposed solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and deliver powerful presentations and demos that clearly communicate the uniqueness of the value proposition</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect and document competitive intelligence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Model the financial business case associated with each sales opportunity</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience as a Sales/Solutions Engineer preferably in the SaaS space.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred knowledge of cloud providers, such as AWS, GCP, etc</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building out proof of concepts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record selling/supporting complex enterprise solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to forge strong, long-lasting relationships with senior executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy to understand manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in software development and web technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent presentation and creativity skills</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, employees <em>and their dependents</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between £152,200 - £188,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nWe are looking for a seasoned, hardworking, smart and over achieving Senior Sales Engineer with proven experience and a passion for selling technology solutions to senior executives. You will be responsible for selling into new prospects as well as farming back into existing customers to ensure high renewal and customer satisfaction levels. Measures of success include new customer acquisition rates, up-selling, cross-selling, customer satisfaction and contribution to overall sales team and business success.\n\nThis is a hybrid role with the expectation of working in the London office 1-2 days per week.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Partner with sales executives to plan, prepare and execute on strategic deals in sales cycles\n\n - Create a process from the ground-up to streamline the communication and increase efficiencies\n\n - Manage all technical aspects of RFP / RFI responses\n\n - Effectively communicate client needs to the R&D teams for future product enhancements\n\n - Focus on shortening the sales cycles while providing technical support on proof of concepts without overcomplicating the buyer’s journey.\n\n - Support sales executives with solution selling into prospect account base\n\n - Successfully match customer pain/requirements to proposed solutions\n\n - Create and deliver powerful presentations and demos that clearly communicate the uniqueness of the value proposition\n\n - Collect and document competitive intelligence\n\n - Model the financial business case associated with each sales opportunity\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 5+ years of experience as a Sales/Solutions Engineer preferably in the SaaS space.\n\n - Preferred knowledge of cloud providers, such as AWS, GCP, etc\n\n - Experience building out proof of concepts\n\n - Proven track record selling/supporting complex enterprise solutions\n\n - Ability to forge strong, long-lasting relationships with senior executives\n\n - Ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy to understand manner\n\n - Solid technical background with understanding and/or hands-on experience in software development and web technologies\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Excellent presentation and creativity skills\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, employees and their dependents\n\n - Financial Well-being: To support your retirement planning, our EOR offers a pension plan under which you contribute 5% of your basic earnings, and your employer contributes an additional 4%, helping you build a more secure financial future.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between £152,200 - £188,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a91185b8-09a0-4331-93df-6006c320a4d0","title":"Senior Executive Business Partner, CEO's Office","department":"Administrative","team":"Administrative","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T18:30:08.530+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/a91185b8-09a0-4331-93df-6006c320a4d0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/a91185b8-09a0-4331-93df-6006c320a4d0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team? </strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\">what they say here</a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\">LinkedIn</a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Drata scales, we're looking for a strategic, operationally stellar Sr. Executive Business Partner to support our CEO &amp; Co-Founder. This role sits at the heart of Drata's operational engine: translating vision into action, keeping the executive team and internal teams aligned, and giving our CEO the space to lead with clarity and momentum.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll thrive here if you lead with relationships, build trust quickly with everyone from the executive team to board members and investors, and don't take yourself too seriously even when the pace picks up. The CEO's office moves fast and deals with a lot of ambiguity, so we're looking for someone comfortable making calls with incomplete information, adapting as priorities shift, and pulling people together rather than working in isolation. We're also looking for genuine enthusiasm about where AI is headed and how it can reshape executive operations; someone excited to bring new AI tools into the day-to-day of the CEO's office, not just tolerate them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Leadership &amp; Executive Support</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner directly with the CEO to advance strategic initiatives, assess risks, and keep priorities aligned with Drata's mission and growth objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate leadership needs and proactively remove barriers to enable fast, informed decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prioritize and manage critical issues, surfacing the information that guides executive action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare data-backed briefings, presentations, and materials for executive, internal, and investor meetings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate clear communication between the CEO, executive team, and external stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Leadership &amp; Business Continuity</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage day-to-day operations of the CEO's office, keeping decision-making, prioritization, and problem-solving on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the CEO's trusted proxy during key periods or transitions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Finance and Legal on the CEO's office budget, approvals, and resource allocation, using automation where it helps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support planning and execution of leadership offsites, company all-hands, and other high-visibility moments.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Performance &amp; Strategic Execution</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement work plans that move the needle on company-wide goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the creation, tracking, and analysis of company OKRs and KPIs with the executive team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor milestones across departments and recommend course corrections to optimize outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead or support special projects, including M&amp;A, reorganizations, and cross-functional automation efforts, from discovery to execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support headcount planning, org design, and onboarding programs with the People team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the agenda for executive staff meetings and track completion of pre-work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Leadership &amp; Collaboration</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic connector across teams, translating executive priorities into coordinated action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structure leadership meetings, offsites, and planning sessions to build shared vision and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet regularly with cross-functional leaders to keep everyone aligned on the CEO's goals and OKRs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain an active pulse on the State of the State; bringing actionable information and insights to the CEO in a timely manner.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data, Reporting &amp; Continuous Improvement</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee performance reporting and data insights that support executive decision-making.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use tools like Slack Workflows, Zapier, and other automation platforms to streamline operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion continuous improvement and change management efforts across the organization.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication &amp; Stakeholder Management</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft and coordinate internal and external communications on behalf of the CEO, including company-wide updates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ghostwrite executive communications and craft strategic messaging in the CEO's voice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a liaison for investors, board members, customers, and press/analysts as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and escalate communication gaps quickly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Executive Office Management &amp; Travel</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the CEO's calendar with precision, balancing meeting priorities with travel and high-impact events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle timely submission of the CEO's expenses and track related spend.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some travel required for board meetings, investor events, and leadership offsites, including to Drata's San Francisco HQ.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High emotional intelligence, resilience, sound judgment, and a sense of humor.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A warm, energizing relationship-builder who earns trust quickly with the CEO, executive team, board members, and investors alike, and keeps teams aligned amid ambiguity or shifting priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of executive support experience in a SaaS or high-growth startup environment, including direct experience supporting a CEO or other C-level executive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of leadership experience managing business operations or executive support programs across multiple functions and time zones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting board and investor relations with a high degree of discretion and professionalism.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise building and scaling operational frameworks, including OKRs, org planning, and SOPs, for a high-growth organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record leading cross-functional initiatives, including M&amp;A, reorganizations, and automation implementations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to ghostwrite executive communications and craft strategic messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech-savvy, with hands-on experience using tools like Slack, Zapier, Claude, ChatGPT, or Glean to work faster and smarter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for GRC, cybersecurity, compliance, and Drata's mission to build trust across the internet.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $150,000 - $230,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team? \nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs Drata scales, we're looking for a strategic, operationally stellar Sr. Executive Business Partner to support our CEO & Co-Founder. This role sits at the heart of Drata's operational engine: translating vision into action, keeping the executive team and internal teams aligned, and giving our CEO the space to lead with clarity and momentum.\n\nYou'll thrive here if you lead with relationships, build trust quickly with everyone from the executive team to board members and investors, and don't take yourself too seriously even when the pace picks up. The CEO's office moves fast and deals with a lot of ambiguity, so we're looking for someone comfortable making calls with incomplete information, adapting as priorities shift, and pulling people together rather than working in isolation. We're also looking for genuine enthusiasm about where AI is headed and how it can reshape executive operations; someone excited to bring new AI tools into the day-to-day of the CEO's office, not just tolerate them.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\nStrategic Leadership & Executive Support\n\n - Partner directly with the CEO to advance strategic initiatives, assess risks, and keep priorities aligned with Drata's mission and growth objectives.\n\n - Anticipate leadership needs and proactively remove barriers to enable fast, informed decisions.\n\n - Prioritize and manage critical issues, surfacing the information that guides executive action.\n\n - Prepare data-backed briefings, presentations, and materials for executive, internal, and investor meetings.\n\n - Facilitate clear communication between the CEO, executive team, and external stakeholders.\n\nOperational Leadership & Business Continuity\n\n - Manage day-to-day operations of the CEO's office, keeping decision-making, prioritization, and problem-solving on track.\n\n - Act as the CEO's trusted proxy during key periods or transitions.\n\n - Partner with Finance and Legal on the CEO's office budget, approvals, and resource allocation, using automation where it helps.\n\n - Support planning and execution of leadership offsites, company all-hands, and other high-visibility moments.\n\nOrganizational Performance & Strategic Execution\n\n - Design and implement work plans that move the needle on company-wide goals.\n\n - Support the creation, tracking, and analysis of company OKRs and KPIs with the executive team.\n\n - Monitor milestones across departments and recommend course corrections to optimize outcomes.\n\n - Lead or support special projects, including M&A, reorganizations, and cross-functional automation efforts, from discovery to execution.\n\n - Support headcount planning, org design, and onboarding programs with the People team.\n\n - Own the agenda for executive staff meetings and track completion of pre-work.\n\nCross-Functional Leadership & Collaboration\n\n - Act as a strategic connector across teams, translating executive priorities into coordinated action.\n\n - Structure leadership meetings, offsites, and planning sessions to build shared vision and outcomes.\n\n - Meet regularly with cross-functional leaders to keep everyone aligned on the CEO's goals and OKRs.\n\n - Maintain an active pulse on the State of the State; bringing actionable information and insights to the CEO in a timely manner.\n\nData, Reporting & Continuous Improvement\n\n - Oversee performance reporting and data insights that support executive decision-making.\n\n - Use tools like Slack Workflows, Zapier, and other automation platforms to streamline operations.\n\n - Champion continuous improvement and change management efforts across the organization.\n\nCommunication & Stakeholder Management\n\n - Draft and coordinate internal and external communications on behalf of the CEO, including company-wide updates.\n\n - Ghostwrite executive communications and craft strategic messaging in the CEO's voice.\n\n - Serve as a liaison for investors, board members, customers, and press/analysts as needed.\n\n - Identify and escalate communication gaps quickly.\n\nExecutive Office Management & Travel\n\n - Manage the CEO's calendar with precision, balancing meeting priorities with travel and high-impact events.\n\n - Handle timely submission of the CEO's expenses and track related spend.\n\n - Some travel required for board meetings, investor events, and leadership offsites, including to Drata's San Francisco HQ.\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - High emotional intelligence, resilience, sound judgment, and a sense of humor.\n\n - A warm, energizing relationship-builder who earns trust quickly with the CEO, executive team, board members, and investors alike, and keeps teams aligned amid ambiguity or shifting priorities.\n\n - 8+ years of executive support experience in a SaaS or high-growth startup environment, including direct experience supporting a CEO or other C-level executive.\n\n - 4+ years of leadership experience managing business operations or executive support programs across multiple functions and time zones.\n\n - Experience supporting board and investor relations with a high degree of discretion and professionalism.\n\n - Expertise building and scaling operational frameworks, including OKRs, org planning, and SOPs, for a high-growth organization.\n\n - A track record leading cross-functional initiatives, including M&A, reorganizations, and automation implementations.\n\n - Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to ghostwrite executive communications and craft strategic messaging.\n\n - Tech-savvy, with hands-on experience using tools like Slack, Zapier, Claude, ChatGPT, or Glean to work faster and smarter.\n\n - Passion for GRC, cybersecurity, compliance, and Drata's mission to build trust across the internet.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $150,000 - $230,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6f8d57db-1008-4c54-90f5-64028ab767a3","title":"Senior Platform Operations Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid - San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T18:09:44.269+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/6f8d57db-1008-4c54-90f5-64028ab767a3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/6f8d57db-1008-4c54-90f5-64028ab767a3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team?</strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\"><u>what they say here</u></a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Senior Platform Operations Manager, you will lead the strategy, execution, and optimization of our marketing technology ecosystem. You will architect, implement, and manage the systems and integrations that power our go-to-market (GTM) engine, with a sharp focus on scalability, data integrity, automation, and lead orchestration.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is pivotal in ensuring that marketing, sales, customer success, business development and product teams are aligned and empowered to execute with speed and precision. You’re a Driver, you don’t just wait for projects and problems to come to you, but you identify them and execute without hesitation.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will report to the Director, Marketing Operations, a critical part of our connected GTM Operations team. You’ll bring a track record of proven success, preferably in a high-growth, fast-paced startup environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the marketing technology stack (e.g., HubSpot, Salesforce integration, LeanData, Qualified, 6sense, attribution tooling, etc) — driving roadmap, implementation, integration, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, recommend, and deploy new tools to enhance marketing execution and measurement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect a scalable infrastructure that supports pipeline acceleration, attribution, scoring, and personalized engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate lead management and routing requirements into system logic.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end implementation of lead assignment rules, SLAs, escalation flows, and scoring models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Sales Ops and Marketing Ops to continuously optimize routing for speed, accuracy, and fairness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure data quality, enrichment, normalization, and compliance across platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor data pipelines and troubleshoot discrepancies across systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish governance frameworks for platform changes, including documentation, QA, and release management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the technical lead for marketing in cross-functional projects, including GTM launches, sales handoff optimization, and analytics integration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify automation opportunities to increase operational efficiency and reduce manual effort.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI and machine learning capabilities in tools to enhance targeting, scoring, and predictive analytics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor and report on system health, performance metrics, and process efficiency.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience with HubSpot, SFDC, 6sense, LeanData and other prospecting tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise with marketing automation, CRM systems, and data integration tools (Marketo, Salesforce, LeanData, Segment, Workato, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of lead lifecycle, funnel stages, routing logic, and attribution models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with API integrations, custom workflows, and marketing data schemas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and project management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An unmatched attention to detail, taking pride in everything you do and understanding that the little things matter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage competing priorities in a results-driven environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $135,000 - $207,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team?\nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAs Senior Platform Operations Manager, you will lead the strategy, execution, and optimization of our marketing technology ecosystem. You will architect, implement, and manage the systems and integrations that power our go-to-market (GTM) engine, with a sharp focus on scalability, data integrity, automation, and lead orchestration.\n\n \n\nThis role is pivotal in ensuring that marketing, sales, customer success, business development and product teams are aligned and empowered to execute with speed and precision. You’re a Driver, you don’t just wait for projects and problems to come to you, but you identify them and execute without hesitation.\n\n \n\nThis role will report to the Director, Marketing Operations, a critical part of our connected GTM Operations team. You’ll bring a track record of proven success, preferably in a high-growth, fast-paced startup environment.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n - Own the marketing technology stack (e.g., HubSpot, Salesforce integration, LeanData, Qualified, 6sense, attribution tooling, etc) — driving roadmap, implementation, integration, and performance.\n\n - Evaluate, recommend, and deploy new tools to enhance marketing execution and measurement.\n\n - Architect a scalable infrastructure that supports pipeline acceleration, attribution, scoring, and personalized engagement.\n\n - Translate lead management and routing requirements into system logic.\n\n - Own end-to-end implementation of lead assignment rules, SLAs, escalation flows, and scoring models.\n\n - Partner with Sales Ops and Marketing Ops to continuously optimize routing for speed, accuracy, and fairness.\n\n - Ensure data quality, enrichment, normalization, and compliance across platforms.\n\n - Monitor data pipelines and troubleshoot discrepancies across systems.\n\n - Establish governance frameworks for platform changes, including documentation, QA, and release management.\n\n - Serve as the technical lead for marketing in cross-functional projects, including GTM launches, sales handoff optimization, and analytics integration.\n\n - Identify automation opportunities to increase operational efficiency and reduce manual effort.\n\n - Leverage AI and machine learning capabilities in tools to enhance targeting, scoring, and predictive analytics.\n\n - Monitor and report on system health, performance metrics, and process efficiency.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 7+ years of experience with HubSpot, SFDC, 6sense, LeanData and other prospecting tools\n\n - Deep expertise with marketing automation, CRM systems, and data integration tools (Marketo, Salesforce, LeanData, Segment, Workato, or similar).\n\n - Strong understanding of lead lifecycle, funnel stages, routing logic, and attribution models.\n\n - Experience with API integrations, custom workflows, and marketing data schemas.\n\n - Strong organizational and project management skills.\n\n - An unmatched attention to detail, taking pride in everything you do and understanding that the little things matter\n\n - Ability to manage competing priorities in a results-driven environment\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $135,000 - $207,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"402f313e-4ba9-4784-b784-f710e937d4c0","title":"Senior Manager, Commercial Account Management","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T22:19:12.171+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/402f313e-4ba9-4784-b784-f710e937d4c0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/402f313e-4ba9-4784-b784-f710e937d4c0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team?</strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\"><u>what they say here</u></a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is looking for a Senior Manager, Commercial Account Management to lead and develop a high-performing team serving primarily mid-market customers with moderate complexity, multiple stakeholders, and meaningful expansion potential. This people-leadership role is accountable for team performance across retention, renewals, expansion, adoption, value realization, customer health, and forecast accuracy, while setting clear standards for customer engagement, commercial execution, and operational discipline. The Senior Manager will coach and develop the team, hire and retain strong talent, provide leadership with forward-looking insight, and build the systems, playbooks, and cross-functional partnerships that make strong customer and recurring-revenue outcomes repeatable. This role does not carry an individual book of business and requires strong executive presence, analytical judgment, GRC or regulated-technology experience, and the ability to collaborate effectively across the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><h3>Lead and develop the team</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hire, coach, and develop Commercial Account Managers, setting clear expectations, performance standards, and career paths.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a high-performing, collaborative team culture through regular coaching, feedback, account reviews, and fair performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish consistent standards for account planning, customer engagement, CRM hygiene, forecasting, and execution.</p></li></ul><h3>Drive team outcomes</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own team performance across gross retention, on-time renewals, expansion / net revenue retention, adoption, customer health, and forecast accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate company goals into clear targets, operating rhythms, coverage expectations, and action plans; provide leadership with forward-looking visibility into risks and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coach renewal and expansion strategy, inspect complex or at-risk situations, and build repeatable plays that improve commercial performance.</p></li></ul><h3>Elevate customer value and manage risk</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the quality bar for success planning, value realization, product adoption, executive engagement, and customer health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the health of the team’s book of business, identify systemic risks, coordinate mitigation, and improve early-warning practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure the team can engage credibly on GRC topics and knows when and how to partner with Compliance Advisors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a reliable escalation leader for complex customer situations and bring the right level of Drata leadership into high-stakes moments.</p></li></ul><h3>Strengthen operations and cross-functional execution</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run the team’s operating rhythm, including account, renewal, expansion, forecast, risk, and performance reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use Salesforce, customer-success or revenue platforms, AI, and automation to improve prioritization, reporting, data discipline, and engagement quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with leadership across Solutions Architecture, Support, Sales Engineering, Compliance Advisory, Sales, Product, Marketing, Professional Services, RevOps, Finance, and other cross-functional teams to remove roadblocks and improve customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Surface patterns and voice-of-customer insights that inform product, onboarding, enablement, positioning, and post-sales improvements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in Account Management, Customer Success, Strategic Account Management, Consulting, or a related post-sales role within B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience managing quota-carrying Account Managers, Customer Success Managers, or comparable post-sales professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success leading teams responsible for renewals, retention, expansion, adoption, customer health, and recurring-revenue outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful experience in GRC, security, compliance, identity, or an adjacent regulated technology environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing and growing mid-market or Commercial customer relationships involving multiple stakeholders and meaningful business complexity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the combined commercial and customer-success motion, with the ability to coach teams across success planning, value realization, risk management, renewal execution, negotiation, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to hire, coach, develop, and retain high-performing teams through clear standards, feedback, accountability, and fair performance management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or improving a team-level operating model, including playbooks, coverage models, forecasting, reporting, and cross-functional processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to influence customers, direct reports, peers, and senior leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to navigate multi-threaded customer organizations and coach others to build relationships across business, operational, technical, and executive stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical, forecasting, prioritization, and organizational skills, with the ability to translate data into action and strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using Salesforce and customer-success or revenue platforms; adaptable to evolving systems and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, customer-centered leadership style and the ability to operate effectively in a high-growth, changing environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A modern, scalable mindset, including curiosity about AI and automation as tools to improve team effectiveness and customer engagement.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected OTE range for this role is between $212,500 - $325,833 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team?\nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is looking for a Senior Manager, Commercial Account Management to lead and develop a high-performing team serving primarily mid-market customers with moderate complexity, multiple stakeholders, and meaningful expansion potential. This people-leadership role is accountable for team performance across retention, renewals, expansion, adoption, value realization, customer health, and forecast accuracy, while setting clear standards for customer engagement, commercial execution, and operational discipline. The Senior Manager will coach and develop the team, hire and retain strong talent, provide leadership with forward-looking insight, and build the systems, playbooks, and cross-functional partnerships that make strong customer and recurring-revenue outcomes repeatable. This role does not carry an individual book of business and requires strong executive presence, analytical judgment, GRC or regulated-technology experience, and the ability to collaborate effectively across the organization.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n\nLEAD AND DEVELOP THE TEAM\n\n - Hire, coach, and develop Commercial Account Managers, setting clear expectations, performance standards, and career paths.\n\n - Build a high-performing, collaborative team culture through regular coaching, feedback, account reviews, and fair performance management.\n\n - Establish consistent standards for account planning, customer engagement, CRM hygiene, forecasting, and execution.\n\n\nDRIVE TEAM OUTCOMES\n\n - Own team performance across gross retention, on-time renewals, expansion / net revenue retention, adoption, customer health, and forecast accuracy.\n\n - Translate company goals into clear targets, operating rhythms, coverage expectations, and action plans; provide leadership with forward-looking visibility into risks and opportunities.\n\n - Coach renewal and expansion strategy, inspect complex or at-risk situations, and build repeatable plays that improve commercial performance.\n\n\nELEVATE CUSTOMER VALUE AND MANAGE RISK\n\n - Set the quality bar for success planning, value realization, product adoption, executive engagement, and customer health.\n\n - Own the health of the team’s book of business, identify systemic risks, coordinate mitigation, and improve early-warning practices.\n\n - Ensure the team can engage credibly on GRC topics and knows when and how to partner with Compliance Advisors.\n\n - Serve as a reliable escalation leader for complex customer situations and bring the right level of Drata leadership into high-stakes moments.\n\n\nSTRENGTHEN OPERATIONS AND CROSS-FUNCTIONAL EXECUTION\n\n - Run the team’s operating rhythm, including account, renewal, expansion, forecast, risk, and performance reviews.\n\n - Use Salesforce, customer-success or revenue platforms, AI, and automation to improve prioritization, reporting, data discipline, and engagement quality.\n\n - Collaborate closely with leadership across Solutions Architecture, Support, Sales Engineering, Compliance Advisory, Sales, Product, Marketing, Professional Services, RevOps, Finance, and other cross-functional teams to remove roadblocks and improve customer outcomes.\n\n - Surface patterns and voice-of-customer insights that inform product, onboarding, enablement, positioning, and post-sales improvements.\n\nWhat you’ll bring:\n\n - 8+ years of experience in Account Management, Customer Success, Strategic Account Management, Consulting, or a related post-sales role within B2B SaaS.\n\n - 3+ years of experience managing quota-carrying Account Managers, Customer Success Managers, or comparable post-sales professionals.\n\n - Demonstrated success leading teams responsible for renewals, retention, expansion, adoption, customer health, and recurring-revenue outcomes.\n\n - Meaningful experience in GRC, security, compliance, identity, or an adjacent regulated technology environment.\n\n - Experience managing and growing mid-market or Commercial customer relationships involving multiple stakeholders and meaningful business complexity.\n\n - Strong understanding of the combined commercial and customer-success motion, with the ability to coach teams across success planning, value realization, risk management, renewal execution, negotiation, and expansion.\n\n - Proven ability to hire, coach, develop, and retain high-performing teams through clear standards, feedback, accountability, and fair performance management.\n\n - Experience building or improving a team-level operating model, including playbooks, coverage models, forecasting, reporting, and cross-functional processes.\n\n - Strong executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to influence customers, direct reports, peers, and senior leaders.\n\n - Ability to navigate multi-threaded customer organizations and coach others to build relationships across business, operational, technical, and executive stakeholders.\n\n - Strong analytical, forecasting, prioritization, and organizational skills, with the ability to translate data into action and strategy.\n\n - Experience using Salesforce and customer-success or revenue platforms; adaptable to evolving systems and processes.\n\n - A collaborative, customer-centered leadership style and the ability to operate effectively in a high-growth, changing environment.\n\n - A modern, scalable mindset, including curiosity about AI and automation as tools to improve team effectiveness and customer engagement.\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected OTE range for this role is between $212,500 - $325,833 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b7216aa8-5f0a-4c44-bf3d-e68c59467bdb","title":"Customer Education Manager","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T02:19:15.901+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/b7216aa8-5f0a-4c44-bf3d-e68c59467bdb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/drata/b7216aa8-5f0a-4c44-bf3d-e68c59467bdb/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.<br /><br /><strong>Why Join the Drata Team?</strong><br />At Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problems without a playbook:</strong> You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real ownership, not just process:</strong> Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A seat at the table:</strong> Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth at rocketship speed:</strong> Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A crew, not just coworkers:</strong> Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/careers/life\"><u>what they say here</u></a> and follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all\"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> for company news, employee stories, and career updates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drata is building a world-class customer education function — and we're looking for the person who will own it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Learning &amp; Development Specialist, you'll be the architect of how Drata customers learn: designing the programs, building the certifications, and creating the infrastructure that helps thousands of security and compliance practitioners get value from Drata faster and more independently. A critical part of this role is understanding that Enterprise and SMB customers don't learn the same way — you'll design programs that meet each segment where they are, with the right depth, format, and pacing for their needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll sit within the Digital CS team — alongside Community, in-app guidance, automated playbooks, and 1:M events — and you'll be the expert who defines what great customer education looks like at Drata across every customer segment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a senior IC role. You won't manage people on day one, but you'll lead the discipline. You'll set the strategy, own the roadmap, and be the voice of customer education across the company. As the function matures, there's a clear path to building a team under you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report directly to the Sr. Director of Digital CS, who leads all of Drata's Digital CS programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and mature the Drata Academy program</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the Drata Academy roadmap — course library strategy, learning path design, and the overall curriculum architecture across Drata's product suite (GRC, Trust Center, AIQA, TPRM)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design distinct learning experiences for Enterprise and SMB customers — Enterprise teams need depth, role-based paths, and content that scales across large orgs; SMB customers need fast time-to-value, opinionated guidance, and lean formats that fit a lean team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take Academy from a newly launched platform to a mature, comprehensive education program with measurable customer outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define what 'good' looks like for customer education at Drata — frameworks, standards, and content quality bar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a scalable content production process using AI-assisted authoring tools (Claude Design, Arcade, and similar) to create high-quality courses without engineering dependency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product to stay ahead of feature releases and ensure education content ships in sync with the product</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Launch and own the Drata Admin Certification program</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build Drata's first customer certification program — the Drata Admin Certification — from curriculum design through to assessment, badging, and renewal</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the certification framework: competency model, exam structure, passing criteria, and credential lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Customer Success, Sales, and Marketing teams to position the Drata Admin Certification as a meaningful credential in the GRC and security compliance market</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the ecosystem around certification: study guides, prep courses, practice assessments, and community-based peer learning</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive education impact with AI and data</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI tools meaningfully throughout the content lifecycle — not just for drafting, but for personalization, adaptive learning paths, and content gap identification at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and own education KPIs: course completion rates, certification pass rates, time-to-proficiency, and correlation between education engagement and GRR/NRR</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Digital CS team's data infrastructure (Snowflake, Hook.co) to connect Academy engagement to customer health scores and retention outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Report education program performance in the quarterly Digital CS QBR and continuously improve based on what the data shows</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Integrate education across the Digital CS ecosystem</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Connect Academy to the broader Digital CS motion — surface course recommendations in automated playbooks, in-app tooltips, and community content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Community Manager to make community a learning accelerator: expert-led sessions, peer knowledge sharing, and certification prep cohorts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the 1:M events program to create learning continuity between live sessions and self-paced Academy content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure education content reinforces the in-app guidance experience — tooltips, Arcade videos, and Academy courses telling a consistent story</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll bring:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–8 years of experience in customer education, learning &amp; development, or instructional design at a B2B SaaS company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record building or maturing a customer education program — ideally across companies at different stages (early-stage build to scaled program)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing L&amp;D programs for both Enterprise and SMB customers — you understand that a Fortune 500 security team and a 20-person startup have fundamentally different learning needs, timelines, and success metrics, and you've built programs that reflect that</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Certification program experience — you've designed, launched, or owned a professional certification or credentialing program end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on LMS expertise — deep experience with Skilljar, Gainsight Academy, Docebo, Thought Industries, or similar platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI fluency with real business impact — you've used AI tools to meaningfully accelerate content creation, improve learning outcomes, or scale a program; you can speak to the results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong instructional design instincts — you understand adult learning principles, can design for different modalities (video, interactive, assessment), and know what makes content actually stick</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-driven — you track completion rates, certification outcomes, and business impact, and you use that data to make decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-functional collaborator — comfortable working with Product, CS, Marketing, and Support to align education to the customer journey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: experience in the GRC, security compliance, or trust space; familiarity with Drata, SOC 2, ISO 27001, or similar frameworks</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why this role?</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own a discipline, not just a program — this is the person who defines what customer education means at Drata, with full strategic ownership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Academy just launched — you're coming in at the moment of maximum leverage, when the platform exists but the real program-building work is just beginning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The certification you build will matter in the market — Drata has thousands of customers in the GRC space; a Drata Admin Certification has real credentialing potential</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be embedded in one of the most forward-thinking Digital CS functions in B2B SaaS — with Community, AI-driven playbooks, in-app guidance, and 1:M events all working together</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear growth path — as the education function matures, this role grows with it</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we support you:<br /></strong>At Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore how we invest in your <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Life at Drata</u></a><u>.</u></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shared Success</strong>: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> Up to <strong>100% employer-paid premiums</strong> for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees <em>and their dependents</em>, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Financial Well-being:</strong> A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a <strong>401(k) plan</strong>, company-paid <strong>life and disability insurance</strong>, <strong>tax-advantaged spending accounts</strong>, and a range of <strong>discounted voluntary offerings</strong> to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family Support:</strong> We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to <strong>Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits</strong> and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth &amp; Development:</strong> Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off &amp; Flexibility:</strong> We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The expected base salary range for this role is between $125,000 - $161,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Candidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Drata is building the trust layer between great companies - automating compliance, managing risk, and helping organizations prove trust continuously as they scale. We're Dratanauts: a global crew of 600+ professionals united by a culture that rewards integrity, ownership, and raising the bar, no matter where in the world we're working from.\n\nWhy Join the Drata Team?\nAt Drata, you're not maintaining legacy compliance software - you're building the agentic AI platform defining what trust looks like for the next generation of companies. Here's what makes the work itself worth showing up for:\n\n - Problems without a playbook: You'll work at the edge of AI and security, building agentic governance, continuous compliance, and real-time trust verification to solve problems that don't have an established answer yet. You're writing it as you go.\n\n - Real ownership, not just process: Our values center on owning outcomes and raising the bar, not checking boxes. You're expected to have opinions and back them.\n\n - A seat at the table: Your perspective is unique and valued. Open debate and diverse viewpoints are built into how decisions actually get made here, at every level.\n\n - Growth at rocketship speed: Drata is scaling fast, which means scope grows fast too. High performers get more ownership, visibility, and experience.\n\n - A crew, not just coworkers: Dratanauts consistently describe a \"come as you are\" culture with sharp, curious people—the kind of team that makes hard problems genuinely fun to solve. See what they say here https://drata.com/about/careers/life and follow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/drata/posts/?feedView=all for company news, employee stories, and career updates.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nDrata is building a world-class customer education function — and we're looking for the person who will own it.\n\nAs Learning & Development Specialist, you'll be the architect of how Drata customers learn: designing the programs, building the certifications, and creating the infrastructure that helps thousands of security and compliance practitioners get value from Drata faster and more independently. A critical part of this role is understanding that Enterprise and SMB customers don't learn the same way — you'll design programs that meet each segment where they are, with the right depth, format, and pacing for their needs.\n\nYou'll sit within the Digital CS team — alongside Community, in-app guidance, automated playbooks, and 1:M events — and you'll be the expert who defines what great customer education looks like at Drata across every customer segment.\n\nThis is a senior IC role. You won't manage people on day one, but you'll lead the discipline. You'll set the strategy, own the roadmap, and be the voice of customer education across the company. As the function matures, there's a clear path to building a team under you.\n\nYou'll report directly to the Sr. Director of Digital CS, who leads all of Drata's Digital CS programs.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n\nBuild and mature the Drata Academy program\n\n - Own the Drata Academy roadmap — course library strategy, learning path design, and the overall curriculum architecture across Drata's product suite (GRC, Trust Center, AIQA, TPRM)\n\n - Design distinct learning experiences for Enterprise and SMB customers — Enterprise teams need depth, role-based paths, and content that scales across large orgs; SMB customers need fast time-to-value, opinionated guidance, and lean formats that fit a lean team\n\n - Take Academy from a newly launched platform to a mature, comprehensive education program with measurable customer outcomes\n\n - Define what 'good' looks like for customer education at Drata — frameworks, standards, and content quality bar\n\n - Build a scalable content production process using AI-assisted authoring tools (Claude Design, Arcade, and similar) to create high-quality courses without engineering dependency\n\n - Partner with Product to stay ahead of feature releases and ensure education content ships in sync with the product\n\nLaunch and own the Drata Admin Certification program\n\n - Design and build Drata's first customer certification program — the Drata Admin Certification — from curriculum design through to assessment, badging, and renewal\n\n - Define the certification framework: competency model, exam structure, passing criteria, and credential lifecycle\n\n - Partner with the Customer Success, Sales, and Marketing teams to position the Drata Admin Certification as a meaningful credential in the GRC and security compliance market\n\n - Build the ecosystem around certification: study guides, prep courses, practice assessments, and community-based peer learning\n\nDrive education impact with AI and data\n\n - Use AI tools meaningfully throughout the content lifecycle — not just for drafting, but for personalization, adaptive learning paths, and content gap identification at scale\n\n - Define and own education KPIs: course completion rates, certification pass rates, time-to-proficiency, and correlation between education engagement and GRR/NRR\n\n - Partner with the Digital CS team's data infrastructure (Snowflake, Hook.co) to connect Academy engagement to customer health scores and retention outcomes\n\n - Report education program performance in the quarterly Digital CS QBR and continuously improve based on what the data shows\n\nIntegrate education across the Digital CS ecosystem\n\n - Connect Academy to the broader Digital CS motion — surface course recommendations in automated playbooks, in-app tooltips, and community content\n\n - Partner with the Community Manager to make community a learning accelerator: expert-led sessions, peer knowledge sharing, and certification prep cohorts\n\n - Collaborate with the 1:M events program to create learning continuity between live sessions and self-paced Academy content\n\n - Ensure education content reinforces the in-app guidance experience — tooltips, Arcade videos, and Academy courses telling a consistent story\n\nWhat you'll bring:\n\n - 5–8 years of experience in customer education, learning & development, or instructional design at a B2B SaaS company\n\n - Proven track record building or maturing a customer education program — ideally across companies at different stages (early-stage build to scaled program)\n\n - Experience designing L&D programs for both Enterprise and SMB customers — you understand that a Fortune 500 security team and a 20-person startup have fundamentally different learning needs, timelines, and success metrics, and you've built programs that reflect that\n\n - Certification program experience — you've designed, launched, or owned a professional certification or credentialing program end-to-end\n\n - Hands-on LMS expertise — deep experience with Skilljar, Gainsight Academy, Docebo, Thought Industries, or similar platforms\n\n - AI fluency with real business impact — you've used AI tools to meaningfully accelerate content creation, improve learning outcomes, or scale a program; you can speak to the results\n\n - Strong instructional design instincts — you understand adult learning principles, can design for different modalities (video, interactive, assessment), and know what makes content actually stick\n\n - Data-driven — you track completion rates, certification outcomes, and business impact, and you use that data to make decisions\n\n - Cross-functional collaborator — comfortable working with Product, CS, Marketing, and Support to align education to the customer journey\n\n - Bonus: experience in the GRC, security compliance, or trust space; familiarity with Drata, SOC 2, ISO 27001, or similar frameworks\n\nWhy this role?\n\n - You'll own a discipline, not just a program — this is the person who defines what customer education means at Drata, with full strategic ownership\n\n - Academy just launched — you're coming in at the moment of maximum leverage, when the platform exists but the real program-building work is just beginning\n\n - The certification you build will matter in the market — Drata has thousands of customers in the GRC space; a Drata Admin Certification has real credentialing potential\n\n - You'll be embedded in one of the most forward-thinking Digital CS functions in B2B SaaS — with Community, AI-driven playbooks, in-app guidance, and 1:M events all working together\n\n - Clear growth path — as the education function matures, this role grows with it\n\nHow we support you:\nAt Drata, our people are our strongest advantage—and we prove it with support that exceeds industry standards. Our total rewards package is designed to power your well-being, accelerate your growth, and keep your work-life balance thriving.\n\nExplore how we invest in your Life at Drata https://drata.com/about/life-at-drata?utm_source=chatgpt.com.\n\n - Shared Success: We provide stock equity to ensure that as the company grows, you share directly in that success. Equity gives every employee a sense of ownership and the opportunity to celebrate our wins together—because your contributions don’t just support our progress; they help drive our collective success.\n\n - Health & Wellness: Up to 100% employer-paid premiums for medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents, along with comprehensive wellness benefits and healthcare concierge services designed to support your needs beyond traditional insurance.\n\n - Financial Well-being: A comprehensive suite of financial benefits, including a 401(k) plan, company-paid life and disability insurance, tax-advantaged spending accounts, and a range of discounted voluntary offerings to help you customize and strengthen your overall financial position.\n\n - Family Support: We want to support you in life's most important moments, so we offer a paid Parental Leave policy, after six months of employment. Employees also receive access to Kindbody fertility and family-building benefits and dedicated leave specialists who help guide you through the entire process.\n\n - Growth & Development: Generous annual stipends for both professional and personal development, empowering you to invest in your continued growth. You’ll also have access to a wide range of internal learning opportunities, ensuring you can build new skills, deepen your expertise, and advance your career with confidence.\n\n - Time Off & Flexibility: We believe that to do your best work, you should get the time you need for rest, rejuvenation and recovery. Drata offers a flexible vacation policy, paid holidays, and other perks to recharge.\n\nThe expected base salary range for this role is between $125,000 - $161,000 and is listed to provide transparency. Actual base pay will vary based on multiple factors — market location, job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and overall alignment to the role. \n\nCandidates shouldn't expect automatic placement at any particular point within the range. Offer amounts are determined by the qualifications each candidate brings to the position. Total compensation may also include equity designed to provide meaningful ownership in the company, as well as health and wellbeing benefits.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}